// RULING-B ROSTER IMPORT SWEEP (#14003 / #14017), computed from the PARSED program, not from text.
//
// A bare free call to a collection kernel head binds natively only when its shape is import-visible
// from std.algebra. This module reads each file the way the compiler does (tokenize, parse, normalize),
// takes the file's own reference sites with their lexical head classification, and computes the
// std.algebra import as a VALUE: the names its existing import declaration binds, plus the shape each
// lexically-unbound roster head needs, deduplicated by Symbol identity. The import declaration is then
// rendered from that value and addressed by its parsed source extent, so a malformed block has no
// construction (the c.dag:866 defect was a spliced block, #14017). Output is rows, never writes:
//   EDIT <path> <start> <end> <replacement>     replacement has backslashes escaped as \\ and newlines as \n (one line per row)
//   REFUSE <path> <cause>
// roster_import_sweep_apply_exit is the committed apply step (stale-read check under an apply lock, then Filesystem.Write).
// This module IS the row-driven wave generator of the NAMESPACE-XL sweeps: roster_head_rows is its row table, the
// HOME TABLE rows are added there as data, and no control flow changes when a row is added. Its controls are the
// gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:roster-import-sweep-controls instrument. Driven as
//   gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry src/v2/workflow/roster_import_sweep.dag
//     --function roster_import_sweep_for_paths --arg paths_csv=<comma-separated paths>
// and applied with roster_import_sweep_apply_exit --arg root_dir=<absolute worktree root> --arg paths_csv=<paths relative to the root>
//
// Pending rows leave the process through roster_import_sweep_exit's reason channel.
// SCOPE: the ruling-B shapes (concat/count/map/join), chars, and map_get -> map_lookup (tidy-ant-251's ruling A: a
// RenameHead row; std.algebra map_lookup already declares the operation). The earlier hold on map_get -- dag/std/graph.dag
// stopping resolving after the rename -- did not reproduce at main 5cadf42 on resolve, typecheck or the emitted self-host
// build. Further homes wait for the operator's home table; the table below is the single place a row would be added.

// ONE ROW PER AMBIENT NAME: the bare call spelling, the name the import binds, and the name's ONE declared home module.
// The generator is home-agnostic; a wave is a row here (NAMESPACE-XL), never a branch.
// `key` IS THE ROW'S IDENTITY: (home, call) is not unique (std.algebra sort_by has a Symbol-order row and a String-order row,
// both the same free head), and the appended text is a spelling, not an identity. A per-site selection (OnlyOccurrences)
// names a row by its key; the key of a row with no sibling is its call.
type RosterHeadRow {
  call: String
  key: String
  import_name: String
  home: QualifiedName
  labels: List<RosterLabelRename>
  head: RosterHeadRewrite
}

// A ROW WHOSE HOME DECLARES THE OPERATION UNDER ANOTHER NAME (tidy-ant-251's map_get ruling A: the ambient spelling's
// operation is already declared, so the call moves to the declaration rather than minting a second name for it).
// KeepHead is every row whose call spelling IS the home's name, so the rows that predate this field are unchanged by
// construction. RenameHead rewrites each selected call head to `to`; its `positional` is the other half of the same
// fact, so it lives in the arm and a KeepHead row cannot carry one: the home declaration's parameter labels, in order, given to a call's positional arguments, because the home's
// callable is called by label where the ambient spelling was called by position. EXACT ARITY IS REQUIRED: a call that does
// not have exactly that many positional arguments refuses. An argument already named with the label this row declares AT
// ITS POSITION is retained as authored; a mismatched or reordered label refuses, because the rewrite never reorders
// arguments -- reordering an argument list reorders its evaluation.
type RosterHeadRewrite
  = KeepHead
  | RenameHead { to: String, positional: List<String> }

// THE ARGUMENT LABELS A ROW'S HOME RENAMES at its call sites: a field of the row, so the call and the home a rename belongs
// to are the row's own facts, stated once (review 82024).
type RosterLabelRename {
  from: String
  to: String
}

// WHICH ROWS ONE RUN MAY TOUCH. A wave moves one NAME, and one home can hold several rows (std.algebra holds four), so a
// one-home run selects its rows too: EveryRowOfHome is the whole home, OnlyCall the wave's own row. Selecting by home
// alone made a one-name wave write, and refuse for, every other row of that home
// (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode a_one_home_sweep_moves_every_row_of_that_home). The selection lives INSIDE OneHome, so a
// mutating run still names exactly one home by construction, which the cycle verdict relies on. A closed sum, so "every
// home" is not an in-band spelling a typo could collide with (review 82002).
type RosterHomeScope
  = AllHomes
  | OneHome { home: QualifiedName, rows: RosterRowSelection }

// OnlyOccurrences is the PER-SITE grain a wave takes when ONE SPELLING splits by ARGUMENT IDENTITY and no row field can
// tell the halves apart: `to_string` over a kernel Int and over a kernel Nat are the same free head, and the row cannot
// read an argument's type (the sweep matches no type), so the two halves are two rows of the same call, each carrying the
// census occurrence keys of ITS sites. The keys are the census location column `file:line:byte column` (1-based, byte
// column; the same rendering the admission join uses at dag/gunbc/instruments/namespace_wave_occurrence_join.dag locus_at);
// they arrive as ONE-SHOT generator INPUT at a run, never as a landed artifact, and every key must meet exactly one FREE
// value-position site of the row's spelling in the file -- a key that matches nothing, matches a site the row would not
// touch (a bound name), or names a file outside the run's paths, REFUSES the run (RefusalOccurrenceKeyUnmatched). There is NO FALLBACK TO SPELLING: a selection carrying keys is
// an exact claim about sites, and a partial match is a stale census, not a hint.
type RosterRowSelection
  = EveryRowOfHome
  | OnlyCall { call: String }
  | OnlyOccurrences { row: String, call: String, occurrences: List<String> }

fn roster_scope_admits(scope: RosterHomeScope, row: RosterHeadRow) -> Bool {
  match scope {
    AllHomes => true
    OneHome { home: h, rows: sel } =>
      roster_qn_text(qn: h) == roster_qn_text(qn: row.home) && roster_selection_admits(selection: sel, row: row)
  }
}

fn roster_selection_admits(selection: RosterRowSelection, row: RosterHeadRow) -> Bool {
  match selection {
    EveryRowOfHome => true
    OnlyCall { call: c } => c == row.call
    OnlyOccurrences { row: k, call: c, occurrences: _ } => k == row.key && c == row.call
  }
}

fn roster_qn_text(qn: QualifiedName) -> String {
  roster_join(xs: list_map(xs: qn, f: fn(s) { symbol_lexeme(sym: s) }), sep: ".")
}

// THE CLOSED SET OF REFUSAL REASONS of this module; every REFUSE row is rendered from one by roster_refusal_text,
// the sole place a reason becomes protocol text. Admission is Optional (Absent = admitted), never a member of this set.
type RosterRefusalReason
  = RefusalTokenizeRefused
  | RefusalParseRefused
  | RefusalNormalizeRefused
  | RefusalShapeNameBoundElsewhere
  | RefusalNoImportAnchor
  | RefusalExtentNotOnCharBoundary
  | RefusalExtentMismatch
  | RefusalExtentHasAnnotation
  | RefusalRootNotAbsoluteCanonical
  | RefusalRootNotGitToplevel
  | RefusalApplyLockUnavailable
  | RefusalApplyLockNotReleased
  | RefusalLockWriteFailed
  | RefusalGenerationHistoryUnestablished
  | RefusalPathOutsideRoot
  | RefusalLockNotHeld
  | RefusalTargetNotTrackedRegular
  | RefusalTargetIndexFlagged
  | RefusalTargetModified
  | RefusalTargetAncestorChanged
  | RefusalGitUnobservable
  | RefusalStaleRead
  | RefusalWriteFailed
  | RefusalUnreadable
  | RefusalGrammarUnprepared
  | RefusalLabelSitesAmbiguous
  // THE CENSUS CANNOT CLASSIFY A HOME THE RULE MUST DECIDE ABOUT (review 83187, DESIGN 5): an unbound head sits at a
  // value or type position and the home's keyed census rows classify NONE of its declarations -- zero rows, or only
  // OtherItem (the census's own cannot-classify answer, which a declaration the host cannot kind reads as).
  // Neither importing nor silently planning no import is honest, so the module refuses, located by home and name.
  | RefusalHomeKindUnclassified { home: String, name: String }
  | RefusalImportClosesCycle { home: String, module: String }
  | RefusalHomeClosureUnread { home: String }
  | RefusalModuleNameUnread
  | RefusalApplyNeedsOneHome
  // A ONE-HOME SCOPE THAT SELECTS NO ROW, OR AN OnlyCall SELECTING MORE THAN ONE (side chat on #14883, DESIGN 5): a
  // misspelled call or a wrong home would otherwise sweep nothing and report converged. Located by home and selection.
  | RefusalScopeSelectsNoRow { home: String, selection: String }
  | RefusalScopeSelectsSeveralRows { home: String, call: String, count: Int }
  // A RenameHead row's call whose arguments the row's positional labels cannot place: EXACT ARITY is required (a different
  // number of positional arguments than the row declares refuses); an argument already named with the label the row declares
  // AT ITS POSITION is retained as authored, while a mismatched or reordered label refuses (the rewrite never reorders
  // arguments); or a bare reference with no call. The file is left untouched and the cause names the call spelling.
  | RefusalRenameCallArity { call: String }
  | RefusalRenameCallNamedArgument { call: String }
  // A `|>` whose right operand starts at the renamed call but extends past it: the call is not the pipe's target, so its
  // operand cannot be taken cleanly as slot 0.
  | RefusalRenamePipeOperandUnclean { call: String }
  // A RenameHead row whose companion import cannot be derived (the home, the callee, its declared return type, the
  // module that declares that type, or the type's variants did not read): a file whose renamed call it would govern
  // refuses rather than leaving the result matched by ambient tags that bind it untyped.
  | RefusalCompanionUnderivable { call: String, detail: String }
  // AN OCCURRENCE KEY THAT DOES NOT MEET A SITE (the per-site selection grain): a key of an OnlyOccurrences selection
  // matched NO free value-position site of the row's spelling in the file, or the selection is empty. A stale census
  // (the file moved since the census was taken) and a typo are both refusals, never a silent narrowing -- the keys are
  // an exact claim about which sites become edits, and there is no fallback to sweeping the spelling (manager ruling,
  // NAMESPACE-XL to_string wave: "if a row does not match, refuse it and list it, never fall back to spelling").
  | RefusalOccurrenceKeyUnmatched { path: String, call: String, key: String }
  // A RenameHead row whose companion would import a tag the module spells at a pattern-tag position whose binding the
  // reference walk could not decide (an enclosing arm's pattern atom of that spelling that may bind it, not an import):
  // whether the import is needed is unknown, so the file refuses rather than leaving the tag possibly ambient.
  | RefusalCompanionTagUndecided { call: String, tag: String }
  // TWO PLANNED EDITS OF ONE FILE THAT ARE NOT DISJOINT: a replacement whose extent covers another edit's start, or two
  // zero-width insertions at one offset. Applied last-first, either would be last-writer-wins on the same bytes, so the
  // plan refuses before any splice and names the extents.
  | RefusalEditsOverlap { start: Int, end: Int, reach: Int }
  | RefusalEditsCoincide { at: Int }

fn roster_refusal_text(reason: RosterRefusalReason) -> String {
  match reason {
    RefusalTokenizeRefused => "tokenize-refused"
    RefusalParseRefused => "parse-refused"
    RefusalNormalizeRefused => "normalize-refused"
    RefusalShapeNameBoundElsewhere => "shape-name-bound-elsewhere"
    RefusalNoImportAnchor => "no-import-anchor"
    RefusalExtentNotOnCharBoundary => "extent-not-on-char-boundary"
    RefusalExtentMismatch => "extent-mismatch"
    RefusalExtentHasAnnotation => "extent-has-annotation"
    RefusalRootNotAbsoluteCanonical => "root-not-absolute-canonical"
    RefusalRootNotGitToplevel => "root-not-git-toplevel"
    RefusalApplyLockUnavailable => "apply-lock-unavailable"
    RefusalApplyLockNotReleased => "apply-lock-not-released"
    RefusalLockWriteFailed => "lock-write-failed"
    RefusalGenerationHistoryUnestablished => "generation-history-unestablished"
    RefusalPathOutsideRoot => "path-outside-root"
    RefusalLockNotHeld => "lock-not-held"
    RefusalTargetNotTrackedRegular => "target-not-tracked-regular"
    RefusalTargetIndexFlagged => "target-index-flagged"
    RefusalTargetModified => "target-modified"
    RefusalTargetAncestorChanged => "target-ancestor-changed"
    RefusalGitUnobservable => "git-unobservable"
    RefusalStaleRead => "stale-read"
    RefusalWriteFailed => "write-failed"
    RefusalUnreadable => "unreadable"
    RefusalGrammarUnprepared => "grammar-unprepared"
    RefusalLabelSitesAmbiguous => "label-sites-ambiguous"
    RefusalHomeKindUnclassified { home: h, name: n } => "home-kind-unclassified home=" + h + " name=" + n
    RefusalImportClosesCycle { home: h, module: m } => "import-closes-cycle home=" + h + " module=" + m
    RefusalHomeClosureUnread { home: h } => "home-closure-unread home=" + h
    RefusalModuleNameUnread => "module-name-unread"
    RefusalApplyNeedsOneHome => "apply-needs-one-home"
    RefusalScopeSelectsNoRow { home: h, selection: sel } => "scope-selects-no-row home=" + h + " " + sel
    RefusalScopeSelectsSeveralRows { home: h, call: c, count: n } => "scope-selects-several-rows home=" + h + " call=" + c + " rows=" + int_to_decimal_string(value: n)
    RefusalRenameCallArity { call: c } => "rename-call-arity call=" + c
    RefusalEditsOverlap { start: st, end: en, reach: re } => "edits-overlap start=" + int_to_decimal_string(value: st) + " end=" + int_to_decimal_string(value: en) + " covered-to=" + int_to_decimal_string(value: re)
    RefusalCompanionTagUndecided { call: c, tag: t } => "companion-tag-undecided call=" + c + " tag=" + t
    RefusalEditsCoincide { at: a } => "edits-coincide at=" + int_to_decimal_string(value: a)
    RefusalRenameCallNamedArgument { call: c } => "rename-call-named-argument call=" + c
    RefusalRenamePipeOperandUnclean { call: c } => "rename-pipe-operand-unclean call=" + c
    RefusalCompanionUnderivable { call: c, detail: d } => "companion-underivable call=" + c + " " + d
    RefusalOccurrenceKeyUnmatched { path: p, call: c, key: k } => "occurrence-key-unmatched path=" + p + " call=" + c + " key=" + k
  }
}

// THE HOME'S IMPORT CLOSURE, read once per run through the compiler's own door (v2.compiler.module_acquisition
// acquire_verified over v2.cli.repository_layout repository_storage_layout). Importing a home into a module that home already
// reaches closes a cycle, and acyclicity is the import graph's only structural law (DESIGN section 3). A closure the door
// cannot verify is carried as unread, and every file needing that home refuses rather than guessing it acyclic.
type RosterHomeClosure
  = RosterClosureRead { home: String, modules: List<String> }
  | RosterClosureUnread { home: String }

fn roster_home_closures(root: String, scope: RosterHomeScope) -> List<RosterHomeClosure> {
  let homes = fold_list(xs: roster_rows_for_scope(scope: scope), empty: [], cons: fn(acc, row) {
    if roster_contains(xs: acc, name: roster_qn_text(qn: row.home)) { acc } else { list_snoc_item(xs: acc, item: roster_qn_text(qn: row.home)) }
  })
  roster_homes_closures_read(homes: homes, bindings: roster_repository_bindings(root: root))
}

fn roster_repository_bindings(root: String) -> List<SourceRootBinding> {
  [
    SourceRootBinding { tree: V2Tree, host_directory: roster_rooted(root: root, dir: repository_tree_directory(tree: V2Tree)) },
    SourceRootBinding { tree: DagTree, host_directory: roster_rooted(root: root, dir: repository_tree_directory(tree: DagTree)) }
  ]
}

fn roster_rooted(root: String, dir: String) -> String {
  if root == "" { dir } else { root + "/" + dir }
}

fn roster_home_closure_read(home: String, bindings: List<SourceRootBinding>) -> RosterHomeClosure {
  match acquire_verified(layout: repository_storage_layout(), bindings: bindings, entries: [home]) {
    AcquisitionVerified { modules: modules, reads: _, absent_probes: _ } => RosterClosureRead { home: home, modules: list_map(xs: modules, f: fn(m) { roster_acquired_name(m: m) }) }
    AcquisitionNotVerified { reason: _, cause: _ } => RosterClosureUnread { home: home }
  }
}

fn roster_acquired_name(m: AcquiredModule) -> String {
  m.name
}

// ONE walk for every home of a run: the union of the homes' closures is acquired and verified once (each file read once),
// and each home's own closure is the acquirer's own traversal (acquisition_reached) from that home over that one member table
// -- the same reach acquisition_exactness certifies, so no second derivation of what a home reaches. A union the door
// cannot verify leaves EVERY home unread (a refusal, never a guess).
fn roster_homes_closures_read(homes: List<String>, bindings: List<SourceRootBinding>) -> List<RosterHomeClosure> {
  match acquire_verified(layout: repository_storage_layout(), bindings: bindings, entries: homes) {
    AcquisitionVerified { modules: modules, reads: _, absent_probes: _ } =>
      list_map(xs: homes, f: fn(home) {
        let reached = acquisition_reached(entries: [home], modules: modules)
        RosterClosureRead { home: home, modules: list_map(xs: fold_list(xs: modules, empty: [], cons: fn(acc, m) { if map_contains_key(m: reached, key: m.name) { list_snoc_item(xs: acc, item: m) } else { acc } }), f: fn(m) { roster_acquired_name(m: m) }) }
      })
    AcquisitionNotVerified { reason: _, cause: _ } => list_map(xs: homes, f: fn(home) { RosterClosureUnread { home: home } })
  }
}

// The cycle verdict for importing `home` into `module`: Absent admits; a refusal names both. A home with no closure entry
// at all is unread, never assumed acyclic.
fn roster_cycle_refusal(closures: List<RosterHomeClosure>, home: String, module: String) -> Optional<RosterRefusalReason> {
  fold_list(xs: closures, empty: Present { value: RefusalHomeClosureUnread { home: home } }, cons: fn(acc, c) {
    match c {
      RosterClosureRead { home: h, modules: ms } =>
        if h != home { acc } else if roster_contains(xs: ms, name: module) { Present { value: RefusalImportClosesCycle { home: home, module: module } } } else { Absent }
      RosterClosureUnread { home: h } => if h == home { Present { value: RefusalHomeClosureUnread { home: home } } } else { acc }
    }
  })
}

fn roster_refuse_row(path: String, reason: RosterRefusalReason) -> String {
  "REFUSE " + path + " " + roster_refusal_text(reason: reason) + "\n"
}

type RosterOutcome
  = RosterClean
  | RosterEdit { start: Int, end: Int, text: String, own_line: Bool }
  | RosterLabelEdits { edits: List<RosterLabelEdit> }
  | RosterEditWithLabels { start: Int, end: Int, text: String, own_line: Bool, labels: List<RosterLabelEdit> }
  | RosterRefused { reason: RosterRefusalReason }

// THE ONE TYPED FACT OF A PIPE SITE'S HEAD (agreed with wise-moth-707 and tidy-ant-251 for #15083 RelocateHeadStep): the edit
// carrying it removes exactly the base head (its own start and `from`, not restated here), and the splice writes `to` then
// `suffix` at insert_at -- the only write at that offset. The written text BEGINS WITH `to` by construction: the carrier holds
// the head name and what follows it, never a whole text that might not start with the head (review 86155, DESIGN section 5).
type RosterHeadRelocation {
  insert_at: Int
  to: String
  suffix: String
}

type RosterLabelEdit {
  start: Int
  end: Int
  from: String
  to: String
  // A PIPE SITE'S HEAD RELOCATION, on the edit that removes exactly the base head: see RosterHeadRelocation. The occurrence
  // join (#15083 RelocateHeadStep) maps the one by the other instead of refusing a covered head. Absent on every other edit.
  // DISSOLVES WITH A3 (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode pipe_into_a_declared_function_resolves_as_a_method): once a pipe into a
  // declared function resolves natively, a pipe site keeps its pipe, the head is renamed in place, and nothing relocates.
  relocation: Optional<RosterHeadRelocation>
}

fn roster_head_rows() -> List<RosterHeadRow> {
  [
    RosterHeadRow { call: "shell_materialize_operation_argv", key: "shell_materialize_operation_argv", import_name: "shell_materialize_operation_argv", home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.operation_argv"), labels: [], head: KeepHead },
    RosterHeadRow { call: "concat", key: "concat", import_name: "collection_concat_shape", home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.algebra"), labels: [], head: KeepHead },
    RosterHeadRow { call: "count", key: "count", import_name: "collection_count_shape", home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.algebra"), labels: [], head: KeepHead },
    RosterHeadRow { call: "map", key: "map", import_name: "collection_map_shape", home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.algebra"), labels: [], head: KeepHead },
    RosterHeadRow { call: "join", key: "join", import_name: "collection_join_shape", home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.algebra"), labels: [], head: KeepHead },
    // list_push is FreeMonoid's own snoc (tidy-ant-251 ruling): one ambient name, one declared home std.algebra.
    RosterHeadRow { call: "list_push", key: "list_push", import_name: "list_push", home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.algebra"), labels: [], head: KeepHead },
    // sha256_hex_of_text: UTF-8 encode, SHA-256, lowercase hex; one declared home beside sha256_hex_digest (sleek-owl-397).
    RosterHeadRow { call: "sha256_hex_of_text", key: "sha256_hex_of_text", import_name: "sha256_hex_of_text", home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.content_hash"), labels: [], head: KeepHead },
    // compile_dag_diagnostic_census is the census builtin's one declared home (root-coordinator decision, sleek-owl-397).
    RosterHeadRow { call: "compile_dag_diagnostic_census", key: "compile_dag_diagnostic_census", import_name: "compile_dag_diagnostic_census", home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "gunbc.compile_diagnostic_census"), labels: [], head: KeepHead },
    // map_keys is the map's key support (sleek-owl-397 root-coordinator decision): one ambient name, one declared home std.algebra.
    RosterHeadRow { call: "map_keys", key: "map_keys", import_name: "map_keys", home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.algebra"), labels: [], head: KeepHead },
    // NAMESPACE-XL wave 1 (tidy-ant-251's H2/H4 rulings, #14233): chars has one declared home.
    RosterHeadRow {
      call: "chars",
      key: "chars",
      import_name: "chars",
      home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.host_text"),
      // std.host_text declares fn chars(text: HostText); the ambient spelling's callers wrote s:.
      labels: [RosterLabelRename { from: "s", to: "text" }],
      head: KeepHead
    },
    // map_get's operation is ALREADY declared (tidy-ant-251's ruling A): std.algebra map_lookup(m, key), the same keyed
    // read with the same Optional<V> answer, so the call moves to that declaration instead of minting a second name for it.
    RosterHeadRow {
      call: "map_get",
      key: "map_get",
      import_name: "map_lookup",
      home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.algebra"),
      labels: [],
      head: RenameHead { to: "map_lookup", positional: ["m", "key"] }
    }
  ]
}

// THE VERDICT IS CONVERGENCE: no pending rows is ExitSuccess (the post-apply re-run), pending rows
// are an ExitFailure whose reason IS the rows, so a refused or unconverged sweep cannot read as done.
fn roster_import_sweep_exit(paths_csv: String) -> ProcessExit {
  let rows = roster_import_sweep_for_paths(paths_csv: paths_csv)
  if (rows == "") { ExitSuccess } else { exit_failure(reason: rows) }
}

// ONE WAVE'S ROWS: the same generator restricted to the rows whose home is `home` (a NAMESPACE-XL wave moves one name;
// a file's pending rows for other homes are another wave's and are neither emitted nor applied here). The dotted argument is
// read into a QualifiedName at this boundary, once.
fn roster_import_sweep_home_exit(paths_csv: String, home: String) -> ProcessExit {
  let scope = OneHome { home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: home), rows: EveryRowOfHome }
  let rows = match dag_prepared_grammar() {
    Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => roster_refuse_row(path: "*", reason: RefusalGrammarUnprepared)
    Accepted { value: prepared, diagnostics: _ } => roster_sweep_all(paths_csv: paths_csv, prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex(), scope: scope)
  }
  if (rows == "") { ExitSuccess } else { exit_failure(reason: rows) }
}

// THE RENAME CENSUS (tidy-ant-251's condition 2 on the map_get ruling): report-only, one home, one asked call spelling.
// Every file gets a `CENSUS <path> call=<call> heads=<n>` line -- the lexical primary heads spelled `call`, the population
// to account for -- followed by exactly the rows the sweep would emit for it (EDIT, LABEL, REFUSE), from ONE read and ONE
// parse of the file. A head that is counted but planned no edit is bound elsewhere (a parameter, a local, a module-level
// declaration, an import of another `call`) and the sweep's own classifier says so; a disagreement refuses located. A
// method spelling (`x.call`) is not a primary head and is not counted. Nothing is written.
fn roster_rename_census_exit(paths_csv: String, home: String, call: String) -> ProcessExit {
  let scope = OneHome { home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: home), rows: OnlyCall { call: call } }
  match roster_scope_selection_refusal_in(table: roster_head_rows(), scope: scope) {
    Present { value: reason } => exit_failure(reason: roster_refuse_row(path: "*", reason: reason))
    Absent => roster_rename_census_selected(paths_csv: paths_csv, scope: scope, call: call)
  }
}

fn roster_rename_census_selected(paths_csv: String, scope: RosterHomeScope, call: String) -> ProcessExit {
  match dag_prepared_grammar() {
    Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => exit_failure(reason: roster_refuse_row(path: "*", reason: RefusalGrammarUnprepared))
    Accepted { value: prepared, diagnostics: _ } =>
      let closures = roster_home_closures(root: "", scope: scope)
      let lex = dag_prepared_lex()
      let sides = roster_home_sides(rows: roster_rows_for_scope(scope: scope))
      let companions = roster_rename_companions(rows: roster_rows_for_scope(scope: scope), prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
      exit_failure(reason: fold_list(
        xs: split(s: paths_csv, delimiter: ","),
        empty: "",
        cons: fn(acc, path) { acc + roster_census_path(sides: sides, companions: companions, path: path, prepared: prepared, lex: lex, scope: scope, closures: closures, call: call) }
      ))
  }
}

fn roster_census_path(sides: List<RosterHomeSide>, companions: List<RosterCompanion>, path: String, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules, scope: RosterHomeScope, closures: List<RosterHomeClosure>, call: String) -> String {
  let read = Filesystem.Read(path: path)
  if read.success {
    let census = roster_census_text_rows(sides: sides, companions: companions, path: path, text: read.content, prepared: prepared, lex: lex, candidates: roster_rows_for_scope(scope: scope), closures: closures, census_call: Present { value: call }, gates: roster_scope_gates(scope: scope, path: path, text: read.content))
    "CENSUS " + path + " call=" + call + " heads=" + int_to_decimal_string(value: census.heads) + "\n" + roster_render_outcome(path: path, outcome: census.outcome)
  } else {
    roster_refuse_row(path: path, reason: RefusalUnreadable)
  }
}

fn roster_import_sweep_apply_home_exit(root_dir: String, paths_csv: String, home: String) -> ProcessExit {
  let report = roster_apply_for_paths(root_dir: root_dir, paths_csv: paths_csv, home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: home), rows: EveryRowOfHome)
  if (report == "") { ExitSuccess } else { exit_failure(reason: report) }
}

// ONE WAVE'S ROW: the run and the apply restricted to the row whose home is `home` AND whose call is `call` -- the grain a
// wave actually moves. A file's other rows of the same home are another wave's and are neither emitted nor applied here.
fn roster_import_sweep_row_exit(paths_csv: String, home: String, call: String) -> ProcessExit {
  let scope = OneHome { home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: home), rows: OnlyCall { call: call } }
  let rows = match dag_prepared_grammar() {
    Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => roster_refuse_row(path: "*", reason: RefusalGrammarUnprepared)
    Accepted { value: prepared, diagnostics: _ } => roster_sweep_all(paths_csv: paths_csv, prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex(), scope: scope)
  }
  if (rows == "") { ExitSuccess } else { exit_failure(reason: rows) }
}

fn roster_import_sweep_apply_row_exit(root_dir: String, paths_csv: String, home: String, call: String) -> ProcessExit {
  let report = roster_apply_for_paths(root_dir: root_dir, paths_csv: paths_csv, home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: home), rows: OnlyCall { call: call })
  if (report == "") { ExitSuccess } else { exit_failure(reason: report) }
}

// THE PER-SITE WAVE ENTRY (NAMESPACE-XL, manager ruling): one row, and the SITES it acts on arrive as a
// one-shot input FILE of census location keys (`<file>:<line>:<byte column>`, one per line) -- never a landed artifact,
// never a fallback to sweeping the spelling. A wave needs this because ONE SPELLING splits by ARGUMENT TYPE
// (kernel Int vs kernel Nat vs Bool vs Float vs List vs record) and the sweep matches no type: the typed census, not the
// row, decides which half is this wave's. A key that meets no site refuses the run (RefusalOccurrenceKeyUnmatched); an
// empty key file refuses before any read (RefusalScopeSelectsNoRow).
fn roster_import_sweep_occurrences_exit(paths_csv: String, home: String, row_key: String, call: String, keys_file: String) -> ProcessExit {
  let selection = roster_occurrence_selection(keys_file: keys_file)
  let scope = OneHome { home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: home), rows: OnlyOccurrences { row: row_key, call: call, occurrences: roster_selection_keys(selection: selection) } }
  let rows = match selection {
    RosterKeysRead { keys: _ } =>
      match dag_prepared_grammar() {
        Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => roster_refuse_row(path: "*", reason: RefusalGrammarUnprepared)
        Accepted { value: prepared, diagnostics: _ } => roster_sweep_all(paths_csv: paths_csv, prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex(), scope: scope)
      }
    RosterKeysRefused { detail: _ } => roster_refuse_row(path: keys_file, reason: RefusalUnreadable)
  }
  if (rows == "") { ExitSuccess } else { exit_failure(reason: rows) }
}

fn roster_import_sweep_apply_occurrences_exit(root_dir: String, paths_csv: String, home: String, row_key: String, call: String, keys_file: String) -> ProcessExit {
  let selection = roster_occurrence_selection(keys_file: keys_file)
  let report = match selection {
    RosterKeysRead { keys: ks } =>
      roster_apply_occurrences(root_dir: root_dir, paths_csv: paths_csv, home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: home), row_key: row_key, call: call, keys: ks)
    RosterKeysRefused { detail: _ } => roster_refuse_row(path: keys_file, reason: RefusalUnreadable)
  }
  if (report == "") { ExitSuccess } else { exit_failure(reason: report) }
}

type RosterKeySelection
  = RosterKeysRead { keys: List<String> }
  | RosterKeysRefused { detail: String }

fn roster_selection_keys(selection: RosterKeySelection) -> List<String> {
  match selection {
    RosterKeysRead { keys: ks } => ks
    RosterKeysRefused { detail: _ } => []
  }
}

// Keys are read from a file the wave harness generated ONE-SHOT from the typed census (the census TSV itself is never
// landed). Blank lines are dropped; a key that is not exactly file:line:column is refused at the SITE join, where the
// refusal names the key, so the read stays simple and the verdict stays located.
fn roster_occurrence_selection(keys_file: String) -> RosterKeySelection {
  let read = Filesystem.Read(path: keys_file)
  if !read.success {
    RosterKeysRefused { detail: "cannot read " + keys_file }
  } else {
    RosterKeysRead { keys: roster_dedupe(base: [], more: roster_key_lines(text: read.content)) }
  }
}

fn roster_key_lines(text: String) -> List<String> {
  fold_list(xs: split(s: text, delimiter: "\n"), empty: [], cons: fn(acc, k) {
    let t = roster_trim(text: k)
    if t == "" { acc } else { list_snoc_item(xs: acc, item: t) }
  })
}

fn roster_trim(text: String) -> String {
  match split(s: text, delimiter: "\r") {
    Empty => text
    Cons { head: t, tail: _ } => t
  }
}

// The apply restricted to occurrence keys: the SAME apply the row grain uses (base-census provenance, stale-read check,
// apply lock), with OnlyOccurrences as the selection. The gate is derived from the scope at read time, so what the
// admission instrument recomputes from the same scope byte-equals what this applied -- the gate is a property of the
// scope, and the instrument recomputes from the scope.
fn roster_apply_occurrences(root_dir: String, paths_csv: String, home: QualifiedName, row_key: String, call: String, keys: List<String>) -> String {
  roster_apply_for_paths(root_dir: root_dir, paths_csv: paths_csv, home: home, rows: OnlyOccurrences { row: row_key, call: call, occurrences: keys })
}

// ONE HomeKindSide PER ROW, READ ONCE WHEN A RUN STARTS (v2.workflow.roster_home_kind roster_home_sides_read, one census read per home directory) and carried
// to every site fold; the site folds never ask the census themselves.
fn roster_home_sides(rows: List<RosterHeadRow>) -> List<RosterHomeSide> {
  roster_home_sides_read(asks: list_map(xs: rows, f: fn(r) { RosterHomeAsk { home: roster_qn_text(qn: r.home), import_name: r.import_name } }))
}

fn roster_rows_for_scope(scope: RosterHomeScope) -> List<RosterHeadRow> {
  roster_rows_for_scope_in(table: roster_head_rows(), scope: scope)
}

fn roster_rows_for_scope_in(table: List<RosterHeadRow>, scope: RosterHomeScope) -> List<RosterHeadRow> {
  fold_list(xs: table, empty: [], cons: fn(acc, r) { if roster_scope_admits(scope: scope, row: r) { list_snoc_item(xs: acc, item: r) } else { acc } })
}

// THE SCOPE MUST SELECT WHAT IT NAMES, checked once before any read, lock or write (side chat on #14883). A one-home scope
// selecting no row of the table is a typo or a wrong home, never a converged wave; an OnlyCall selecting several rows is a
// table defect the wave cannot resolve. AllHomes names no row and selects the table as it is. Pure over the supplied table so
// the several-rows arm has an authorable RED (the production table holds no duplicate).
fn roster_scope_selection_refusal_in(table: List<RosterHeadRow>, scope: RosterHomeScope) -> Optional<RosterRefusalReason> {
  let selected = roster_rows_for_scope_in(table: table, scope: scope)
  match scope {
    AllHomes => Absent
    OneHome { home: h, rows: sel } =>
      match sel {
        EveryRowOfHome =>
          if is_empty(xs: selected) { Present { value: RefusalScopeSelectsNoRow { home: roster_qn_text(qn: h), selection: "every-row" } } } else { Absent }
        OnlyCall { call: c } =>
          if is_empty(xs: selected) {
            Present { value: RefusalScopeSelectsNoRow { home: roster_qn_text(qn: h), selection: "call=" + c } }
          } else if length(xs: selected) > 1 {
            Present { value: RefusalScopeSelectsSeveralRows { home: roster_qn_text(qn: h), call: c, count: length(xs: selected) } }
          } else {
            Absent
          }
        // The per-site grain checks the same row-selection facts as OnlyCall, PLUS that the selection carries keys at
        // all: an OnlyOccurrences with an empty key list would gate EVERY site of the call off, sweeping nothing while
        // reporting Clean -- an empty claim is a broken claim, refused before any read.
        OnlyOccurrences { row: k, call: c, occurrences: os } =>
          if is_empty(xs: os) {
            Present { value: RefusalScopeSelectsNoRow { home: roster_qn_text(qn: h), selection: "row=" + k + " call=" + c + " occurrences=empty" } }
          } else if is_empty(xs: selected) {
            Present { value: RefusalScopeSelectsNoRow { home: roster_qn_text(qn: h), selection: "row=" + k + " call=" + c } }
          } else if length(xs: selected) > 1 {
            Present { value: RefusalScopeSelectsSeveralRows { home: roster_qn_text(qn: h), call: c, count: length(xs: selected) } }
          } else {
            Absent
          }
      }
  }
}

// The grammar and lex rules are prepared ONCE per run and passed down: preparing them per file
// re-derived the same compiled ground for every path (the cost that made an 83-file run take 25+ minutes).
fn roster_import_sweep_for_paths(paths_csv: String) -> String {
  match dag_prepared_grammar() {
    Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => roster_refuse_row(path: "*", reason: RefusalGrammarUnprepared)
    Accepted { value: prepared, diagnostics: _ } =>
      roster_sweep_all(paths_csv: paths_csv, prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex(), scope: AllHomes)
  }
}

// A KEY NAMING A FILE OUTSIDE THE RUN'S PATHS meets no file's run, so it would vanish without a refusal: refused here, once,
// before any read, lock or write (DESIGN section 5, never a silent narrowing). The census location column is `<file>:<line>:<col>`.
fn roster_key_outside_paths(paths_csv: String, scope: RosterHomeScope) -> Optional<RosterRefusalReason> {
  let paths = split(s: paths_csv, delimiter: ",")
  match scope {
    AllHomes => Absent
    OneHome { home: _, rows: sel } =>
      match sel {
        OnlyOccurrences { row: _, call: c, occurrences: os } =>
          fold_list(xs: os, empty: Absent, cons: fn(acc, k) {
            match acc {
              Present { value: r } => Present { value: r }
              Absent => if roster_contains(xs: paths, name: roster_key_file(key: k)) { Absent } else { Present { value: RefusalOccurrenceKeyUnmatched { path: roster_key_file(key: k), call: c, key: k } } }
            }
          })
        EveryRowOfHome => Absent
        OnlyCall { call: _ } => Absent
      }
  }
}

fn roster_selection_and_paths_refusal(paths_csv: String, scope: RosterHomeScope) -> Optional<RosterRefusalReason> {
  match roster_scope_selection_refusal_in(table: roster_head_rows(), scope: scope) {
    Present { value: r } => Present { value: r }
    Absent => roster_key_outside_paths(paths_csv: paths_csv, scope: scope)
  }
}

fn roster_sweep_all(paths_csv: String, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules, scope: RosterHomeScope) -> String {
  match roster_selection_and_paths_refusal(paths_csv: paths_csv, scope: scope) {
    Present { value: reason } => roster_refuse_row(path: "*", reason: reason)
    Absent => roster_sweep_selected(paths_csv: paths_csv, prepared: prepared, lex: lex, scope: scope)
  }
}

fn roster_sweep_selected(paths_csv: String, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules, scope: RosterHomeScope) -> String {
  let closures = roster_home_closures(root: "", scope: scope)
  let sides = roster_home_sides(rows: roster_rows_for_scope(scope: scope))
  let companions = roster_rename_companions(rows: roster_rows_for_scope(scope: scope), prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
  fold_list(
    xs: split(s: paths_csv, delimiter: ","),
    empty: "",
    cons: fn(acc, path) { acc + roster_sweep_path(sides: sides, companions: companions, path: path, prepared: prepared, lex: lex, scope: scope, closures: closures) }
  )
}

fn roster_sweep_path(sides: List<RosterHomeSide>, companions: List<RosterCompanion>, path: String, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules, scope: RosterHomeScope, closures: List<RosterHomeClosure>) -> String {
  let read = Filesystem.Read(path: path)
  if read.success {
    roster_render_outcome(path: path, outcome: roster_sweep_text_scoped(sides: sides, companions: companions, path: path, text: read.content, prepared: prepared, lex: lex, scope: scope, closures: closures))
  } else {
    roster_refuse_row(path: path, reason: RefusalUnreadable)
  }
}

// THE APPLY STEP, in the same entry family as the generator: the file is read, the outcome computed,
// the file re-read and required byte-identical to what the outcome was computed from (a stale-read check; the apply
// holds an exclusive create-new lock file for its whole run, so two appliers cannot interleave, but a writer that is
// not this applier and writes between the re-read and the write is outside the contract: the worktree must be
// exclusively owned for the run, std.durable_compare_and_set being a generation-slot store that cannot reach a source file),
// the extent required to hold what the parsed decl said it holds, and only then written with
// Filesystem.Write. Anything else is a REFUSE row and the file is untouched. Success is silent, so the
// exit reason is exactly the refusals.
// ONE HOME PER MUTATING RUN, BY CONSTRUCTION (side chat on #14513). The cycle verdict reads each home's closure once, at
// the start of the run; two homes applied in one run could each be admitted against that snapshot (H1 -> H2 and H2 -> H1)
// and together close a cycle. The apply path therefore takes exactly one home (roster_apply_for_paths), so a multi-home
// mutation has no construction, and this home-less entry refuses, typed. A wave is one home; AllHomes stays a read-and-
// report scope (roster_import_sweep_for_paths), whose rows no route applies.
fn roster_import_sweep_apply_exit(root_dir: String, paths_csv: String) -> ProcessExit {
  exit_failure(reason: roster_refuse_row(path: "*", reason: RefusalApplyNeedsOneHome))
}

// THE LOCK IDENTITY is derived from the worktree root the caller names (an absolute path with no `.`, `..` or empty
// segment), never from the working directory: two invocations from different directories on the same root contend for
// the same file. Every target is a relative path confined under that root (no leading `/`, no `.`, `..` or empty segment);
// a target that is not is refused before any read. The effectful steps take a RosterHeldLock, whose only constructor is
// roster_lock_acquire, and roster_apply_edit re-checks that the lock file still exists before it writes, so an entry
// that never acquired the lock refuses `lock-not-held` and writes nothing. The root and every target are then checked
// against git itself (roster_root_is_toplevel, roster_target_refusal), which also covers symlinks.
// WHY NOT std.durable_exclusive_hold / std.temporal_effect::HeldLease (DESIGN §3b leasing home): durable_hold_*_assess
// and held_lease are pure assessments over a caller-supplied observation; none of them takes or releases anything, and no
// durable store for a source tree exists to observe. Using them first needs that store plus holder-liveness reporting,
// which is more machinery than the apply they would guard. The cost of the lock file is a stuck lock after a killed run:
// loud (every later apply refuses `apply-lock-unavailable` naming the root, writing nothing) and cleared by the root's
// single owner deleting `<root>/.roster_import_sweep.lock`. Expiry and stale-holder recovery are not built.
// TRIGGER to move onto the hold home: the first apply run by more than one writer or unattended (CI), when the
// durable-hold store and liveness report exist.
type RosterHeldLock sole_constructor {
  root: String
  nonce: String
}

type RosterLockAcquisition
  = RosterLockAcquired { held: RosterHeldLock }
  | RosterLockRefused { reason: RosterRefusalReason }

fn roster_segments_admitted(segments: List<String>) -> Bool {
  fold_list(xs: segments, empty: true, cons: fn(ok, seg) { ok && seg != "" && seg != "." && seg != ".." })
}

fn roster_root_admitted(root_dir: String) -> Bool {
  match split(s: root_dir, delimiter: "/") {
    Cons { head: first, tail: rest } => first == "" && !is_empty(xs: rest) && roster_segments_admitted(segments: rest)
    Empty => false
  }
}

fn roster_path_admitted(path: String) -> Bool {
  roster_segments_admitted(segments: split(s: path, delimiter: "/"))
}

fn roster_lock_file(root: String) -> String {
  root + "/.roster_import_sweep.lock"
}

fn roster_generation_file(root: String) -> String {
  root + "/.roster_import_sweep.generation"
}

fn roster_lock_body(nonce: String) -> String {
  "roster_import_sweep_apply nonce=" + nonce + "\n"
}

// THE ROOT IS WHAT GIT SAYS IT IS. `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` (git.Inspect.Toplevel, the declared git tool) answers the
// real toplevel of the working directory, symlinks resolved; the root must equal it, so a symlinked or subdirectory
// spelling of the same worktree is refused and one worktree has one lock identity. Toplevel takes no input: the
// observation is of the CLI's working directory, which is why the target checks below also require the root to be it.
fn roster_root_is_toplevel(root_dir: String) -> Bool {
  let top = git.Inspect.Toplevel().path as String
  top == root_dir
}

// A TARGET IS WRITTEN ONLY IF GIT TRACKS IT AS A REGULAR UNMODIFIED FILE. `git ls-tree HEAD -- <path>` names the entry's mode
// (100644 regular; 120000 a symlink; nothing for an untracked path or one behind a symlinked directory, which git does not
// track through), and `git status --porcelain` must not name the path (unmodified, so the sweep never lands on someone's
// uncommitted work). Both are git's own observation; nothing here resolves a path itself. Returns Absent when admitted, else the reason.
fn roster_target_refusal(root: String, path: String) -> Optional<RosterRefusalReason> {
  if !roster_root_is_toplevel(root_dir: root) {
    Present { value: RefusalRootNotGitToplevel }
  } else {
    let tree = git.Inspect.ListTreeEntryAtPath(ref: "HEAD" as GitRef, path: path)
    let status = git.Inspect.WorkingTreeStatus(repository_path: root)
    let flags = git.Inspect.IndexFlagsIn(repository_path: root, path: path)
    if !tree.success || !status.success || !flags.success {
      Present { value: RefusalGitUnobservable }
    } else if string_length(s: tree.entries_nul) < 12 || substring(s: tree.entries_nul, start: 0, end: 12) != "100644 blob " {
      Present { value: RefusalTargetNotTrackedRegular }
    } else if flags.entries_nul != "H " + path + "\u{0}" {
      Present { value: RefusalTargetIndexFlagged }
    } else if roster_status_names_path(entries_nul: status.entries_nul, path: path) {
      Present { value: RefusalTargetModified }
    } else if roster_status_names_ancestor(entries_nul: status.entries_nul, path: path) {
      Present { value: RefusalTargetAncestorChanged }
    } else {
      Absent
    }
  }
}

fn roster_ends_with_space_path(field: String, path: String) -> Bool {
  let n = string_length(s: field)
  let m = string_length(s: path)
  n > m && substring(s: field, start: n - m - 1, end: n) == " " + path
}

// ANY status entry naming a directory above the target (`?? src` for a replaced directory, a typechange, a deletion) refuses the
// target: the committed tree says nothing about what the worktree path now resolves through.
fn roster_status_names_ancestor(entries_nul: String, path: String) -> Bool {
  fold_list(xs: split(s: entries_nul, delimiter: "\u{0}"), empty: false, cons: fn(hit, f) { hit || roster_names_ancestor(candidate: f, path: path) || (string_length(s: f) > 3 && substring(s: f, start: 2, end: 3) == " " && roster_names_ancestor(candidate: substring(s: f, start: 3, end: string_length(s: f)), path: path)) })
}

fn roster_names_ancestor(candidate: String, path: String) -> Bool {
  let dir = if string_length(s: candidate) > 0 && substring(s: candidate, start: string_length(s: candidate) - 1, end: string_length(s: candidate)) == "/" { candidate } else { candidate + "/" }
  string_length(s: candidate) > 0 && string_length(s: path) > string_length(s: dir) && substring(s: path, start: 0, end: string_length(s: dir)) == dir
}

// porcelain v1 -z fields are "XY path", and a rename source is the bare path: either spelling names the path.
fn roster_status_names_path(entries_nul: String, path: String) -> Bool {
  fold_list(xs: split(s: entries_nul, delimiter: "\u{0}"), empty: false, cons: fn(hit, f) { hit || f == path || roster_ends_with_space_path(field: f, path: path) })
}

// The generation history is either established or it is not: an ABSENT file is the first use of this root; any other read
// failure leaves the history unestablished, and acquisition refuses rather than restarting the count (which would let an
// old token's nonce match again).
type RosterGenerationHistory
  = RosterHistoryKnown { content: String }
  | RosterHistoryUnestablished

fn roster_generation_history(success: Bool, content: String, error_kind: String) -> RosterGenerationHistory {
  if success {
    RosterHistoryKnown { content: content }
  } else if error_kind == "not_found" {
    RosterHistoryKnown { content: "" }
  } else {
    RosterHistoryUnestablished
  }
}

// ONE NONCE PER ACQUISITION. The generation file is written only while the lock is held, one more character per
// acquisition, so the nonce is the count of acquisitions on this root and a token from an earlier holder never equals
// the current lock's nonce. (Neither lock file nor generation file is tracked; both are scratch beside the tree.)
fn roster_lock_acquire(root_dir: String) -> RosterLockAcquisition {
  if !roster_root_admitted(root_dir: root_dir) {
    RosterLockRefused { reason: RefusalRootNotAbsoluteCanonical }
  } else if !roster_root_is_toplevel(root_dir: root_dir) {
    RosterLockRefused { reason: RefusalRootNotGitToplevel }
  } else {
    roster_lock_take(root_dir: root_dir)
  }
}

// The lock-file mechanics alone, with no claim about the root: acquire is the only caller that admits a root; the controls
// call this on a scratch directory that is not a git toplevel.
fn roster_lock_take(root_dir: String) -> RosterLockAcquisition {
  if !Filesystem.WriteCreateNew(path: roster_lock_file(root: root_dir), content: "roster_import_sweep_apply pending\n").success {
    RosterLockRefused { reason: RefusalApplyLockUnavailable }
  } else {
    let prior = Filesystem.Read(path: roster_generation_file(root: root_dir))
    match roster_generation_history(success: prior.success, content: prior.content, error_kind: prior.error_kind) {
      RosterHistoryUnestablished => {
        let undone = Filesystem.Delete(path: roster_lock_file(root: root_dir))
        RosterLockRefused { reason: RefusalGenerationHistoryUnestablished }
      }
      RosterHistoryKnown { content: before } => {
        let nonce = int_to_decimal_string(value: string_length(s: before) + 1)
        if Filesystem.Write(path: roster_generation_file(root: root_dir), content: before + "x").success && Filesystem.Write(path: roster_lock_file(root: root_dir), content: roster_lock_body(nonce: nonce)).success {
          RosterLockAcquired { held: RosterHeldLock { root: root_dir, nonce: nonce } }
        } else {
          let undone = Filesystem.Delete(path: roster_lock_file(root: root_dir))
          RosterLockRefused { reason: RefusalLockWriteFailed }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

fn roster_lock_still_held(held: RosterHeldLock) -> Bool {
  let now = Filesystem.Read(path: roster_lock_file(root: held.root))
  now.success && now.content == roster_lock_body(nonce: held.nonce)
}

// Release only what this acquisition owns: a token whose nonce no longer matches the lock file deletes nothing.
fn roster_lock_release(held: RosterHeldLock) -> Bool {
  roster_lock_still_held(held: held) && Filesystem.Delete(path: roster_lock_file(root: held.root)).success
}

fn roster_apply_for_paths(root_dir: String, paths_csv: String, home: QualifiedName, rows: RosterRowSelection) -> String {
  let scope = OneHome { home: home, rows: rows }
  match roster_selection_and_paths_refusal(paths_csv: paths_csv, scope: scope) {
    Present { value: reason } => roster_refuse_row(path: "*", reason: reason)
    Absent =>
      match roster_lock_acquire(root_dir: root_dir) {
        RosterLockRefused { reason: reason } => roster_refuse_row(path: "*", reason: reason)
        RosterLockAcquired { held: held } => {
          let report = roster_apply_locked(held: held, paths_csv: paths_csv, scope: scope)
          if roster_lock_release(held: held) { report } else { report + roster_refuse_row(path: "*", reason: RefusalApplyLockNotReleased) }
        }
      }
  }
}

fn roster_apply_locked(held: RosterHeldLock, paths_csv: String, scope: RosterHomeScope) -> String {
  match dag_prepared_grammar() {
    Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => roster_refuse_row(path: "*", reason: RefusalGrammarUnprepared)
    Accepted { value: prepared, diagnostics: _ } => {
      let closures = roster_home_closures(root: held.root, scope: scope)
      let sides = roster_home_sides(rows: roster_rows_for_scope(scope: scope))
      let companions = roster_rename_companions(rows: roster_rows_for_scope(scope: scope), prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex())
      fold_list(
        xs: split(s: paths_csv, delimiter: ","),
        empty: "",
        cons: fn(acc, path) { acc + roster_apply_path(sides: sides, companions: companions, held: held, path: path, prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex(), scope: scope, closures: closures) }
      )
    }
  }
}

fn roster_apply_path(sides: List<RosterHomeSide>, companions: List<RosterCompanion>, held: RosterHeldLock, path: String, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules, scope: RosterHomeScope, closures: List<RosterHomeClosure>) -> String {
  if !roster_path_admitted(path: path) {
    roster_refuse_row(path: path, reason: RefusalPathOutsideRoot)
  } else {
    let read = Filesystem.Read(path: held.root + "/" + path)
    if read.success {
      match roster_sweep_text_scoped(sides: sides, companions: companions, path: path, text: read.content, prepared: prepared, lex: lex, scope: scope, closures: closures) {
        RosterClean => ""
        RosterRefused { reason: reason } => roster_refuse_row(path: path, reason: reason)
        RosterEdit { start: start, end: end, text: text, own_line: own_line } =>
          roster_apply_edit(held: held, path: path, before: read.content, outcome: RosterEdit { start: start, end: end, text: text, own_line: own_line })
        RosterLabelEdits { edits: edits } =>
          roster_apply_edit(held: held, path: path, before: read.content, outcome: RosterLabelEdits { edits: edits })
        RosterEditWithLabels { start: st, end: en, text: tx, own_line: ol, labels: ls } =>
          roster_apply_edit(held: held, path: path, before: read.content, outcome: RosterEditWithLabels { start: st, end: en, text: tx, own_line: ol, labels: ls })
      }
    } else {
      roster_refuse_row(path: path, reason: RefusalUnreadable)
    }
  }
}

fn roster_apply_edit(held: RosterHeldLock, path: String, before: String, outcome: RosterOutcome) -> String {
  if !roster_path_admitted(path: path) {
    roster_refuse_row(path: path, reason: RefusalPathOutsideRoot)
  } else if !roster_lock_still_held(held: held) {
    roster_refuse_row(path: path, reason: RefusalLockNotHeld)
  } else {
    match roster_target_refusal(root: held.root, path: path) {
      Present { value: refusal } => roster_refuse_row(path: path, reason: refusal)
      Absent =>
        if !roster_target_unchanged(root: held.root, path: path, before: before) {
          roster_refuse_row(path: path, reason: RefusalStaleRead)
        } else {
          match roster_applied(before: before, outcome: outcome) {
            RosterApplyRefused { reason: reason } => roster_refuse_row(path: path, reason: reason)
            RosterApplyWritten { content: content } =>
              if content == before {
                ""
              } else if Filesystem.Write(path: held.root + "/" + path, content: content).success {
                ""
              } else {
                roster_refuse_row(path: path, reason: RefusalWriteFailed)
              }
          }
        }
    }
  }
}

fn roster_target_unchanged(root: String, path: String, before: String) -> Bool {
  let now = Filesystem.Read(path: root + "/" + path)
  now.success && now.content == before
}

type RosterApplied
  = RosterApplyWritten { content: String }
  | RosterApplyRefused { reason: RosterRefusalReason }

// THE PURE SPLICE the apply step performs, separate from its filesystem effects so the controls run it on text.
fn roster_applied(before: String, outcome: RosterOutcome) -> RosterApplied {
  match outcome {
    RosterClean => RosterApplyWritten { content: before }
    RosterRefused { reason: reason } => RosterApplyRefused { reason: reason }
    RosterEdit { start: start, end: end, text: text, own_line: own_line } =>
      roster_splice(before: before, start: start, end: end, replacement: roster_edit_replacement(text: text, own_line: own_line))
    RosterLabelEdits { edits: edits } => roster_label_splices(before: before, edits: edits)
    // THE LABELS LAND IN THE SAME WRITE AS THE IMPORT THAT MAKES THEM NECESSARY: a file with the import and the old label
    // does not resolve (the home's parameter is `text`), and a file the generator itself loads would stop the generator.
    // The labels sit below the import, so they are spliced first and the import's offsets stay valid.
    RosterEditWithLabels { start: start, end: end, text: text, own_line: own_line, labels: labels } =>
      match roster_label_splices(before: before, edits: labels) {
        RosterApplyRefused { reason: r } => RosterApplyRefused { reason: r }
        RosterApplyWritten { content: relabelled } =>
          match roster_import_and_labels_disjoint(start: start, end: end, text: text, labels: labels) {
            Present { value: r } => RosterApplyRefused { reason: r }
            Absent =>
              if roster_labels_below(labels: labels, at: end) {
                roster_splice(before: relabelled, start: start, end: end, replacement: roster_edit_replacement(text: text, own_line: own_line))
              } else {
                RosterApplyRefused { reason: RefusalExtentMismatch }
              }
          }
      }
  }
}

// THE IMPORT EDIT AND THE LABEL EDITS ARE ONE PLAN FOR DISJOINTNESS (tidy-ant-251's side chat on #15062): the import
// (possibly zero-width) is checked with every label and head edit by the one predicate, so a zero-width label at the
// import's offset refuses as coincident instead of slipping past a separate check.
fn roster_import_and_labels_disjoint(start: Int, end: Int, text: String, labels: List<RosterLabelEdit>) -> Optional<RosterRefusalReason> {
  let import_edit = RosterLabelEdit { start: start, end: end, from: "", to: text, relocation: Absent }
  match roster_label_edits_disjoint(edits: list_sort_by_key(xs: list_snoc_item(xs: roster_expand_relocations(edits: labels), item: import_edit), key: roster_label_edit_order_key, order: int_total_order())) {
    LabelsRenameRefused { reason: r } => Present { value: r }
    LabelsSelected { edits: _ } => Absent
    LabelsAmbiguous => Present { value: RefusalLabelSitesAmbiguous }
  }
}

// Label edits are applied last-first, so an earlier edit's offsets are unaffected by a later one's length change. Each
// extent must land on scalar boundaries and hold exactly its `from` label; any other byte refuses the whole file.
fn roster_labels_below(labels: List<RosterLabelEdit>, at: Int) -> Bool {
  fold_list(xs: labels, empty: true, cons: fn(ok, e) { ok && e.start >= at })
}

// A RELOCATION EDIT AS ITS TWO WRITES: the removal of exactly the base head, and the insertion of `inserted` at insert_at.
// The disjointness check and the splice both read the plan through this, so the relocated name is an insertion point like
// any other (a second insert there refuses as coincident) and is written exactly once.
fn roster_expand_relocations(edits: List<RosterLabelEdit>) -> List<RosterLabelEdit> {
  let expanded = fold_list(xs: edits, empty: [], cons: fn(acc, e) { roster_expand_relocation_step(acc: acc, e: e) })
  list_sort_by_key(xs: expanded, key: roster_label_edit_order_key, order: int_total_order())
}

fn roster_expand_relocation_step(acc: List<RosterLabelEdit>, e: RosterLabelEdit) -> List<RosterLabelEdit> {
  match e.relocation {
    Absent => list_snoc_item(xs: acc, item: e)
    Present { value: r } =>
      list_snoc_item(xs: list_snoc_item(xs: acc, item: RosterLabelEdit { start: e.start, end: e.end, from: e.from, to: e.to, relocation: Absent }), item: RosterLabelEdit { start: r.insert_at, end: r.insert_at, from: "", to: r.to + r.suffix, relocation: Absent })
  }
}

// THE SPLICE: each relocation expands to its head removal and the `to` + `suffix` write (roster_expand_relocations), applied last-first.
fn roster_label_splices(before: String, edits: List<RosterLabelEdit>) -> RosterApplied {
  let octets = bytes_octets(b: utf8_encode_bytes(s: before))
  fold_list(
    xs: list_reverse(xs: roster_expand_relocations(edits: edits)),
    empty: RosterApplyWritten { content: before },
    cons: fn(acc, e) {
      match acc {
        RosterApplyRefused { reason: r } => RosterApplyRefused { reason: r }
        RosterApplyWritten { content: content } =>
          let from = roster_scalar_boundary(octets: octets, byte: e.start)
          let to = roster_scalar_boundary(octets: octets, byte: e.end)
          if from < 0 || to < from {
            RosterApplyRefused { reason: RefusalExtentNotOnCharBoundary }
          } else if substring(s: content, start: from, end: to) != e.from {
            RosterApplyRefused { reason: RefusalExtentMismatch }
          } else {
            RosterApplyWritten { content: substring(s: content, start: 0, end: from) + e.to + substring(s: content, start: to, end: string_length(s: content)) }
          }
      }
    }
  )
}

fn roster_splice(before: String, start: Int, end: Int, replacement: String) -> RosterApplied {
  let octets = bytes_octets(b: utf8_encode_bytes(s: before))
  let from = roster_scalar_boundary(octets: octets, byte: start)
  let to = roster_scalar_boundary(octets: octets, byte: end)
  if from < 0 || to < from {
    RosterApplyRefused { reason: RefusalExtentNotOnCharBoundary }
  } else if !roster_extent_holds(before: before, start: from, end: to) {
    RosterApplyRefused { reason: RefusalExtentMismatch }
  } else if length(xs: split(s: substring(s: before, start: from, end: to), delimiter: "//")) > 1 {
    RosterApplyRefused { reason: RefusalExtentHasAnnotation }
  } else {
    RosterApplyWritten { content: substring(s: before, start: 0, end: from) + replacement + substring(s: before, start: to, end: string_length(s: before)) }
  }
}

// ByteRange comes from the parser in UTF-8 bytes; substring indexes Unicode scalars. A byte offset converts to the
// scalar offset that precedes it (the count of non-continuation octets before it) and is valid only when it falls
// on a scalar boundary; -1 otherwise.
fn roster_scalar_boundary(octets: List<Int>, byte: Int) -> Int {
  let total = length(xs: octets)
  if byte < 0 || byte > total {
    0 - 1
  } else if byte == total {
    roster_scalar_count_before(octets: octets, byte: byte)
  } else {
    match list_at_optional(xs: octets, index: byte) {
      Present { value: o } => if roster_is_continuation(octet: o) { 0 - 1 } else { roster_scalar_count_before(octets: octets, byte: byte) }
      Absent => -1
    }
  }
}

// The scalars that start before `byte`, in ONE fold over the octets: a prefix copy (take_prefix) recursed once per byte and
// exceeded the evaluator's call depth on a 132 KB file (v2.extdeps.languages.rust_fixtures), so the count is accumulated.
type RosterScalarScan {
  index: Int
  scalars: Int
}

fn roster_scalar_count_before(octets: List<Int>, byte: Int) -> Int {
  fold_list(
    xs: octets,
    empty: RosterScalarScan { index: 0, scalars: 0 },
    cons: fn(acc, o) {
      RosterScalarScan {
        index: acc.index + 1,
        scalars: if acc.index < byte && !roster_is_continuation(octet: o) { acc.scalars + 1 } else { acc.scalars }
      }
    }
  ).scalars
}

fn roster_scalar_count(octets: List<Int>) -> Int {
  fold_list(xs: octets, empty: 0, cons: fn(n, o) { if roster_is_continuation(octet: o) { n } else { n + 1 } })
}

fn roster_is_continuation(octet: Int) -> Bool {
  octet >= 128 && octet < 192
}

// A replaced extent is a whole std.algebra import declaration (it opens with the keyword and the module and ends at
// its closing brace (roster_apply_edit also refuses an extent carrying a `//` annotation, which the replacement would erase); an insertion point is the end of an import block. Offsets here are scalar offsets.
// An insertion holds where the parse put it: after an import block's closing brace, or (a module with no import yet) at the
// end of the module header's line.
fn roster_ends_module_header_line(before: String, at: Int) -> Bool {
  let line = fold_list(xs: split(s: substring(s: before, start: 0, end: at), delimiter: "\n"), empty: "", cons: fn(_last, l) { l })
  substring(s: line, start: 0, end: 7) == "module " && substring(s: before, start: at, end: at + 1) == "\n"
}

fn roster_extent_holds(before: String, start: Int, end: Int) -> Bool {
  if start == end {
    substring(s: before, start: start - 1, end: start) == "}" || roster_ends_module_header_line(before: before, at: start)
  } else {
    substring(s: before, start: start, end: start + 7) == "import " && substring(s: before, start: end - 1, end: end) == "}"
  }
}

// The one rendering of an outcome as protocol rows: replacement newlines are escaped as \n.
// THE REPLACEMENT A ROW CARRIES is exactly the bytes the apply splices in (roster_applied): the own-line newline, then the text.
fn roster_edit_replacement(text: String, own_line: Bool) -> String {
  (if own_line { "\n" } else { "" }) + text
}

// The row encoding of a replacement, total and invertible: backslash first, then newline, so a row is always one line
// and roster_unescape_replacement recovers the bytes exactly.
fn roster_escape_replacement(text: String) -> String {
  roster_join_exact(xs: split(s: roster_join_exact(xs: split(s: text, delimiter: "\\"), sep: "\\\\"), delimiter: "\n"), sep: "\\n")
}

fn roster_unescape_replacement(text: String) -> String {
  roster_join_exact(
    xs: list_map(xs: split(s: text, delimiter: "\\\\"), f: fn(part) { roster_unescape_newlines(part: part) }),
    sep: "\\"
  )
}

fn roster_unescape_newlines(part: String) -> String {
  roster_join_exact(xs: split(s: part, delimiter: "\\n"), sep: "\n")
}

// split's inverse: every part kept, the separator between each adjacent pair, so empty parts (a leading or doubled
// separator) survive. roster_join drops them and is not an inverse.
fn roster_join_exact(xs: List<String>, sep: String) -> String {
  match xs {
    Empty => ""
    Cons { head: h, tail: t } => fold_list(xs: t, empty: h, cons: fn(acc, x) { acc + sep + x })
  }
}

// THE READER of one EDIT row, the round trip the controls hold the renderer to: a row is exactly one line, and its fields
// decode back to the start, end and replacement it was rendered from.
fn roster_edit_row_reads_back(row: String, start: Int, end: Int, replacement: String) -> Bool {
  let lines = split(s: row, delimiter: "\n")
  let fields = split(s: substring(s: row, start: 0, end: string_length(s: row) - 1), delimiter: " ")
  if length(xs: lines) != 2 || length(xs: fields) < 5 {
    false
  } else {
    roster_field(fields: fields, at: 0) == "EDIT"
      && roster_field(fields: fields, at: 2) == int_to_decimal_string(value: start)
      && roster_field(fields: fields, at: 3) == int_to_decimal_string(value: end)
      && roster_unescape_replacement(text: roster_join(xs: roster_fields_from(fields: fields, at: 4), sep: " ")) == replacement
  }
}

fn roster_field(fields: List<String>, at: Int) -> String {
  match list_at_optional(xs: fields, index: at) {
    Present { value: f } => f
    Absent => ""
  }
}

fn roster_fields_from(fields: List<String>, at: Int) -> List<String> {
  fold_list(xs: fields, empty: RosterFieldTail { index: 0, kept: [] }, cons: fn(acc, f) {
    RosterFieldTail { index: acc.index + 1, kept: if acc.index >= at { list_snoc_item(xs: acc.kept, item: f) } else { acc.kept } }
  }).kept
}

type RosterFieldTail {
  index: Int
  kept: List<String>
}

fn roster_render_outcome(path: String, outcome: RosterOutcome) -> String {
  match outcome {
    RosterClean => ""
    RosterEdit { start: start, end: end, text: text, own_line: own_line } =>
      "EDIT " + path + " " + int_to_decimal_string(value: start) + " " + int_to_decimal_string(value: end) + " "
        + roster_escape_replacement(text: roster_edit_replacement(text: text, own_line: own_line)) + "\n"
    RosterEditWithLabels { start: start, end: end, text: text, own_line: own_line, labels: labels } =>
      roster_render_outcome(path: path, outcome: RosterEdit { start: start, end: end, text: text, own_line: own_line })
        + roster_render_outcome(path: path, outcome: RosterLabelEdits { edits: labels })
    RosterLabelEdits { edits: edits } =>
      fold_list(xs: edits, empty: "", cons: fn(acc, e) {
        acc + "LABEL " + path + " " + int_to_decimal_string(value: e.start) + " " + int_to_decimal_string(value: e.end) + " " + e.from + " " + e.to + "\n"
      })
    RosterRefused { reason: reason } => roster_refuse_row(path: path, reason: reason)
  }
}

fn roster_sweep_text(path: String, text: String, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> RosterOutcome {
  roster_sweep_text_scoped(sides: roster_home_sides(rows: roster_head_rows()), companions: [], path: path, text: text, prepared: prepared, lex: lex, scope: AllHomes, closures: roster_control_closures())
}

fn roster_sweep_text_scoped(sides: List<RosterHomeSide>, companions: List<RosterCompanion>, path: String, text: String, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules, scope: RosterHomeScope, closures: List<RosterHomeClosure>) -> RosterOutcome {
  roster_sweep_text_gate(sides: sides, companions: companions, path: path, text: text, prepared: prepared, lex: lex, candidates: roster_rows_for_scope(scope: scope), closures: closures, gates: roster_scope_gates(scope: scope, path: path, text: text))
}

// THE SAME SWEEP OVER AN AUTHORED CANDIDATE LIST. The controls name the exact row they are about (an aliased type home
// the production table does not carry -- Wave 2's shape) so a refusal or a plan is measured against THAT row, never
// against whatever the generator's table happens to hold. The production path reaches it through the scope filter above;
// controls that exercise the PER-SITE grain call roster_sweep_text_gate with the gate they want.
fn roster_sweep_text_rows(sides: List<RosterHomeSide>, companions: List<RosterCompanion>, path: String, text: String, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules, candidates: List<RosterHeadRow>, closures: List<RosterHomeClosure>) -> RosterOutcome {
  roster_sweep_text_gate(sides: sides, companions: companions, path: path, text: text, prepared: prepared, lex: lex, candidates: candidates, closures: closures, gates: [])
}

// THE GATED SWEEP: the per-site selection reaches every site scan in the run through this one parameter, so the
// admission instrument's recomputation (which calls the scoped entry and therefore derives the same gate from the same
// scope) byte-equals what the applier produced -- the gate is a property of the SCOPE, and the scope is what the
// instrument recomputes from.
fn roster_sweep_text_gate(sides: List<RosterHomeSide>, companions: List<RosterCompanion>, path: String, text: String, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules, candidates: List<RosterHeadRow>, closures: List<RosterHomeClosure>, gates: List<RosterSiteGate>) -> RosterOutcome {
  roster_census_text_rows(sides: sides, companions: companions, path: path, text: text, prepared: prepared, lex: lex, candidates: candidates, closures: closures, census_call: Absent, gates: gates).outcome
}

// THE SWEEP'S ONE READ OF A FILE, with the census count beside its outcome: `heads` is the number of parse-tree primary
// heads spelled `census_call` (the lexical population the rename census accounts for; 0 when no call is asked, Absent), counted
// off the same parse the outcome came from, so the census never re-reads or re-parses a file.
type RosterCensusRead {
  outcome: RosterOutcome
  heads: Int
}

fn roster_census_refused(reason: RosterRefusalReason) -> RosterCensusRead {
  RosterCensusRead { outcome: RosterRefused { reason: reason }, heads: 0 }
}

fn roster_census_heads(parse_root: Node, call: Optional<String>) -> Int {
  match call {
    Absent => 0
    Present { value: c } => length(xs: roster_primary_heads(parse_root: parse_root, call: c))
  }
}

fn roster_census_text_rows(sides: List<RosterHomeSide>, companions: List<RosterCompanion>, path: String, text: String, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules, candidates: List<RosterHeadRow>, closures: List<RosterHomeClosure>, census_call: Optional<String>, gates: List<RosterSiteGate>) -> RosterCensusRead {
  match tokenize_prepared(text: text, file: symbol_intern_lexeme(lexeme: path), prepared: lex) {
        Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => roster_census_refused(reason: RefusalTokenizeRefused)
        Accepted { value: stream, diagnostics: _ } =>
          match parse_module_prepared(tokens: stream, prepared: prepared) {
            Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => roster_census_refused(reason: RefusalParseRefused)
            Accepted { value: artifact, diagnostics: _ } =>
              match normalize_with(parse_tree: artifact.tree, source: NormalizeWithIsolatedAllocator, spans: artifact.span_index) {
                Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => roster_census_refused(reason: RefusalNormalizeRefused)
                Accepted { value: scoped, diagnostics: _ } =>
                  let unmet = roster_gate_unmet(sides: sides, gates: gates, candidates: candidates, sites: collect_scoped_module_reference_sites(root: scoped.tree.root, imported: list_map(xs: scoped.tree.import_bindings, f: fn(b) { b.binding })).sites, spans: artifact.span_index, imported: scoped.tree.import_bindings)
                  let outcome = match unmet {
                    Present { value: reason } => RosterRefused { reason: reason }
                    Absent => match roster_sweep_rows(sides: sides, 
                      parse_root: artifact.tree,
                      spans: artifact.span_index,
                      normalized_root: scoped.tree.root,
                      imported: scoped.tree.import_bindings,
                      candidates: candidates,
                      closures: closures,
                      gates: gates,
                    ) {
                      RosterClean => roster_label_outcome(sides: sides, text: text, gates: gates, parse_root: artifact.tree, spans: artifact.span_index, normalized_root: scoped.tree.root, imported: scoped.tree.import_bindings, candidates: candidates)
                      other => other
                    }
                  }
                  let converged = match outcome {
                    RosterClean => roster_companion_outcome(companions: companions, parse_root: artifact.tree, spans: artifact.span_index, normalized_root: scoped.tree.root, imported: scoped.tree.import_bindings, homes: candidates)
                    other => other
                  }
                  RosterCensusRead { outcome: converged, heads: roster_census_heads(parse_root: artifact.tree, call: census_call) }
              }
          }
  }
}

// THE FREE HEADS OF ONE ROW: the parse tree's primary heads spelled `call` whose joined reference site is free. The one head
// selection the label plan and the rename plan share (the rename plan's own count-only selection was a second path beside the offset
// join, and is deleted): a head or site that cannot be placed, or a free site off a value position, makes the module ambiguous.
type RosterFreeHeads
  = FreeHeads { heads: List<Node> }
  | FreeHeadsAmbiguous

fn roster_free_heads(sides: List<RosterHomeSide>, parse_root: Node, spans: SpanIndex, normalized_root: Node, imported: List<AliasBindingRow>, row: RosterHeadRow, gates: List<RosterSiteGate>) -> RosterFreeHeads {
  let gate = roster_gate_for(gates: gates, row: row)
  let sites = collect_scoped_module_reference_sites(
    root: normalized_root,
    imported: list_map(xs: imported, f: fn(b) { b.binding })
  ).sites
  let imported_from_home = roster_symbol_imported(imported: imported, row: row)
  let free_off_value = fold_list(xs: sites, empty: 0, cons: fn(n, st) {
    if roster_spelling_is(qn: st.site.spelling, call: row.call) {
      match st.position {
        ValuePosition => n
        _ => if roster_site_is_free(sides: sides, site: st, row: row, imported_from_home: imported_from_home) { n + 1 } else { n }
      }
    } else {
      n
    }
  })
  // THE JOIN IS ON IDENTITY, NOT ORDER (DESIGN section 5): each value-position site is placed by the source offset its occurrence
  // records, each parse head by the offset of its own node, and a head is paired with the site that starts at the same byte.
  // A site or head with no recorded offset, an offset two sites share, or a head no site starts at REFUSES the module.
  let value_sites = roster_value_sites(sites: sites, call: row.call)
  let all_heads = roster_primary_heads(parse_root: parse_root, call: row.call)
  let site_starts = roster_site_starts(sites: value_sites, spans: spans)
  let head_starts = list_map(xs: all_heads, f: fn(h) { roster_node_start(node: h, spans: spans) })
  let unplaced = roster_absent_count(xs: site_starts) + roster_absent_count(xs: head_starts)
  let joined = list_map(xs: all_heads, f: fn(h) {
    roster_sites_starting_at(sites: value_sites, starts: site_starts, at: roster_node_start(node: h, spans: spans))
  })
  let well_joined = for_all(xs: joined, predicate: fn(m) { length(xs: m) == 1 })
  if free_off_value != 0 || unplaced != 0 || length(xs: all_heads) != length(xs: value_sites) || !well_joined {
    FreeHeadsAmbiguous
  } else {
    FreeHeads { heads: fold_list(xs: zip_map(a: all_heads, b: joined, f: fn(h, m) {
      if fold_list(xs: m, empty: false, cons: fn(acc2, st) { roster_site_is_free(sides: sides, site: st, row: row, imported_from_home: imported_from_home) && roster_gate_allows_site(gate: gate, st: st, spans: spans) }) { [h] } else { [] }
    }), empty: [], cons: fn(acc, one) { list_append(left: acc, right: one) }) }
  }
}

// THE LABEL SITES ARE READ FROM RESOLUTION, NOT FROM LEXEMES (review 82002). A label edit is selected only at a call whose
// head is the row's spelling as a FREE name: each parse-tree primary-expression head spelled `call` is JOINED, by the source
// offset of its node, to the reference-site collector's value-position site of that spelling that starts at the same byte
// (ScopedReferenceSite.occurrence, v2.compiler.reference_site_collector), and the edit goes only to heads whose site is free.
// A bound occurrence (a parameter, a local) is joined and left alone. A method or field spelling, a head or site with no
// recorded offset, or a head that does not meet exactly one site cannot be placed, and the file REFUSES with
// label-sites-ambiguous rather than relabelling what it cannot place. The free name is any occurrence no lexical frame binds
// (roster_site_is_free); that it is the row's HOME is decided by roster_symbol_imported, never by the head class.
type RosterLabelPlan
  = LabelsSelected { edits: List<RosterLabelEdit> }
  | LabelsAmbiguous
  | LabelsRenameRefused { reason: RosterRefusalReason }

fn roster_label_plan(sides: List<RosterHomeSide>, gates: List<RosterSiteGate>, 
  parse_root: Node,
  spans: SpanIndex,
  normalized_root: Node,
  imported: List<AliasBindingRow>,
  row: RosterHeadRow,
  rename: RosterLabelRename
) -> RosterLabelPlan {
  match roster_free_heads(sides: sides, parse_root: parse_root, spans: spans, normalized_root: normalized_root, imported: imported, row: row, gates: gates) {
    FreeHeadsAmbiguous => LabelsAmbiguous
    FreeHeads { heads: heads } =>
    fold_list(xs: heads, empty: LabelsSelected { edits: [] }, cons: fn(acc, head) {
      match acc {
        LabelsAmbiguous => LabelsAmbiguous
        LabelsRenameRefused { reason: rr } => LabelsRenameRefused { reason: rr }
        LabelsSelected { edits: es } =>
          fold_list(xs: dag_call_direct_arg_slots(node: head), empty: LabelsSelected { edits: es }, cons: fn(inner, slot) {
            match inner {
              LabelsAmbiguous => LabelsAmbiguous
              LabelsRenameRefused { reason: rr } => LabelsRenameRefused { reason: rr }
              LabelsSelected { edits: es2 } =>
                // An argument whose capture does not read could be the label this row renames; it is never skipped.
                match slot {
                  Absent => LabelsAmbiguous
                  Present { value: arg } =>
                match dag_named_arg_name_node_optional(arg_capture: arg) {
                  Absent => inner
                  Present { value: name_node } =>
                    match node_atom_identity_optional(node: name_node) {
                      Present { value: label } =>
                        if symbol_lexeme(sym: label) == rename.from {
                          match roster_node_byte_range(node: name_node, spans: spans) {
                            Present { value: r } => LabelsSelected { edits: list_snoc_item(xs: es2, item: RosterLabelEdit { start: r.start, end: r.end, from: rename.from, to: rename.to, relocation: Absent }) }
                            Absent => LabelsAmbiguous
                          }
                        } else {
                          inner
                        }
                      Absent => inner
                    }
                }
                }
            }
          })
      }
    })
  }
}

// THE ONE FREE-NAME CLASSIFIER, used by the import count (roster_sites_count) and the label plan alike (review 82014).
// THE ROSTER ASKS THE QUESTION ACQUISITION DOES NOT: "would emitting an import (or relabelling) for this name be
// WRONG?" That needs the POSITION and the home's declared KIND as well as the binding, which is why it takes the site
// and the row and not the head (tidy-ant-251's D3 ruling; v2.compiler.module_acquisition reads the binding alone).
//
// THE POSITION AXIS (this PR, from the site as issued by v2.compiler.occurrence_role reference_position_step):
//   Label, PatternTag       => NEVER free. A mention at an argument label or a pattern tag is not a name any value
//                              frame explains, so there is nothing to import or relabel.
//   Value                   => the binding fact alone, exactly as before this PR: unbound is free, and an imported
//                              head is free only when the import comes from the home the row claims. That keeps an
//                              imported qualified tag (Choice.Yes under ConstructTagEdge with Choice imported) out of
//                              the rows, where v2.compiler.module_acquisition keeps the same head a non-candidate --
//                              one site, one reading per question, no widening.
//   TypeAnnotation, Return  => the KIND AXIS decides, per tidy-ant-251's roster correction (msg_66a5409b): a site
//                              needs the home's import when its position is compatible with the KIND the home
//                              declaration declares. Wave 2's homes are TYPE homes (std.types List/Map/Set) used
//                              precisely in these positions, so a position-only rule would import nothing for them;
//                              Wave 1's chars is a VALUE home, so `chars: List` in an annotation must import nothing.
//                              The kind is read from the home's declaration identity by
//                              v2.workflow.roster_home_kind position_matches_home_kind (v2.std.decl_index's keyed
//                              read), never from the spelling; this module decides nothing about positions or kinds.
//
// THE DECLARATION QUESTION IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT. v2.compiler.occurrence_role's index does not key the
// atoms the normalized tree carries (measured; recorded in the recurring-failure-mode row
// a_roster_sweep_counts_a_bound_or_label_spelling_as_an_unbound_call), so a role conjunct here would be a
// gate that never fires -- a decoration. The let-binder cell is settled at the collector instead: a `let`'s declaring
// occurrence is not a site (v2.compiler.lexical_scope child_is_declaring_occurrence), and its uses read HeadBoundInFrame.
fn roster_site_is_free(sides: List<RosterHomeSide>, site: ScopedReferenceSite, row: RosterHeadRow, imported_from_home: Bool) -> Bool {
  roster_site_needs_home_import(
    site: site,
    side: roster_home_side_of(sides: sides, home: roster_qn_text(qn: row.home), import_name: row.import_name),
    imported_from_home: imported_from_home
  )
}

// The start byte of one occurrence / node, from the span index the parse recorded. Absent when no extent is recorded.
fn roster_site_starts(sites: List<ScopedReferenceSite>, spans: SpanIndex) -> List<Int?> {
  list_map(xs: sites, f: fn(st) { roster_identity_start(identity: st.occurrence, spans: spans) })
}

// THE GATE, one per scoped file run: a scope carries per-LEG selections, so the run carries at most one gate per leg
// (a wave of two OnlyOccurrences legs carries two gates, on two homes of possibly ONE call). An ungated run carries the
// empty list, which admits every site (the behavior every existing wave and control sees). The gate carries the home it
// belongs to -- with ONE spelling split across TWO homes the call alone cannot name the row -- plus the file's path and
// line starts, so a site's census key is derived once per run from the SAME offsets the plans act on; no plan re-reads
// the census.
type RosterSiteGate {
  home: String
  row_key: String
  call: String
  keys: List<String>
  path: String
  starts: List<Int>
}

// THE ROW'S GATE: the gate whose home AND row key name this row, or Absent (an ungated row admits every site). With two legs over one call
// (to_string over std.integer and over std.nat) the call alone would let either leg's keys admit the other row's sites;
// the home is what makes each row answer to ITS keys only.
fn roster_gate_for(gates: List<RosterSiteGate>, row: RosterHeadRow) -> Optional<RosterSiteGate> {
  fold_list(xs: gates, empty: Absent, cons: fn(acc, g) {
    match acc {
      Present { value: _ } => acc
      Absent => if g.home == roster_qn_text(qn: row.home) && g.row_key == row.key { Present { value: g } } else { Absent }
    }
  })
}

// The gates the run's scope carries: one per OnlyOccurrences leg, none for EveryRowOfHome/OnlyCall legs and none for
// AllHomes. The keys are the census location column `<file>:<line>:<byte column>` (1-based line, 1-based BYTE column),
// rendered by the SAME convention the admission join uses at
// dag/gunbc/instruments/namespace_wave_occurrence_join.dag locus_at, over the byte-split line starts of the same text.
fn roster_scope_gates(scope: RosterHomeScope, path: String, text: String) -> List<RosterSiteGate> {
  match scope {
    AllHomes => []
    OneHome { home: h, rows: sel } => roster_leg_gates(home: h, rows: sel, path: path, text: text)
  }
}

fn roster_leg_gates(home: QualifiedName, rows: RosterRowSelection, path: String, text: String) -> List<RosterSiteGate> {
  match rows {
    OnlyOccurrences { row: k, call: c, occurrences: os } => [RosterSiteGate { home: roster_qn_text(qn: home), row_key: k, call: c, keys: os, path: path, starts: line_starts(text: text) }]
    EveryRowOfHome => []
    OnlyCall { call: _ } => []
  }
}

// THE PER-SITE GATE. A gated site passes iff its head start -- the minted occurrence offset, resolved through the same
// SpanIndex the plans edit from -- renders to a key naming this file. Sites of another spelling pass untouched: the
// gate belongs to one row's call, and the scope already admits one home. An ungated run admits every site.
// There is NO FALLBACK TO SPELLING: in an active run, a site of the gated call passes ONLY if a key of the selection
// names this file and matches the site's derived key. A file the selection names no key of has the gated row ACT AS
// ABSENT there (its gated-call sites allow nothing: no import, no rename) -- it is never swept by spelling.
fn roster_gate_allows_site(gate: Optional<RosterSiteGate>, st: ScopedReferenceSite, spans: SpanIndex) -> Bool {
  match gate {
    Absent => true
    Present { value: g } =>
      !roster_spelling_is(qn: st.site.spelling, call: g.call) ||
        roster_key_matches_site(keys: roster_keys_for_path(keys: g.keys, path: g.path), key: roster_site_key(st: st, spans: spans, path: g.path, starts: g.starts))
  }
}

// EVERY KEY MUST MEET A SITE. A key naming this file that meets no value-position site of the gated call -- free or
// bound -- is a stale census (the file moved since the census was read) or a typo, and REFUSES the run: never a silent
// narrowing, and never a fallback to sweeping the spelling (manager ruling, NAMESPACE-XL to_string wave: "if a row
// does not match, refuse it and list it, never fall back to spelling"). A key the file does not name belongs to another
// path's sweep; the per-file path list is already base-receipt-governed (wave_runs_base_census + base_selection_refusal).
//
// THE RE-CHECK RUNS ON THE UNCONVERTED FILE ONLY (already_imported). A convergence re-run sees the sweep's OWN output:
// pass 1 renamed the keyed heads and landed the home's import, so the census loci have shifted by every edit before
// them and re-testing the keys against converted text would false-refuse a CONVERGED file. Once the gated row's import
// is visible the file has been through the gate; a typo or drift in THAT state cannot silently narrow either -- it
// leaves an unconverted keyed site, and the wave's census NEW-0 gate is red on it -- while the admission instrument
// recomputes the plan from the scope over the same text and must byte-equal what landed. The net is the wave's, not
// this fold's; the fold stays the pre-conversion tripwire.
// EVERY ACTIVE GATE RE-CHECKS ITS OWN KEYS against the file's sites, skipped once ITS OWN row's import is visible (the
// post-conversion rule; see roster_gate_keys_all_met). With two gates of one call (std.integer and std.nat to_string),
// each gate tests only ITS keys, and the skip is per row: a file that already imports std.integer but not std.nat is
// still gated on the nat keys.
fn roster_gate_unmet(sides: List<RosterHomeSide>, gates: List<RosterSiteGate>, candidates: List<RosterHeadRow>, sites: FreeMonoid<ScopedReferenceSite>, spans: SpanIndex, imported: List<AliasBindingRow>) -> Optional<RosterRefusalReason> {
  fold_list(xs: gates, empty: Absent, cons: fn(acc, g) {
    match acc {
      Present { value: r } => Present { value: r }
      Absent =>
        let gated = fold_list(xs: candidates, empty: [], cons: fn(hit, row) {
          if row.key == g.row_key && roster_qn_text(qn: row.home) == g.home { list_snoc_item(xs: hit, item: row) } else { hit }
        })
        let row_imported = fold_list(xs: gated, empty: false, cons: fn(hit, row) { hit || roster_symbol_imported(imported: imported, row: row) })
        // A KEY IS MET ONLY BY A SITE THE ROW WOULD EDIT: a free value-position site of the call (roster_free_heads' own test),
        // never a bound one -- a key on a parameter or local spelled like the call would otherwise pass and edit nothing.
        let editable = fold_list(xs: gated, empty: [], cons: fn(acc, row) {
          let imported_from_home = roster_symbol_imported(imported: imported, row: row)
          fold_list(xs: sites, empty: acc, cons: fn(acc2, st) {
            if roster_site_is_value_position(st: st) && roster_site_is_free(sides: sides, site: st, row: row, imported_from_home: imported_from_home) { list_snoc_item(xs: acc2, item: st) } else { acc2 }
          })
        })
        roster_gate_keys_all_met(gate: g, sites: editable, spans: spans, already_imported: row_imported)
    }
  })
}

fn roster_site_is_value_position(st: ScopedReferenceSite) -> Bool {
  match st.position {
    ValuePosition => true
    _ => false
  }
}

fn roster_gate_keys_all_met(gate: RosterSiteGate, sites: FreeMonoid<ScopedReferenceSite>, spans: SpanIndex, already_imported: Bool) -> Optional<RosterRefusalReason> {
  if already_imported {
    Absent
  } else {
    match roster_first_unmet_key(keys: roster_keys_for_path(keys: gate.keys, path: gate.path), sites: sites, gate: gate, spans: spans) {
      Present { value: k } => Present { value: RefusalOccurrenceKeyUnmatched { path: gate.path, call: gate.call, key: k } }
      Absent => Absent
    }
  }
}

// THE SITE KEYS ARE DERIVED ONCE PER FILE, not once per key-site pair: the keys of the gated call's sites are collected
// in one fold (each rendering its locus over the line starts ONCE), and a key is met by membership in that list. The
// first draft re-rendered every site's key for every key, a quadratic-in-keys scan over the whole line-start fold.
fn roster_first_unmet_key(keys: List<String>, sites: FreeMonoid<ScopedReferenceSite>, gate: RosterSiteGate, spans: SpanIndex) -> Optional<String> {
  let met = fold_list(xs: sites, empty: [], cons: fn(acc, st) {
    if roster_spelling_is(qn: st.site.spelling, call: gate.call) {
      list_snoc_item(xs: acc, item: roster_site_key(st: st, spans: spans, path: gate.path, starts: gate.starts))
    } else {
      acc
    }
  })
  fold_list(
    xs: keys,
    empty: Absent,
    cons: fn(acc, k) {
      match acc {
        Present { value: r } => Present { value: r }
        Absent =>
          if for_all(xs: met, predicate: fn(m) { m != k }) {
            Present { value: k }
          } else {
            Absent
          }
      }
    }
  )
}

// THE CENSUS LOCATION KEY of a site: `<path>:<line>:<byte column>` of its head start, both 1-based, from the site's own
// minted occurrence offset (identity, never a re-lex of the text) rendered over the byte-split line starts.
fn roster_site_key(st: ScopedReferenceSite, spans: SpanIndex, path: String, starts: List<Int>) -> String {
  path + ":" + roster_locus_at(starts: starts, offset: roster_identity_start(identity: st.occurrence, spans: spans))
}

// `<line>:<byte column>` for a head-start offset; "-" when the offset is absent.
fn roster_locus_at(starts: List<Int>, offset: Optional<Int>) -> String {
  match offset {
    Absent => "-"
    Present { value: o } => locus_at(starts: starts, offset: o)
  }
}

// The keys of a selection that name THIS file: the text before the first `:` is the file (a repo path carries no colon;
// the census location column is exactly file:line:column).
fn roster_keys_for_path(keys: List<String>, path: String) -> List<String> {
  fold_list(xs: keys, empty: [], cons: fn(acc, k) {
    if roster_key_file(key: k) == path { list_snoc_item(xs: acc, item: k) } else { acc }
  })
}

fn roster_key_file(key: String) -> String {
  match split(s: key, delimiter: ":") {
    Empty => ""
    Cons { head: h, tail: _ } => h
  }
}

fn roster_key_matches_site(keys: List<String>, key: String) -> Bool {
  fold_list(xs: keys, empty: false, cons: fn(found, k) { found || k == key })
}

fn roster_value_sites(sites: List<ScopedReferenceSite>, call: String) -> List<ScopedReferenceSite> {
  fold_list(xs: sites, empty: [], cons: fn(acc, st) {
    if roster_spelling_is(qn: st.site.spelling, call: call) {
      match st.position {
        ValuePosition => list_snoc_item(xs: acc, item: st)
        _ => acc
      }
    } else {
      acc
    }
  })
}

fn roster_identity_start(identity: NodeOccurrenceIdentity, spans: SpanIndex) -> Int? {
  match roster_identity_byte_range(identity: identity, spans: spans) {
    Present { value: r } => Present { value: r.start }
    Absent => Absent
  }
}

fn roster_node_start(node: Node, spans: SpanIndex) -> Int? {
  match roster_node_byte_range(node: node, spans: spans) {
    Present { value: r } => Present { value: r.start }
    Absent => Absent
  }
}

fn roster_absent_count(xs: List<Int?>) -> Int {
  fold_list(xs: xs, empty: 0, cons: fn(n, o) {
    match o {
      Present { value: _ } => n
      Absent => n + 1
    }
  })
}

fn roster_site_if_start(site: ScopedReferenceSite, got: Int?, want: Int) -> List<ScopedReferenceSite> {
  match got {
    Present { value: g } => if g == want { [site] } else { [] }
    Absent => []
  }
}

// The sites whose recorded start is `at`; empty for an unplaced head.
fn roster_sites_starting_at(sites: List<ScopedReferenceSite>, starts: List<Int?>, at: Int?) -> List<ScopedReferenceSite> {
  match at {
    Absent => []
    Present { value: want } =>
      fold_list(xs: zip_map(a: sites, b: starts, f: fn(st, o) { roster_site_if_start(site: st, got: o, want: want) }), empty: [], cons: fn(acc, one) { list_append(left: acc, right: one) })
  }
}

// Every primary-expression capture whose head (the sequence's left atom) is spelled `call`: a bare `call(...)` or a bare
// `call` reference. A method or field spelling sits in a postfix suffix, not at a primary-expression head.
fn roster_primary_heads(parse_root: Node, call: String) -> List<Node> {
  fold_list(xs: node_subtree_nodes(root: parse_root), empty: [], cons: fn(acc, n) {
    match parse_production_emitted_identity_optional(node: n) {
      Present { value: id } =>
        if id == ^dag_surface_primary_expr {
          match parse_production_captured_child_optional(node: n) {
            Present { value: cap } =>
              match find_named_child(root: cap, name: ^grammar_sequence_left_node_projection) {
                Accepted { value: left, diagnostics: _ } =>
                  match node_atom_identity_optional(node: left) {
                    Present { value: sym } => if symbol_lexeme(sym: sym) == call { list_snoc_item(xs: acc, item: cap) } else { acc }
                    Absent => acc
                  }
                Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => acc
              }
            Absent => acc
          }
        } else {
          acc
        }
      Absent => acc
    }
  })
}

// THE LABEL PLAN OF A SET OF ROWS: every rename of every row, in one fold. The pipe sites of the parse are indexed ONCE
// here (the fold's shared value): a head's pipe read is a map lookup, never a subtree walk.
fn roster_rows_label_plan(sides: List<RosterHomeSide>, 
  text: Optional<String>,
  gates: List<RosterSiteGate>, 
  parse_root: Node,
  spans: SpanIndex,
  normalized_root: Node,
  imported: List<AliasBindingRow>,
  rows: List<RosterHeadRow>
) -> RosterLabelPlan {
  let pipe_index = roster_pipe_index(parse_root: parse_root, spans: spans)
  let planned = fold_list(xs: rows, empty: LabelsSelected { edits: [] }, cons: fn(acc, row) {
    match acc {
      LabelsAmbiguous => LabelsAmbiguous
      LabelsRenameRefused { reason: rr } => LabelsRenameRefused { reason: rr }
      LabelsSelected { edits: es } =>
        match row.head {
          KeepHead => roster_row_label_edits(sides: sides, gates: gates, parse_root: parse_root, spans: spans, normalized_root: normalized_root, imported: imported, row: row, edits: es)
          RenameHead { to: to, positional: positional } =>
            match roster_row_label_edits(sides: sides, gates: gates, parse_root: parse_root, spans: spans, normalized_root: normalized_root, imported: imported, row: row, edits: es) {
              LabelsSelected { edits: es3 } =>
                match roster_rename_plan(sides: sides, text: text, gates: gates, parse_root: parse_root, pipe_index: pipe_index, spans: spans, normalized_root: normalized_root, imported: imported, row: row, to: to, positional: positional) {
                  LabelsSelected { edits: more } => LabelsSelected { edits: list_append(left: es3, right: more) }
                  LabelsAmbiguous => LabelsAmbiguous
                  other => other
                }
              LabelsAmbiguous => LabelsAmbiguous
              other => other
            }
        }
    }
  })
  // THE SPLICE NEEDS ITS EDITS IN SOURCE ORDER (roster_label_splices applies them last-first). A rename's head edit and
  // its argument insertions, and a call nested in another's argument, are planned call by call, so the plan is put in
  // byte order once here. At one byte, a zero-width insertion sorts before the replacement starting there: applied
  // last-first, the replacement lands first and the label is then inserted in front of it.
  // The sorted plan must then be pairwise disjoint (roster_label_edits_disjoint), or it refuses: the order alone does not
  // make two edits of the same bytes safe.
  match planned {
    LabelsSelected { edits: es } => roster_sorted_disjoint_plan(sorted: list_sort_by_key(xs: es, key: roster_label_edit_order_key, order: int_total_order()))
    other => other
  }
}

fn roster_sorted_disjoint_plan(sorted: List<RosterLabelEdit>) -> RosterLabelPlan {
  match roster_label_edits_disjoint(edits: roster_expand_relocations(edits: sorted)) {
    LabelsSelected { edits: _ } => LabelsSelected { edits: sorted }
    other => other
  }
}

// THE DISJOINT-EDIT INVARIANT over a plan in source order. `reach` is the furthest end of any replacement already
// scanned, so an edit starting before it lies inside that replacement; `insert_at` is the last zero-width insertion's
// offset, so a second insertion there coincides. A zero-width insertion at a replacement's start (sorted before it) and
// any edit starting exactly at an earlier one's end are disjoint and pass.
type RosterEditScan {
  reach: Int
  insert_at: Optional<Int>
  refused: Optional<RosterRefusalReason>
}

fn roster_label_edits_disjoint(edits: List<RosterLabelEdit>) -> RosterLabelPlan {
  let scan = fold_list(xs: edits, empty: RosterEditScan { reach: 0, insert_at: Absent, refused: Absent }, cons: fn(acc, e) {
    match acc.refused {
      Present { value: _ } => acc
      Absent =>
        if e.start < acc.reach {
          RosterEditScan { reach: acc.reach, insert_at: acc.insert_at, refused: Present { value: RefusalEditsOverlap { start: e.start, end: e.end, reach: acc.reach } } }
        } else if e.start == e.end {
          match acc.insert_at {
            Present { value: at } =>
              if at == e.start {
                RosterEditScan { reach: acc.reach, insert_at: acc.insert_at, refused: Present { value: RefusalEditsCoincide { at: e.start } } }
              } else {
                RosterEditScan { reach: acc.reach, insert_at: Present { value: e.start }, refused: Absent }
              }
            Absent => RosterEditScan { reach: acc.reach, insert_at: Present { value: e.start }, refused: Absent }
          }
        } else {
          RosterEditScan { reach: e.end, insert_at: acc.insert_at, refused: Absent }
        }
    }
  })
  match scan.refused {
    Present { value: r } => LabelsRenameRefused { reason: r }
    Absent => LabelsSelected { edits: edits }
  }
}

fn roster_label_edit_order_key(e: RosterLabelEdit) -> Int {
  if e.start == e.end { e.start * 2 } else { e.start * 2 + 1 }
}

// ONE ROW'S LABEL RENAMES appended to `edits`; a row with no label renames returns `edits` unchanged.
fn roster_row_label_edits(sides: List<RosterHomeSide>, gates: List<RosterSiteGate>, parse_root: Node, spans: SpanIndex, normalized_root: Node, imported: List<AliasBindingRow>, row: RosterHeadRow, edits: List<RosterLabelEdit>) -> RosterLabelPlan {
  fold_list(xs: row.labels, empty: LabelsSelected { edits: edits }, cons: fn(inner, rename) {
    match inner {
      LabelsAmbiguous => LabelsAmbiguous
      LabelsRenameRefused { reason: rr } => LabelsRenameRefused { reason: rr }
      LabelsSelected { edits: es2 } =>
        match roster_label_plan(sides: sides, gates: gates, parse_root: parse_root, spans: spans, normalized_root: normalized_root, imported: imported, row: row, rename: rename) {
          LabelsAmbiguous => LabelsAmbiguous
          LabelsRenameRefused { reason: rr } => LabelsRenameRefused { reason: rr }
          LabelsSelected { edits: more } => LabelsSelected { edits: list_append(left: es2, right: more) }
        }
    }
  })
}

// THE RENAME PLAN OF ONE RenameHead ROW. The calls it rewrites are exactly the ones the label plan would relabel: the
// parse tree's primary heads spelled `call`, which must agree in number with the reference-site collector's FREE sites of
// that spelling (roster_site_is_free -- the one classifier, so a head bound by a parameter, a local, a module-level
// declaration or an import of another `call` is never a candidate, and a disagreement refuses label-sites-ambiguous).
// Each selected call gets one replacement of its head atom (`call` to `to`, checked byte-for-byte again at apply) and one
// zero-width insertion of `<label>: ` before each positional argument, in the row's declared order.
fn roster_rename_plan(
  sides: List<RosterHomeSide>,
  text: Optional<String>,
  gates: List<RosterSiteGate>,
  parse_root: Node,
  pipe_index: Map<Int, List<RosterPipeSite>>,
  spans: SpanIndex,
  normalized_root: Node,
  imported: List<AliasBindingRow>,
  row: RosterHeadRow,
  to: String,
  positional: List<String>
) -> RosterLabelPlan {
  match roster_free_heads(sides: sides, parse_root: parse_root, spans: spans, normalized_root: normalized_root, imported: imported, row: row, gates: gates) {
    FreeHeadsAmbiguous => LabelsAmbiguous
    FreeHeads { heads: heads } =>
    // INNERMOST FIRST: a pipe whose left operand holds another of this row's selected calls waits for the next pass, after
    // the inner call is rewritten (a chain `a |> f() |> join(s)` converges stage by stage). The pipe read rides the selection
    // into the rename fold below, so each head is read off the index once, not once per pass over the head.
    fold_list(xs: roster_heads_innermost_first(pipe_index: pipe_index, spans: spans, heads: heads), empty: LabelsSelected { edits: [] }, cons: fn(acc, selected) {
      match acc {
        LabelsSelected { edits: es } =>
          match roster_rename_call_edits(text: text, selected: selected, spans: spans, row: row, to: to, positional: positional) {
            LabelsSelected { edits: more } => LabelsSelected { edits: list_append(left: es, right: more) }
            LabelsAmbiguous => LabelsAmbiguous
            other => other
          }
        LabelsAmbiguous => LabelsAmbiguous
        other => other
      }
    })
  }
}

// A PIPE SITE (`lhs |> call(args)`) is the same rename with the pipe's left operand as positional slot 0: arity counts it, a
// named argument still refuses with the existing causes, and the site becomes `to(label0: <lhs>, label1: <arg1>, ...)` through
// the edits of roster_rename_pipe_edit, no operand or argument byte moved (a nested or multi-line operand stays intact). A declared home cannot keep the pipe (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode
// pipe_into_a_declared_function_resolves_as_a_method). A pipe whose right operand is more than the call refuses typed.
fn roster_rename_call_edits(text: Optional<String>, selected: RosterSelectedHead, spans: SpanIndex, row: RosterHeadRow, to: String, positional: List<String>) -> RosterLabelPlan {
  let head = selected.head
  match selected.read {
    NotPiped => roster_rename_direct_call_edits(head: head, spans: spans, row: row, to: to, positional: positional)
    PipeOperandUnclean => LabelsRenameRefused { reason: RefusalRenamePipeOperandUnclean { call: row.call } }
    PipedFrom { left: lr, call: cr } =>
      // Arity and labels are read without the text, so the import pass refuses a bad pipe site exactly as the label pass
      // would; only the edit itself waits for the text.
      match roster_pipe_site_refusal(head: head, row: row, positional: positional) {
        Present { value: r } => LabelsRenameRefused { reason: r }
        Absent =>
          match text {
            Absent => LabelsSelected { edits: [] }
            Present { value: t } => roster_rename_pipe_edit(text: t, head: head, spans: spans, row: row, to: to, positional: positional, left: lr, call: cr)
          }
      }
  }
}

fn roster_pipe_site_refusal(head: Node, row: RosterHeadRow, positional: List<String>) -> Optional<RosterRefusalReason> {
  let slots = dag_call_direct_arg_slots(node: head)
  if length(xs: slots) + 1 != length(xs: positional) {
    Present { value: RefusalRenameCallArity { call: row.call } }
  } else {
    fold_list(xs: roster_zip_slots(slots: slots, labels: roster_drop_first(xs: positional)), empty: Absent, cons: fn(acc, pair) { roster_pipe_label_refusal(acc: acc, pair: pair, call: row.call) })
  }
}

fn roster_pipe_label_refusal(acc: Optional<RosterRefusalReason>, pair: RosterSlotLabel, call: String) -> Optional<RosterRefusalReason> {
  match acc {
    Present { value: r } => Present { value: r }
    Absent =>
      match pair.slot {
        Absent => Absent
        Present { value: arg } =>
          if roster_arg_is_named(arg: arg) && !roster_named_arg_label_is(arg: arg, label: pair.label) { Present { value: RefusalRenameCallNamedArgument { call: call } } } else { Absent }
      }
  }
}

// THE PIPE AS STEPS, NO OPERAND MOVED (tidy-ant-251's ruling for #15101): `lhs |> call(a1, ..)` becomes an INSERT of
// `to(label0: ` at the left operand's start, a REPLACE of the span from the operand's end to the first remaining argument's
// start (` |> call(`) by `, label1: ` (or by nothing when the call has no remaining argument), and the ordinary label
// inserts before each later positional argument. Every operand and argument byte stays where it was and only shifts, so a
// reader that joins occurrences across the edit (#15083) maps the operand by offset and the head by its rename.
fn roster_rename_pipe_edit(text: String, head: Node, spans: SpanIndex, row: RosterHeadRow, to: String, positional: List<String>, left: RosterByteRange, call: RosterByteRange) -> RosterLabelPlan {
  let slots = dag_call_direct_arg_slots(node: head)
  let label0 = roster_field_or_empty(xs: positional, index: 0)
  match find_named_child(root: head, name: ^grammar_sequence_left_node_projection) {
    Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => LabelsAmbiguous
    Accepted { value: atom, diagnostics: _ } =>
      match roster_node_byte_range(node: atom, spans: spans) {
        Absent => LabelsAmbiguous
        Present { value: hr } =>
          match roster_text_between(text: text, start: left.end, end: hr.start) {
            Absent => LabelsAmbiguous
            Present { value: connector } =>
              match roster_text_between(text: text, start: hr.end, end: hr.end + 1) {
                Absent => LabelsAmbiguous
                Present { value: paren } =>
                  if paren != "(" {
                    LabelsAmbiguous
                  } else {
                    let relocation = RosterLabelEdit { start: hr.start, end: hr.end, from: row.call, to: "", relocation: Present { value: RosterHeadRelocation { insert_at: left.start, to: to, suffix: "(" + label0 + ": " } } }
                    let drop_connector = RosterLabelEdit { start: left.end, end: hr.start, from: connector, to: "", relocation: Absent }
                    match list_head(xs: slots) {
                      // `lhs |> call()`: the head's `(` goes, its `)` closes the rewritten call.
                      Absent => LabelsSelected { edits: [relocation, drop_connector, RosterLabelEdit { start: hr.end, end: hr.end + 1, from: "(", to: "", relocation: Absent }] }
                      Present { value: first_slot } =>
                        match first_slot {
                          Absent => LabelsAmbiguous
                          Present { value: first_arg } =>
                            let label1 = roster_field_or_empty(xs: positional, index: 1)
                            // An argument the author already labelled with the row's label keeps its label.
                            let joiner = if roster_arg_is_named(arg: first_arg) { ", " } else { ", " + label1 + ": " }
                            fold_list(
                              xs: roster_drop_first_slot_labels(pairs: roster_zip_slots(slots: slots, labels: roster_drop_first(xs: positional))),
                              empty: LabelsSelected { edits: [relocation, drop_connector, RosterLabelEdit { start: hr.end, end: hr.end + 1, from: "(", to: joiner, relocation: Absent }] },
                              cons: fn(acc, pair) {
                                match acc {
                                  LabelsSelected { edits: es } => roster_positional_label_edit(edits: es, pair: pair, spans: spans, call: row.call)
                                  other => other
                                }
                              }
                            )
                        }
                    }
                  }
              }
          }
      }
  }
}

fn roster_drop_first_slot_labels(pairs: List<RosterSlotLabel>) -> List<RosterSlotLabel> {
  match pairs {
    Empty => pairs
    Cons { head: _, tail: t } => t
  }
}

fn roster_field_or_empty(xs: List<String>, index: Int) -> String {
  match list_at_optional(xs: xs, index: index) {
    Present { value: t } => t
    Absent => ""
  }
}

fn roster_drop_first(xs: List<String>) -> List<String> {
  match xs {
    Empty => xs
    Cons { head: _, tail: t } => t
  }
}

fn roster_arg_is_named(arg: Node) -> Bool {
  match dag_named_arg_value_optional(arg_capture: arg) {
    Present { value: _ } => true
    Absent => false
  }
}

fn roster_named_arg_label_is(arg: Node, label: String) -> Bool {
  match dag_named_arg_name_node_optional(arg_capture: arg) {
    Absent => false
    Present { value: name_node } =>
      match node_atom_identity_optional(node: name_node) {
        Present { value: sym } => symbol_lexeme(sym: sym) == label
        Absent => false
      }
  }
}

// WHERE A CALL HEAD SITS RELATIVE TO A PIPE, read off the parse tree's binary infix nodes (the operator at
// grammar_infix_operator_node_projection, operands at its left/right projections). PipedFrom: some `|>` infix node's right
// operand is exactly the call (same byte extent), and its left operand is the pipe's input. PipeOperandUnclean: a `|>` right
// operand STARTS at the call but extends past it (`lhs |> call(..) + x`), so the call is not the pipe's target. Otherwise
// NotPiped.
type RosterPipeRead
  = NotPiped
  | PipedFrom { left: RosterByteRange, call: RosterByteRange }
  | PipeOperandUnclean

// ONE `|>` INFIX NODE'S RELEVANT GEOMETRY: its right operand's extent (the key) and its left operand's extent, Absent
// when the left cannot be placed (the same condition the fold read as PipeOperandUnclean).
type RosterPipeSite {
  left: Optional<RosterByteRange>
  right: RosterByteRange
}

// A SELECTED CALL HEAD with its pipe read, carried from the selection fold into the rename fold so the read is computed
// once per head, not once per pass over the head (DESIGN.md §2: share the first value).
type RosterSelectedHead {
  head: Node
  read: RosterPipeRead
}

// THE PIPE SITES OF ONE PARSE, INDEXED ONCE: keyed by the start byte of each `|>` infix node's right operand, the entries
// in tree order so the whole-tree fold's first-match semantics survive a lookup. Built once per file plan (the label pass
// and the import pass, over the same parse); a head is then a lookup, not a subtree walk.
fn roster_pipe_index(parse_root: Node, spans: SpanIndex) -> Map<Int, List<RosterPipeSite>> {
  let empty_index: Map<Int, List<RosterPipeSite>> = empty_map()
  fold_list(xs: node_subtree_nodes(root: parse_root), empty: empty_index, cons: fn(acc, n) {
    match roster_pipe_site_of(node: n, spans: spans) {
      Present { value: s } => roster_pipe_index_snoc(acc: acc, site: s)
      Absent => acc
    }
  })
}

fn roster_pipe_index_snoc(acc: Map<Int, List<RosterPipeSite>>, site: RosterPipeSite) -> Map<Int, List<RosterPipeSite>> {
  let prior = match map_lookup(m: acc, key: site.right.start) {
    Present { value: p } => p
    Absent => []
  }
  map_insert(m: acc, key: site.right.start, value: list_snoc_item(xs: prior, item: site))
}

fn roster_pipe_site_of(node: Node, spans: SpanIndex) -> Optional<RosterPipeSite> {
  match find_named_child(root: node, name: ^grammar_infix_operator_node_projection) {
    Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => Absent
    Accepted { value: op, diagnostics: _ } =>
      if !roster_is_pipe_operator(op: op) {
        Absent
      } else {
        match find_named_child(root: node, name: ^grammar_infix_right_node_projection) {
          Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => Absent
          Accepted { value: right, diagnostics: _ } =>
            match roster_node_byte_range(node: right, spans: spans) {
              Absent => Absent
              Present { value: rr } =>
                match find_named_child(root: node, name: ^grammar_infix_left_node_projection) {
                  Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => Present { value: RosterPipeSite { left: Absent, right: rr } }
                  Accepted { value: left, diagnostics: _ } =>
                    match roster_node_byte_range(node: left, spans: spans) {
                      Absent => Present { value: RosterPipeSite { left: Absent, right: rr } }
                      Present { value: lr } => Present { value: RosterPipeSite { left: Present { value: lr }, right: rr } }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
      }
  }
}

// WHERE A CALL HEAD SITS RELATIVE TO A PIPE, read off the index: the entries at the head's start byte, in tree order,
// first decisive one wins -- exactly what the whole-tree fold returned.
fn roster_pipe_read(index: Map<Int, List<RosterPipeSite>>, spans: SpanIndex, head: Node) -> RosterPipeRead {
  match roster_node_byte_range(node: head, spans: spans) {
    Absent => NotPiped
    Present { value: hr } =>
      match map_lookup(m: index, key: hr.start) {
        Absent => NotPiped
        Present { value: sites } =>
          fold_list(xs: sites, empty: NotPiped, cons: fn(acc, s) {
            match acc {
              NotPiped => roster_pipe_read_against(site: s, call: hr)
              other => other
            }
          })
      }
  }
}

fn roster_pipe_read_against(site: RosterPipeSite, call: RosterByteRange) -> RosterPipeRead {
  if (site.right.start == call.start) && (site.right.end == call.end) {
    match site.left {
      Absent => PipeOperandUnclean
      Present { value: lr } => PipedFrom { left: lr, call: call }
    }
  } else if (site.right.start == call.start) && (site.right.end > call.end) {
    PipeOperandUnclean
  } else {
    NotPiped
  }
}


fn roster_is_pipe_operator(op: Node) -> Bool {
  match node_atom_identity_optional(node: op) {
    Present { value: id } => id == ^dag_token_pipe_gt
    Absent => false
  }
}

fn roster_heads_innermost_first(pipe_index: Map<Int, List<RosterPipeSite>>, spans: SpanIndex, heads: List<Node>) -> List<RosterSelectedHead> {
  let ranges = fold_list(xs: heads, empty: roster_no_ranges(), cons: fn(acc, h) { roster_range_snoc(acc: acc, node: h, spans: spans) })
  fold_list(xs: heads, empty: [], cons: fn(acc, h) {
    let read = roster_pipe_read(index: pipe_index, spans: spans, head: h)
    match read {
      PipedFrom { left: lr, call: _ } => if roster_any_range_within(ranges: ranges, outer: lr) { acc } else { list_snoc_item(xs: acc, item: RosterSelectedHead { head: h, read: read }) }
      _ => list_snoc_item(xs: acc, item: RosterSelectedHead { head: h, read: read })
    }
  })
}

fn roster_no_ranges() -> List<RosterByteRange> { [] }

fn roster_range_snoc(acc: List<RosterByteRange>, node: Node, spans: SpanIndex) -> List<RosterByteRange> {
  match roster_node_byte_range(node: node, spans: spans) {
    Present { value: r } => list_snoc_item(xs: acc, item: r)
    Absent => acc
  }
}

fn roster_any_range_within(ranges: List<RosterByteRange>, outer: RosterByteRange) -> Bool {
  fold_list(xs: ranges, empty: false, cons: fn(found, r) { found || roster_range_within(inner: r, outer: outer) })
}

fn roster_range_within(inner: RosterByteRange, outer: RosterByteRange) -> Bool {
  (outer.start <= inner.start) && (inner.end <= outer.end)
}

// The source text between two BYTE offsets, through the scalar-boundary reading the apply uses, or Absent.
fn roster_text_between(text: String, start: Int, end: Int) -> String? {
  let octets = bytes_octets(b: utf8_encode_bytes(s: text))
  let from = roster_scalar_boundary(octets: octets, byte: start)
  let to = roster_scalar_boundary(octets: octets, byte: end)
  if from < 0 || to < from { Absent } else { Present { value: substring(s: text, start: from, end: to) } }
}

fn roster_rename_direct_call_edits(head: Node, spans: SpanIndex, row: RosterHeadRow, to: String, positional: List<String>) -> RosterLabelPlan {
  match find_named_child(root: head, name: ^grammar_sequence_left_node_projection) {
    Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => LabelsAmbiguous
    Accepted { value: atom, diagnostics: _ } =>
      match roster_node_byte_range(node: atom, spans: spans) {
        Absent => LabelsAmbiguous
        Present { value: r } =>
          let slots = dag_call_direct_arg_slots(node: head)
          if length(xs: slots) != length(xs: positional) {
            LabelsRenameRefused { reason: RefusalRenameCallArity { call: row.call } }
          } else {
            fold_list(
              xs: roster_zip_slots(slots: slots, labels: positional),
              empty: LabelsSelected { edits: [RosterLabelEdit { start: r.start, end: r.end, from: row.call, to: to, relocation: Absent }] },
              cons: fn(acc, pair) {
                match acc {
                  LabelsSelected { edits: es } => roster_positional_label_edit(edits: es, pair: pair, spans: spans, call: row.call)
                  LabelsAmbiguous => LabelsAmbiguous
                  other => other
                }
              }
            )
          }
      }
  }
}

type RosterSlotLabel {
  slot: Optional<Node>
  label: String
}

fn roster_zip_slots(slots: List<Optional<Node>>, labels: List<String>) -> List<RosterSlotLabel> {
  match slots {
    Empty => []
    Cons { head: s, tail: rest } =>
      match labels {
        Empty => []
        Cons { head: l, tail: more } => Cons { head: RosterSlotLabel { slot: s, label: l }, tail: roster_zip_slots(slots: rest, labels: more) }
      }
  }
}

// An argument whose capture does not read, or that is NAMED, is never given a label: the first is a placement the row
// cannot verify, the second a parameter choice the author already made and the row cannot map.
fn roster_positional_label_edit(edits: List<RosterLabelEdit>, pair: RosterSlotLabel, spans: SpanIndex, call: String) -> RosterLabelPlan {
  match pair.slot {
    Absent => LabelsAmbiguous
    Present { value: arg } =>
      match dag_named_arg_value_optional(arg_capture: arg) {
        // THE NAMED-ARGUMENT RULE: a named argument whose label IS the row's label at its position already binds, so it is
        // left as authored; any other label refuses typed. A reordered named argument therefore refuses (its label is not the
        // one at its position): the rewrite never reorders arguments, which would reorder their evaluation.
        Present { value: _ } =>
          if roster_named_arg_label_is(arg: arg, label: pair.label) {
            LabelsSelected { edits: edits }
          } else {
            LabelsRenameRefused { reason: RefusalRenameCallNamedArgument { call: call } }
          }
        Absent =>
          match roster_node_byte_range(node: arg, spans: spans) {
            Absent => LabelsAmbiguous
            Present { value: r } => LabelsSelected { edits: list_snoc_item(xs: edits, item: RosterLabelEdit { start: r.start, end: r.start, from: "", to: pair.label + ": ", relocation: Absent }) }
          }
      }
  }
}

// THE LABEL PASS for a file whose imports are already converged: the in-scope rows whose call is import-visible from their home.
fn roster_label_outcome(sides: List<RosterHomeSide>, 
  text: String,
  gates: List<RosterSiteGate>,
  parse_root: Node,
  spans: SpanIndex,
  normalized_root: Node,
  imported: List<AliasBindingRow>,
  candidates: List<RosterHeadRow>
) -> RosterOutcome {
  let rows = fold_list(xs: candidates, empty: [], cons: fn(acc, row) {
    if roster_symbol_imported(imported: imported, row: row) { list_snoc_item(xs: acc, item: row) } else { acc }
  })
  match roster_rows_label_plan(sides: sides, text: Present { value: text }, gates: gates, parse_root: parse_root, spans: spans, normalized_root: normalized_root, imported: imported, rows: rows) {
    LabelsAmbiguous => RosterRefused { reason: RefusalLabelSitesAmbiguous }
    LabelsRenameRefused { reason: rr } => RosterRefused { reason: rr }
    LabelsSelected { edits: es } => if is_empty(xs: es) { RosterClean } else { RosterLabelEdits { edits: es } }
  }
}

// THE LABELS THE IMPORT EDIT MAKES NECESSARY ride the same outcome: exactly the renames of the rows that edit imports, passed
// in by the import row that rendered it (no home is compared or re-read; reviews 82002 and 82024).
fn roster_with_pending_labels(sides: List<RosterHomeSide>, gates: List<RosterSiteGate>, 
  parse_root: Node,
  spans: SpanIndex,
  normalized_root: Node,
  imported: List<AliasBindingRow>,
  rows: List<RosterHeadRow>,
  edit: RosterOutcome
) -> RosterOutcome {
  // THE IMPORT PASS PLANS NO PIPE SITE (no source text reaches it): a pipe call is rewritten by the label pass that follows
  // the import, so the convergence loop takes it one pass later.
  match roster_rows_label_plan(sides: sides, text: Absent, gates: gates, parse_root: parse_root, spans: spans, normalized_root: normalized_root, imported: imported, rows: rows) {
    LabelsAmbiguous => RosterRefused { reason: RefusalLabelSitesAmbiguous }
    LabelsRenameRefused { reason: rr } => RosterRefused { reason: rr }
    LabelsSelected { edits: labels } =>
      match edit {
        RosterEdit { start: st, end: en, text: tx, own_line: ol } =>
          if is_empty(xs: labels) { edit } else {
            match roster_import_and_labels_disjoint(start: st, end: en, text: tx, labels: labels) {
              Present { value: r } => RosterRefused { reason: r }
              Absent => RosterEditWithLabels { start: st, end: en, text: tx, own_line: ol, labels: labels }
            }
          }
        RosterClean => RosterClean
        other => other
      }
  }
}

// The roster rows whose call head is lexically unbound in this file: the heads ruling B refuses
// natively without an import. HeadLexicallyUnbound is the collector's own classification, so a local
// binding, a module-level declaration or an existing import of the same spelling is never swept.
fn roster_needed_rows(sides: List<RosterHomeSide>, sites: FreeMonoid<ScopedReferenceSite>, imported: List<AliasBindingRow>, candidates: List<RosterHeadRow>, gates: List<RosterSiteGate>, spans: SpanIndex) -> List<RosterHeadRow> {
  fold_list(
    xs: candidates,
    empty: [],
    cons: fn(acc, row) {
      if roster_sites_count(sides: sides, sites: sites, row: row, gates: gates, spans: spans) > 0 && !roster_symbol_imported(imported: imported, row: row) {
        list_snoc_item(xs: acc, item: row)
      } else {
        acc
      }
    }
  )
}

// ANY CANDIDATE SITE THE CENSUS CANNOT DECIDE, located (review 83187). The fold runs over the SAME candidate rows as
// roster_needed_rows -- the scope's rows whose import name is not yet visible -- and over the collector's own sites, so
// it can only fire for a name the sweep is actually asked about; a spelling no row claims (List in the production
// table today) is never a refusal. The decision itself is v2.workflow.roster_home_kind's verdict: KindUnclassified is
// reached only from an unbound head at a value or type position whose home's keyed rows classify nothing. Bound,
// label/tag, and undecided heads cannot reach it, so this refuses NOTHING that the binding fact alone passed before.
fn roster_any_unclassified_head(sides: List<RosterHomeSide>, sites: FreeMonoid<ScopedReferenceSite>, imported: List<AliasBindingRow>, candidates: List<RosterHeadRow>) -> Optional<RosterRefusalReason> {
  fold_list(
    xs: candidates,
    empty: Absent,
    cons: fn(acc, row) {
      match acc {
        Present { value: r } => Present { value: r }
        Absent =>
          if fold_list(xs: sites, empty: false, cons: fn(f, st) {
            f || (roster_spelling_is(qn: st.site.spelling, call: row.call) && roster_site_verdict_is_unclassified(site: st, side: roster_home_side_of(sides: sides, home: roster_qn_text(qn: row.home), import_name: row.import_name), imported_from_home: roster_symbol_imported(imported: imported, row: row)))
          }) {
            Present { value: RefusalHomeKindUnclassified { home: roster_qn_text(qn: row.home), name: row.import_name } }
          } else {
            Absent
          }
      }
    }
  )
}

// The import binds the SHAPE name, not the call spelling, so the collector keeps classifying the bare call as
// unbound after the import is present. A row is needed only while its shape name is not yet import-visible.
// The shape counts as imported only when the binding's declaring module is std.algebra: a same-named shape bound
// from elsewhere (target not std.algebra.<name>) leaves the std.algebra import required.
fn roster_symbol_imported(imported: List<AliasBindingRow>, row: RosterHeadRow) -> Bool {
  fold_list(xs: imported, empty: false, cons: fn(found, b) { found || (symbol_lexeme(sym: b.binding) == row.import_name && roster_target_is_home(qn: b.target, row: row)) })
}

// The binding's target is exactly <home>.<import_name>.
fn roster_target_is_home(qn: QualifiedName, row: RosterHeadRow) -> Bool {
  roster_qn_text(qn: qn) == roster_qn_text(qn: row.home) + "." + row.import_name
}

// The import row is needed only while its name is not yet import-visible, so its sites are counted in the pre-import phase of
// the one classifier (roster_site_is_free), which also asks the home's declared KIND about its type-position sites.
fn roster_sites_count(sides: List<RosterHomeSide>, sites: FreeMonoid<ScopedReferenceSite>, row: RosterHeadRow, gates: List<RosterSiteGate>, spans: SpanIndex) -> Int {
  let gate = roster_gate_for(gates: gates, row: row)
  fold_list(
    xs: sites,
    empty: 0,
    cons: fn(n, s) {
      if roster_spelling_is(qn: s.site.spelling, call: row.call) && roster_site_is_free(sides: sides, site: s, row: row, imported_from_home: false) && roster_gate_allows_site(gate: gate, st: s, spans: spans) { n + 1 } else { n }
    }
  )
}

fn roster_spelling_is(qn: QualifiedName, call: String) -> Bool {
  match qn {
    Cons { head: h, tail: Empty } => (symbol_lexeme(sym: h) == call)
    _ => false
  }
}

fn roster_sweep_rows(sides: List<RosterHomeSide>, gates: List<RosterSiteGate>, 
  parse_root: Node,
  spans: SpanIndex,
  normalized_root: Node,
  imported: List<AliasBindingRow>,
  candidates: List<RosterHeadRow>,
  closures: List<RosterHomeClosure>
) -> RosterOutcome {
  let sites = collect_scoped_module_reference_sites(
    root: normalized_root,
    imported: list_map(xs: imported, f: fn(row) { row.binding })
  ).sites
  let needed = roster_needed_rows(sides: sides, sites: sites, imported: imported, candidates: candidates, gates: gates, spans: spans)
  match roster_any_unclassified_head(sides: sides, sites: sites, imported: imported, candidates: candidates) {
    // THE REFUSAL OUTRANKS CLEAN: a module whose census-unc classifiable free head sits among rows that need nothing is
    // exactly the "finished as if it succeeded" reading the review named; silence there is a fabricated Clean.
    Present { value: reason } => RosterRefused { reason: reason }
    Absent => if is_empty(xs: needed) {
      RosterClean
    } else if roster_any_needed_bound_elsewhere(needed: needed, imported: imported) {
    RosterRefused { reason: RefusalShapeNameBoundElsewhere }
  } else {
    roster_import_row(sides: sides, parse_root: parse_root, spans: spans, normalized_root: normalized_root, imported: imported, needed: needed, closures: closures, gates: gates)
  }
  }
}

// A needed shape name this module already binds to a DIFFERENT declaration: adding the std.algebra import would give one
// local name two targets, so the sweep names the conflict and leaves the file unchanged.
fn roster_any_needed_bound_elsewhere(needed: List<RosterHeadRow>, imported: List<AliasBindingRow>) -> Bool {
  fold_list(
    xs: needed,
    empty: false,
    cons: fn(found, row) {
      found || fold_list(xs: imported, empty: false, cons: fn(hit, b) { hit || symbol_lexeme(sym: b.binding) == row.import_name })
    }
  )
}

// ONE EXISTING std.algebra IMPORT: its bound names are the value's base. NONE: the value starts empty
// and the block is inserted after the last import declaration. TWO OR MORE std.algebra imports refuse
// (a merge would choose which declaration survives).
type ImportDeclFact {
  module_name: String
  names: List<String>
  start: Int
  end: Int
}

// ONE HOME PER OUTCOME: the needed rows of the FIRST home in table order are rendered; a file that needs a second home
// still has pending rows after the apply, so the convergence re-run (roster_import_sweep_exit) emits that home's edit next.
fn roster_import_row(sides: List<RosterHomeSide>, parse_root: Node, spans: SpanIndex, normalized_root: Node, imported: List<AliasBindingRow>, needed: List<RosterHeadRow>, closures: List<RosterHomeClosure>, gates: List<RosterSiteGate>) -> RosterOutcome {
  match needed {
    Empty => RosterClean
    Cons { head: first, tail: _ } =>
      let home_rows = fold_list(xs: needed, empty: [], cons: fn(acc, r) { if roster_qn_text(qn: r.home) == roster_qn_text(qn: first.home) { list_snoc_item(xs: acc, item: r) } else { acc } })
      match roster_module_cycle_refusal(parse_root: parse_root, closures: closures, home: roster_qn_text(qn: first.home)) {
        Present { value: reason } => RosterRefused { reason: reason }
        Absent =>
          roster_with_pending_labels(sides: sides, gates: gates, 
            parse_root: parse_root,
            spans: spans,
            normalized_root: normalized_root,
            imported: imported,
            rows: home_rows,
            edit: roster_import_row_home(parse_root: parse_root, spans: spans, home: first.home, needed: home_rows)
          )
      }
  }
}

// The swept module's own name, read off its parse by the reader acquisition uses (qualified_name_from_module_node), then the
// cycle verdict for importing `home` into it.
fn roster_module_cycle_refusal(parse_root: Node, closures: List<RosterHomeClosure>, home: String) -> Optional<RosterRefusalReason> {
  match qualified_name_from_module_node(root: parse_root) {
    Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => Present { value: RefusalModuleNameUnread }
    Accepted { value: qn, diagnostics: _ } => roster_cycle_refusal(closures: closures, home: home, module: roster_qn_text(qn: qn))
  }
}

fn roster_import_row_home(parse_root: Node, spans: SpanIndex, home: QualifiedName, needed: List<RosterHeadRow>) -> RosterOutcome {
  roster_import_names_edit(parse_root: parse_root, spans: spans, home: home, wanted: list_map(xs: needed, f: fn(r) { r.import_name }))
}

// THE ONE IMPORT RENDERER: `wanted` names imported from `home`, extending the module's existing import of it or inserting
// one after the last import (or the header). The rows' import edit and a rename's companion import both come through here.
fn roster_import_names_edit(parse_root: Node, spans: SpanIndex, home: QualifiedName, wanted: List<String>) -> RosterOutcome {
  let decls = roster_import_decl_facts(parse_root: parse_root, spans: spans)
  let algebra = roster_filter_module(decls: decls, module_name: roster_qn_text(qn: home))
  match length(xs: algebra) {
    0 =>
      match roster_last_decl_end(decls: decls) {
        Present { value: at } =>
          RosterEdit { start: at, end: at, text: roster_render_import(home: home, names: roster_dedupe(base: [], more: wanted)), own_line: true }
        // NO IMPORT YET: the first import goes where the grammar puts the first top-level item, directly after the module
        // header (v2.extdeps.languages.dag dag_grammar_module_expr: module_header, then top_level_item*). The anchor is the
        // header's own parsed extent, never a text search; a module whose header the parse does not place still refuses.
        Absent =>
          match roster_module_header_end(parse_root: parse_root, spans: spans) {
            Present { value: at } =>
              RosterEdit { start: at, end: at, text: "\n" + roster_render_import(home: home, names: roster_dedupe(base: [], more: wanted)), own_line: true }
            Absent => RosterRefused { reason: RefusalNoImportAnchor }
          }
      }
    _ =>
      // Several std.algebra imports make the same names visible; the first one is extended and the rest stay as authored.
      fold_list(
        xs: algebra,
        empty: RosterClean,
        cons: fn(acc, d) {
          match acc {
            RosterClean =>
              RosterEdit { start: d.start, end: d.end, text: roster_render_import(home: home, names: roster_dedupe(base: d.names, more: wanted)), own_line: false }
            _ => acc
          }
        }
      )
  }
}

// The end of the module header's parsed extent: exactly one header, read by its emitted production identity. None, or more
// than one, or one with no recorded extent, is Absent and the caller refuses.
fn roster_module_header_end(parse_root: Node, spans: SpanIndex) -> Int? {
  let headers = fold_list(xs: node_subtree_nodes(root: parse_root), empty: [], cons: fn(acc, n) {
    match parse_production_emitted_identity_optional(node: n) {
      Present { value: id } => if id == ^dag_surface_module_header { list_snoc_item(xs: acc, item: n) } else { acc }
      Absent => acc
    }
  })
  match headers {
    Cons { head: h, tail: Empty } =>
      match roster_node_byte_range(node: h, spans: spans) {
        Present { value: r } => Present { value: r.end }
        Absent => Absent
      }
    _ => Absent
  }
}

fn roster_render_import(home: QualifiedName, names: List<String>) -> String {
  "import " + roster_qn_text(qn: home) + " { " + roster_join(xs: names, sep: ", ") + " }"
}

// Deduplicated by spelling identity; the existing names keep their order, new names follow.
fn roster_dedupe(base: List<String>, more: List<String>) -> List<String> {
  fold_list(
    xs: more,
    empty: base,
    cons: fn(acc, name) {
      if roster_contains(xs: acc, name: name) { acc } else { list_snoc_item(xs: acc, item: name) }
    }
  )
}

fn roster_contains(xs: List<String>, name: String) -> Bool {
  fold_list(xs: xs, empty: false, cons: fn(found, x) { found || (x == name) })
}

fn roster_filter_module(decls: List<ImportDeclFact>, module_name: String) -> List<ImportDeclFact> {
  fold_list(
    xs: decls,
    empty: [],
    cons: fn(acc, d) {
      if (d.module_name == module_name) { list_snoc_item(xs: acc, item: d) } else { acc }
    }
  )
}

fn roster_last_decl_end(decls: List<ImportDeclFact>) -> Int? {
  fold_list(
    xs: decls,
    empty: Absent,
    cons: fn(acc, d) { Present { value: d.end } }
  )
}

fn roster_import_decl_facts(parse_root: Node, spans: SpanIndex) -> List<ImportDeclFact> {
  fold_list(
    xs: node_subtree_nodes(root: parse_root),
    empty: [],
    cons: fn(acc, n) {
      match parse_production_emitted_identity_optional(node: n) {
        Present { value: id } =>
          if id == ^dag_surface_import_decl {
            match roster_import_decl_fact(decl: n, root: parse_root, spans: spans) {
              Present { value: fact } => list_snoc_item(xs: acc, item: fact)
              Absent => acc
            }
          } else {
            acc
          }
        Absent => acc
      }
    }
  )
}

fn roster_import_decl_fact(decl: Node, root: Node, spans: SpanIndex) -> ImportDeclFact? {
  match import_decl_target_module(decl: decl, module_root: root) {
    Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => Absent
    Accepted { value: target, diagnostics: _ } =>
      match parse_import_block_idents(import_decl_node: decl, root: root) {
        Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => Absent
        Accepted { value: names, diagnostics: _ } =>
          match roster_node_byte_range(node: decl, spans: spans) {
            Present { value: range } =>
              Present {
                value: ImportDeclFact {
                  module_name: roster_join(xs: list_map(xs: target, f: fn(s) { symbol_lexeme(sym: s) }), sep: "."),
                  names: list_map(xs: names, f: fn(s) { symbol_lexeme(sym: s) }),
                  start: range.start,
                  end: range.end
                }
              }
            Absent => Absent
          }
      }
  }
}

type RosterByteRange {
  start: Int
  end: Int
}

fn roster_node_byte_range(node: Node, spans: SpanIndex) -> RosterByteRange? {
  roster_identity_byte_range(identity: node.occurrence_id, spans: spans)
}

fn roster_identity_byte_range(identity: NodeOccurrenceIdentity, spans: SpanIndex) -> RosterByteRange? {
  match identity {
    OccurrenceMinted { id: id } => roster_id_byte_range(id: id, spans: spans)
    OccurrenceProjected { id: id, caused_by: _ } => roster_id_byte_range(id: id, spans: spans)
    OccurrenceSynthetic => Absent
    OccurrencePending { caused_by: _ } => Absent
  }
}

fn roster_id_byte_range(id: OccurrenceId, spans: SpanIndex) -> RosterByteRange? {
  match span_index_extent(index: spans, id: id) {
    Present { value: recorded } =>
      match recorded {
        SourceExtentKnown { locus: Textual { file: _, extent: ByteRange { start: s, end: e } } } =>
          Present { value: RosterByteRange { start: s, end: e } }
        _ => Absent
      }
    Absent => Absent
  }
}

fn roster_join(xs: List<String>, sep: String) -> String {
  fold_list(xs: xs, empty: "", cons: fn(acc, x) { if acc == "" { x } else { acc + sep + x } })
}

// THE CONTROLS, run as `gunbc run --entry src/v2/workflow/roster_import_sweep.dag --function roster_import_sweep_controls_exit`.
// Each case is source text pushed through the same tokenize/parse/normalize route and the same pure splice the apply step
// performs, so a divergence between parser coordinates and applier coordinates fails here with the case named.
//   homonym:  a same-named shape imported from another module does not satisfy the std.algebra import (an EDIT, not Clean).
//   present:  the std.algebra import already carries the shape (Clean).
//   multibyte: UTF-8 text before and after the import; byte extents must land on scalar boundaries and everything outside
//             the extent is preserved byte for byte.
//   annotation: a `//` inside the replaced import would be erased, so the splice refuses.
// The OnlyOccurrences controls alone (roster_occ_controls), for a bounded run of the selection's own verdicts.
fn roster_import_sweep_occ_controls_exit() -> ProcessExit {
  let report = match dag_prepared_grammar() {
    Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => "CONTROL-FAIL grammar-unprepared\n"
    Accepted { value: prepared, diagnostics: _ } =>
      fold_list(xs: roster_occ_controls(prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex()), empty: "", cons: fn(acc, v) { acc + v.fail })
  }
  if (report == "") { ExitSuccess } else { exit_failure(reason: report) }
}

fn roster_import_sweep_controls_exit() -> ProcessExit {
  let report = roster_controls_report()
  if (report == "") { ExitSuccess } else { exit_failure(reason: report) }
}

// THE GATED ENTRY: `gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:roster-import-sweep-controls` (gunbc.instrument_targets
// roster_import_sweep_controls_binding, a CliWireProgramProducer row). It runs the pure controls; the effectful lock controls
// need a caller-made empty directory and stay a hand-run entry.
fn roster_import_sweep_controls_wire() -> CliWireResponse {
  let report = roster_controls_report()
  if (report == "") {
    CliWirePrintable { bytes: "roster-import-sweep controls held\n", exit: ExitSuccess }
  } else {
    CliWirePrintable { bytes: report, exit: exit_failure(reason: report) }
  }
}

// THE BOUNDARY CONTROLS USE AN OTHERWISE VALID EDIT: an import the splice accepts (roster_control_edit_splices proves
// it on the text), so a refusal at the write boundary can only be the boundary's own, never an invalid splice's.
fn roster_control_source(module_name: String) -> String {
  "module " + module_name + "\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(xs: List<String>) -> Int {\n  count(xs: xs)\n}\n"
}

fn roster_control_valid_edit(module_name: String) -> RosterOutcome {
  let start = string_length(s: "module " + module_name + "\n\n")
  RosterEdit { start: start, end: start + 27, text: "import std.algebra { Cons, collection_count_shape }", own_line: false }
}

fn roster_control_edit_splices() -> String {
  match roster_applied(before: roster_control_source(module_name: "c.unheld"), outcome: roster_control_valid_edit(module_name: "c.unheld")) {
    RosterApplyWritten { content: content } =>
      if content == "module c.unheld\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, collection_count_shape }\n\nfn f(xs: List<String>) -> Int {\n  count(xs: xs)\n}\n" { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL valid-edit: spliced to unexpected text\n" }
    RosterApplyRefused { reason: reason } => "CONTROL-FAIL valid-edit: refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: reason) + "\n"
  }
}

// THE CONTROLS' CLOSURES ARE SUPPLIED VALUES (DESIGN section 3, a witness discriminates at one interface): each home a
// control fixture imports, with a closure that holds no c.* fixture module. roster_control_closure_inhabited pins the real
// producer separately.
fn roster_control_closures() -> List<RosterHomeClosure> {
  [
    RosterClosureRead { home: "std.algebra", modules: ["std.algebra", "std.optional", "std.error_primitives"] },
    RosterClosureRead { home: "std.host_text", modules: ["std.host_text", "std.types"] }
  ]
}

fn roster_controls_report() -> String {
  match dag_prepared_grammar() {
    Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => "CONTROL-FAIL grammar-unprepared\n"
    Accepted { value: prepared, diagnostics: _ } =>
      roster_control_homonym(prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex())
        + roster_control_present(prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex())
        + roster_control_multibyte(prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex())
        + roster_control_annotation(prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex())
        + roster_control_home_converges(prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex())
        + roster_control_no_import_anchor(prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex())
        + roster_control_import_closes_cycle(prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex())
        + roster_control_closure_inhabited()
        + roster_control_row_scope(prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex())
        + roster_control_scope_selects_its_row()
        + roster_home_exact_file_control()
        + roster_control_apply_needs_one_home()
        + roster_control_label_local_call(prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex())
        + roster_control_label_method_spelling(prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex())
        + roster_control_imported_qualified_tag(prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex())
        + roster_control_unbound_qualified_tag(prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex())
        + roster_control_d4_value_call_positive(prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex())
        + roster_control_free_call_beside_param(prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex())
        + roster_control_free_call_after_param(prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex())
        + roster_control_nested_call_beside_param(prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex())
        + roster_control_label_bound_occurrence(prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex())
        + roster_control_free_call_beside_let(prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex())
        + roster_control_free_call_beside_pun(prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex())
        + roster_control_specimen(prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex())
        + roster_control_called_parameter(prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex())
        + roster_control_nested_call_label(prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex())
        + roster_control_label_sites_disagree(prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex())
        + roster_control_label_pass2_clean(prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex())
        + roster_kind_controls(prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex())
        + roster_rename_controls_counted(prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex())
        + roster_control_positional_past_unreadable()
        + roster_control_edit_splices()
        + roster_control_generation()
        + roster_control_status_names()
        + roster_control_ancestor()
  }
}

// THE RENAME ROW'S CONTROLS, over the PRODUCTION map_get row (never a copy of it), so a change to the row is measured.
// Positive: one write imports map_lookup, rewrites both heads and labels both arguments, including a call nested in
// another's argument; pass 2 is Clean. Each refusal is the row's own: a named argument and a missing argument. A call spelling a
// parameter binds is never a candidate (Clean), nor is a method spelling `x.map_get(...)`, which is not a primary head and is left alone.
fn roster_rename_production_row() -> List<RosterHeadRow> {
  fold_list(xs: roster_head_rows(), empty: [], cons: fn(acc, r) {
    match r.head {
      KeepHead => acc
      RenameHead { to: _, positional: _ } => list_snoc_item(xs: acc, item: r)
    }
  })
}

fn roster_rename_outcome(companions: List<RosterCompanion>, text: String, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> RosterOutcome {
  roster_sweep_text_rows(sides: roster_home_sides(rows: roster_rename_production_row()), companions: companions, path: "control/rename.dag", text: text, prepared: prepared, lex: lex, candidates: roster_rename_production_row(), closures: roster_control_closures())
}

fn roster_rename_expect_refusal(companions: List<RosterCompanion>, name: String, text: String, want: String, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  match roster_rename_outcome(companions: companions, text: text, prepared: prepared, lex: lex) {
    RosterRefused { reason: r } => if roster_refusal_text(reason: r) == want { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + ", wanted " + want + "\n" }
    other => "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": not refused, got " + roster_render_outcome(path: "control/rename.dag", outcome: other)
  }
}

// The generator's own fixed point on a text: sweep, splice, repeat (as the apply step converges), at most four passes.
type RosterConverged
  = ConvergedText { text: String }
  | ConvergedRefused { cause: String }

fn roster_rename_converge(companions: List<RosterCompanion>, text: String, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> RosterConverged {
  fold_list(xs: [0, 1, 2, 3], empty: ConvergedText { text: text }, cons: fn(acc, _i) {
    match acc {
      ConvergedRefused { cause: c } => ConvergedRefused { cause: c }
      ConvergedText { text: t } =>
        match roster_rename_outcome(companions: companions, text: t, prepared: prepared, lex: lex) {
          RosterClean => acc
          RosterRefused { reason: r } => ConvergedRefused { cause: roster_refusal_text(reason: r) }
          outcome =>
            match roster_applied(before: t, outcome: outcome) {
              RosterApplyRefused { reason: r } => ConvergedRefused { cause: "splice " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) }
              RosterApplyWritten { content: c } => ConvergedText { text: c }
            }
        }
    }
  })
}

fn roster_rename_expect_text(companions: List<RosterCompanion>, name: String, before: String, after: String, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  match roster_rename_converge(companions: companions, text: before, prepared: prepared, lex: lex) {
    ConvergedRefused { cause: c } => "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": refused " + c + "\n"
    ConvergedText { text: t } =>
      if t != after {
        "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": converged to unexpected text: " + t + "\n"
      } else {
        match roster_rename_outcome(companions: companions, text: t, prepared: prepared, lex: lex) {
          RosterClean => ""
          other => "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": not a fixed point: " + roster_render_outcome(path: "control/rename.dag", outcome: other)
        }
      }
  }
}

// THE COMPANION IS DERIVED, NOT SUPPLIED: these controls read it from the real std.algebra and std.optional sources
// (roster_rename_companions over the production map_get row) and require it to be exactly std.optional's two variants.
fn roster_companion_derived_check(companions: List<RosterCompanion>) -> String {
  match companions {
    Cons { head: CompanionDerived { call: _, to: _, module: m, tags: ts, closure: _ }, tail: Empty } =>
      if (m == "std.optional") && (roster_join(xs: ts, sep: ",") == "Absent,Present") { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL companion-derivation: got " + m + " {" + roster_join(xs: ts, sep: ",") + "}\n" }
    Cons { head: CompanionUnderivable { call: _, to: _, detail: d }, tail: _ } => "CONTROL-FAIL companion-derivation: underivable " + d + "\n"
    _ => "CONTROL-FAIL companion-derivation: not exactly one derived companion\n"
  }
}

// ONE CONTROL'S VERDICT: its name, and its failure text ("" when it held). A report of failures alone reads the same when every
// control held and when none ran, so the rename controls are also counted against a declared list (tidy-ant-251, #15101).
type RosterControlVerdict {
  name: String
  fail: String
}

fn roster_control_verdict(name: String, fail: String) -> RosterControlVerdict {
  RosterControlVerdict { name: name, fail: fail }
}

fn roster_control_fails(verdicts: List<RosterControlVerdict>) -> String {
  fold_list(xs: verdicts, empty: "", cons: fn(acc, v) { acc + v.fail })
}

// THE DECLARED CONTROLS, written out and not derived from the verdicts, so a control that is dropped from the run, or one
// added without being declared, fails the count. A name is matched by identity in both directions.
fn roster_rename_control_names() -> List<String> {
  [
    "companion-derived",
    "rename-positive (with the companion import)",
    "rename-in-argument (no tag used: no companion)",
    "companion imports only the tags used",
    "companion tags already imported",
    "no renamed call: ambient tags left for their own wave",
    "rename-named-argument-matching",
    "rename-named-argument-mixed",
    "rename-named-argument-mismatched",
    "rename-named-argument-reordered",
    "rename-companion-tag-undecided",
    "rename-arity",
    "rename-parameter-bound",
    "rename-method-spelling",
    "rename-pipe",
    "rename-pipe-multiline-operand",
    "rename-pipe-chain",
    "rename-pipe-nested-operand",
    "rename-pipe-into-a-chain-step",
    "rename-pipe-parameter-bound",
    "rename-pipe-operand-unclean",
    "rename-pipe-arity",
    "rename-pipe-named-argument-matching",
    "rename-pipe-named-argument-mismatched",
    "companion-underivable",
    "edits-coincide",
    "edits-overlap",
    "edits-insert-inside-replacement",
    "edits-rename-shape",
    "import-and-label-coincide",
    "import-then-label-disjoint",
    "edits-adjacent-replacements",
    "edits-pipe-three-adjacent",
    "edits-connector-overlaps-head-by-one",
    "relocation-splice",
    "occurrences-selected-site-rewrites-unselected-untouched",
    "occurrences-every-site-selected",
    "occurrences-stale-key-refuses",
    "occurrences-key-off-the-head-refuses",
    "occurrences-empty-key-list-refuses",
    "occurrences-byte-column-after-multibyte-text",
    "occurrences-scalar-column-after-multibyte-text-refuses",
    "occurrences-two-rows-one-call-each-scope-rewrites-only-its-own",
    "occurrences-unknown-row-key-refuses",
    "occurrences-key-on-a-bound-site-refuses",
    "occurrences-key-outside-the-paths-refuses"
  ]
}

fn roster_rename_control_count_check(verdicts: List<RosterControlVerdict>) -> String {
  let ran = list_map(xs: verdicts, f: fn(v) { v.name })
  let declared = roster_rename_control_names()
  let missing = fold_list(xs: declared, empty: "", cons: fn(acc, n) { if roster_contains(xs: ran, name: n) { acc } else { acc + "CONTROL-FAIL control-count: declared control did not run: " + n + "\n" } })
  let undeclared = fold_list(xs: ran, empty: "", cons: fn(acc, n) { if roster_contains(xs: declared, name: n) { acc } else { acc + "CONTROL-FAIL control-count: ran an undeclared control: " + n + "\n" } })
  let count = if length(xs: ran) == length(xs: declared) { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL control-count: ran " + int_to_decimal_string(value: length(xs: ran)) + ", declared " + int_to_decimal_string(value: length(xs: declared)) + "\n" }
  missing + undeclared + count
}

fn roster_rename_controls_verdicts_all(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> List<RosterControlVerdict> {
  list_append(left: roster_rename_control_verdicts(prepared: prepared, lex: lex), right: list_append(left: roster_control_edits_disjoint_verdicts(), right: roster_occ_controls(prepared: prepared, lex: lex)))
}

// The rename controls' failures and the count check, as the gated report reads them.
fn roster_rename_controls_counted(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  let verdicts = roster_rename_controls_verdicts_all(prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
  roster_control_fails(verdicts: verdicts) + roster_rename_control_count_check(verdicts: verdicts)
}

fn roster_rename_control_verdicts(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> List<RosterControlVerdict> {
  let companions = roster_rename_companions(rows: roster_rename_production_row(), prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
  let before = "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> String {\n  match map_get(m, k) {\n    Present { value: v } => match map_get(m, v) {\n      Present { value: w } => w\n      Absent => k\n    }\n    Absent => k\n  }\n}\n"
  let after = "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, map_lookup }\nimport std.optional { Absent, Present }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> String {\n  match map_lookup(m: m, key: k) {\n    Present { value: v } => match map_lookup(m: m, key: v) {\n      Present { value: w } => w\n      Absent => k\n    }\n    Absent => k\n  }\n}\n"
  let nested = "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, Map<String, String>>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  g(x: map_get(m, k), k: k)\n}\n"
  let nested_after = "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, map_lookup }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, Map<String, String>>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  g(x: map_lookup(m: m, key: k), k: k)\n}\n"
  let only_present = "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Bool {\n  match map_get(m, k) {\n    Present { value: _ } => true\n    _ => false\n  }\n}\n"
  let only_present_after = "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, map_lookup }\nimport std.optional { Present }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Bool {\n  match map_lookup(m: m, key: k) {\n    Present { value: _ } => true\n    _ => false\n  }\n}\n"
  let tags_imported = "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\nimport std.optional { Absent, Present }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> String {\n  match map_get(m, k) {\n    Present { value: v } => v\n    Absent => k\n  }\n}\n"
  let tags_imported_after = "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, map_lookup }\nimport std.optional { Absent, Present }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> String {\n  match map_lookup(m: m, key: k) {\n    Present { value: v } => v\n    Absent => k\n  }\n}\n"
  let unrenamed = "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(o: Optional<String>, k: String) -> String {\n  match o {\n    Present { value: v } => v\n    Absent => k\n  }\n}\n"
  [
    roster_control_verdict(name: "companion-derived", fail: roster_companion_derived_check(companions: companions)),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "rename-positive (with the companion import)", fail: roster_rename_expect_text(companions: companions, name: "rename-positive (with the companion import)", before: before, after: after, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "rename-in-argument (no tag used: no companion)", fail: roster_rename_expect_text(companions: companions, name: "rename-in-argument (no tag used: no companion)", before: nested, after: nested_after, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "companion imports only the tags used", fail: roster_rename_expect_text(companions: companions, name: "companion imports only the tags used", before: only_present, after: only_present_after, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "companion tags already imported", fail: roster_rename_expect_text(companions: companions, name: "companion tags already imported", before: tags_imported, after: tags_imported_after, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "no renamed call: ambient tags left for their own wave", fail: roster_rename_expect_text(companions: companions, name: "no renamed call: ambient tags left for their own wave", before: unrenamed, after: unrenamed, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    // THE NAMED-ARGUMENT RULE: a label equal to the row's label at its position binds as authored; a mismatched label refuses;
    // a reordered pair refuses (never remapped, which would reorder evaluation).
    roster_control_verdict(name: "rename-named-argument-matching", fail: roster_rename_expect_text(companions: companions, name: "rename-named-argument-matching", before: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  map_get(m: m, key: k)\n}\n", after: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, map_lookup }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  map_lookup(m: m, key: k)\n}\n", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "rename-named-argument-mixed", fail: roster_rename_expect_text(companions: companions, name: "rename-named-argument-mixed", before: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  map_get(m, key: k)\n}\n", after: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, map_lookup }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  map_lookup(m: m, key: k)\n}\n", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "rename-named-argument-mismatched", fail: roster_rename_expect_refusal(companions: companions, name: "rename-named-argument-mismatched", text: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  map_get(m: m, k: k)\n}\n", want: "rename-call-named-argument call=map_get", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "rename-named-argument-reordered", fail: roster_rename_expect_refusal(companions: companions, name: "rename-named-argument-reordered", text: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  map_get(key: k, m: m)\n}\n", want: "rename-call-named-argument call=map_get", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "rename-companion-tag-undecided", fail: roster_rename_expect_refusal(companions: companions, name: "rename-companion-tag-undecided", text: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, map_lookup }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String, o: Optional<String>) -> String {\n  match o {\n    Present { value: Present } => match map_lookup(m: m, key: k) {\n      Present { value: v } => v\n      Absent => k\n    }\n    Absent => k\n  }\n}\n", want: "companion-tag-undecided call=map_get tag=Present", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "rename-arity", fail: roster_rename_expect_refusal(companions: companions, name: "rename-arity", text: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  map_get(m)\n}\n", want: "rename-call-arity call=map_get", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "rename-parameter-bound", fail: roster_rename_expect_text(companions: companions, name: "rename-parameter-bound", before: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(map_get: fn(String) -> String, k: String) -> String {\n  map_get(k)\n}\n", after: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(map_get: fn(String) -> String, k: String) -> String {\n  map_get(k)\n}\n", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "rename-method-spelling", fail: roster_rename_expect_text(companions: companions, name: "rename-method-spelling", before: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  m.map_get(k)\n}\n", after: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  m.map_get(k)\n}\n", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    // THE PIPE FORM (sunny-bee-153, tidy-ant-251's ruling): a piped call is the same rename with the pipe's left operand as slot 0,
    // one replacement, the operand copied byte for byte.
    roster_control_verdict(name: "rename-pipe", fail: roster_rename_expect_text(companions: companions, name: "rename-pipe", before: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  m |> map_get(k)\n}\n", after: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, map_lookup }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  map_lookup(m: m, key: k)\n}\n", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "rename-pipe-multiline-operand", fail: roster_rename_expect_text(companions: companions, name: "rename-pipe-multiline-operand", before: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  g(\n    x: m\n  ) |> map_get(k)\n}\n", after: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, map_lookup }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  map_lookup(m: g(\n    x: m\n  ), key: k)\n}\n", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    // A CHAIN and a NESTED operand: the outer pipe replacement holds the inner renamed call, which is deferred to the next pass
    // and converges there, never planned as an overlapping edit.
    roster_control_verdict(name: "rename-pipe-chain", fail: roster_rename_expect_text(companions: companions, name: "rename-pipe-chain", before: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  m |> map_get(k) |> map_get(k)\n}\n", after: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, map_lookup }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  map_lookup(m: map_lookup(m: m, key: k), key: k)\n}\n", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "rename-pipe-nested-operand", fail: roster_rename_expect_text(companions: companions, name: "rename-pipe-nested-operand", before: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  map_get(m, k) |> map_get(k)\n}\n", after: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, map_lookup }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  map_lookup(m: map_lookup(m: m, key: k), key: k)\n}\n", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "rename-pipe-into-a-chain-step", fail: roster_rename_expect_text(companions: companions, name: "rename-pipe-into-a-chain-step", before: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  m |> map_get(k) |> h()\n}\n", after: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, map_lookup }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  map_lookup(m: m, key: k) |> h()\n}\n", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    // A PIPE INTO A PARAMETER-BOUND name stays untouched: selection is the one binding-sensitive classifier.
    roster_control_verdict(name: "rename-pipe-parameter-bound", fail: roster_rename_expect_text(companions: companions, name: "rename-pipe-parameter-bound", before: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(map_get: fn(String, String) -> String, m: String, k: String) -> String {\n  m |> map_get(k)\n}\n", after: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(map_get: fn(String, String) -> String, m: String, k: String) -> String {\n  m |> map_get(k)\n}\n", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    // REDs: an operand the pipe does not cleanly hand to the call, a pipe arity mismatch, and a named argument after the pipe.
    roster_control_verdict(name: "rename-pipe-operand-unclean", fail: roster_rename_expect_refusal(companions: companions, name: "rename-pipe-operand-unclean", text: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Int {\n  m |> map_get(k) + 1\n}\n", want: "rename-pipe-operand-unclean call=map_get", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "rename-pipe-arity", fail: roster_rename_expect_refusal(companions: companions, name: "rename-pipe-arity", text: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  m |> map_get(k, k)\n}\n", want: "rename-call-arity call=map_get", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "rename-pipe-named-argument-matching", fail: roster_rename_expect_text(companions: companions, name: "rename-pipe-named-argument-matching", before: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  m |> map_get(key: k)\n}\n", after: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, map_lookup }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  map_lookup(m: m, key: k)\n}\n", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "rename-pipe-named-argument-mismatched", fail: roster_rename_expect_refusal(companions: companions, name: "rename-pipe-named-argument-mismatched", text: "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  m |> map_get(k2: k)\n}\n", want: "rename-call-named-argument call=map_get", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "companion-underivable", fail: roster_companion_underivable_control(prepared: prepared, lex: lex))
  ]
}

// THE PER-SITE SELECTION (OnlyOccurrences), on one home. The fixture holds two free map_get sites, lines 6 and 7; a
// census key names a site by `<path>:<line>:<byte column>`.
fn roster_occ_gate(text: String, keys: List<String>) -> List<RosterSiteGate> {
  [RosterSiteGate { home: "std.algebra", row_key: "map_get", call: "map_get", keys: keys, path: "control/rename.dag", starts: line_starts(text: text) }]
}

fn roster_occ_outcome(text: String, keys: List<String>, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> RosterOutcome {
  let rows = roster_rename_production_row()
  roster_sweep_text_gate(sides: roster_home_sides(rows: rows), companions: [], path: "control/rename.dag", text: text, prepared: prepared, lex: lex, candidates: rows, closures: roster_control_closures(), gates: roster_occ_gate(text: text, keys: keys))
}

fn roster_occ_expect_text(name: String, before: String, keys: List<String>, after: String, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  match roster_applied(before: before, outcome: roster_occ_outcome(text: before, keys: keys, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)) {
    RosterApplyRefused { reason: r } => "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + "\n"
    RosterApplyWritten { content: c } => if c == after { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": wrote unexpected text: " + c + "\n" }
  }
}

fn roster_occ_expect_unmatched(name: String, text: String, keys: List<String>, key: String, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  match roster_occ_outcome(text: text, keys: keys, prepared: prepared, lex: lex) {
    RosterRefused { reason: r } =>
      if roster_refusal_text(reason: r) == "occurrence-key-unmatched path=control/rename.dag call=map_get key=" + key { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + "\n" }
    other => "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": not refused, got " + roster_render_outcome(path: "control/rename.dag", outcome: other)
  }
}

fn roster_occ_controls(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> List<RosterControlVerdict> {
  let head = "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons"
  let body = " }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  let a = map_get(m, k)\n  map_get(m, k)\n}\n"
  let both = "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, map_lookup }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  let a = map_lookup(m: m, key: k)\n  map_lookup(m: m, key: k)\n}\n"
  let second_only = "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, map_lookup }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  let a = map_get(m, k)\n  map_lookup(m: m, key: k)\n}\n"
  let wide = "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  g(x: \"é😀\", y: map_get(m, k))\n}\n"
  let wide_after = "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, map_lookup }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  g(x: \"é😀\", y: map_lookup(m: m, key: k))\n}\n"
  let src = head + body
  let bound = "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(k: String) -> String {\n  let map_get = k\n  map_get\n}\n"
  [
    roster_control_verdict(name: "occurrences-selected-site-rewrites-unselected-untouched", fail: roster_occ_expect_text(name: "occurrences-selected-site-rewrites-unselected-untouched", before: src, keys: ["control/rename.dag:7:3"], after: second_only, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "occurrences-every-site-selected", fail: roster_occ_expect_text(name: "occurrences-every-site-selected", before: src, keys: ["control/rename.dag:6:11", "control/rename.dag:7:3"], after: both, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "occurrences-stale-key-refuses", fail: roster_occ_expect_unmatched(name: "occurrences-stale-key-refuses", text: src, keys: ["control/rename.dag:7:3", "control/rename.dag:9:3"], key: "control/rename.dag:9:3", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "occurrences-key-off-the-head-refuses", fail: roster_occ_expect_unmatched(name: "occurrences-key-off-the-head-refuses", text: src, keys: ["control/rename.dag:7:4"], key: "control/rename.dag:7:4", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "occurrences-empty-key-list-refuses", fail: roster_occ_empty_control()),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "occurrences-byte-column-after-multibyte-text", fail: roster_occ_expect_text(name: "occurrences-byte-column-after-multibyte-text", before: wide, keys: ["control/rename.dag:6:21"], after: wide_after, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "occurrences-two-rows-one-call-each-scope-rewrites-only-its-own", fail: roster_occ_two_rows_control(prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "occurrences-unknown-row-key-refuses", fail: roster_occ_unknown_row_control()),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "occurrences-scalar-column-after-multibyte-text-refuses", fail: roster_occ_expect_unmatched(name: "occurrences-scalar-column-after-multibyte-text-refuses", text: wide, keys: ["control/rename.dag:6:17"], key: "control/rename.dag:6:17", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "occurrences-key-on-a-bound-site-refuses", fail: roster_occ_expect_unmatched(name: "occurrences-key-on-a-bound-site-refuses", text: bound, keys: ["control/rename.dag:7:3"], key: "control/rename.dag:7:3", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "occurrences-key-outside-the-paths-refuses", fail: roster_occ_outside_paths_control())
  ]
}

fn roster_occ_scope_of(key: String) -> RosterHomeScope {
  OneHome { home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.algebra"), rows: OnlyOccurrences { row: "map_get", call: "map_get", occurrences: [key] } }
}

// A key naming a file outside the run's paths meets no file's run, so it refuses at the entry; a key inside the paths passes it.
fn roster_occ_outside_paths_control() -> String {
  let outside = match roster_key_outside_paths(paths_csv: "a.dag,b.dag", scope: roster_occ_scope_of(key: "c.dag:1:1")) {
    Present { value: r } => if roster_refusal_text(reason: r) == "occurrence-key-unmatched path=c.dag call=map_get key=c.dag:1:1" { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL occurrences-key-outside-the-paths-refuses: refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + "\n" }
    Absent => "CONTROL-FAIL occurrences-key-outside-the-paths-refuses: a key outside the paths was admitted\n"
  }
  let inside = match roster_key_outside_paths(paths_csv: "a.dag,b.dag", scope: roster_occ_scope_of(key: "b.dag:1:1")) {
    Present { value: r } => "CONTROL-FAIL occurrences-key-outside-the-paths-refuses: a key inside the paths refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + "\n"
    Absent => ""
  }
  outside + inside
}

fn roster_occ_empty_control() -> String {
  match roster_scope_selection_refusal_in(table: roster_rename_production_row(), scope: OneHome { home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.algebra"), rows: OnlyOccurrences { row: "map_get", call: "map_get", occurrences: [] } }) {
    Present { value: r } => if roster_refusal_text(reason: r) == "scope-selects-no-row home=std.algebra row=map_get call=map_get occurrences=empty" { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL occurrences-empty-key-list-refuses: refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + "\n" }
    Absent => "CONTROL-FAIL occurrences-empty-key-list-refuses: an empty key list was admitted\n"
  }
}

// ROW IDENTITY, NOT (home, call): two rows over ONE (home, call) -- the shape std.algebra sort_by has (a Symbol-order and a
// String-order row) -- are told apart by their declared keys, and each scope rewrites only its own occurrences. The rows
// here rename to different targets so the output names which row acted.
fn roster_occ_twin_rows() -> List<RosterHeadRow> {
  let algebra = qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.algebra")
  [
    RosterHeadRow { call: "map_get", key: "map_get/first", import_name: "map_lookup", home: algebra, labels: [], head: RenameHead { to: "map_lookup", positional: ["m", "key"] } },
    RosterHeadRow { call: "map_get", key: "map_get/second", import_name: "map_contains_key", home: algebra, labels: [], head: RenameHead { to: "map_contains_key", positional: ["m", "key"] } }
  ]
}

fn roster_occ_twin_outcome(row_key: String, keys: List<String>, text: String, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> RosterOutcome {
  let rows = roster_occ_twin_rows()
  let scope = OneHome { home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.algebra"), rows: OnlyOccurrences { row: row_key, call: "map_get", occurrences: keys } }
  roster_sweep_text_gate(sides: roster_home_sides(rows: rows), companions: [], path: "control/rename.dag", text: text, prepared: prepared, lex: lex, candidates: roster_rows_for_scope_in(table: rows, scope: scope), closures: roster_control_closures(), gates: roster_scope_gates(scope: scope, path: "control/rename.dag", text: text))
}

fn roster_occ_two_rows_control(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  let before = "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  let a = map_get(m, k)\n  map_get(m, k)\n}\n"
  let first = "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, map_lookup }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  let a = map_get(m, k)\n  map_lookup(m: m, key: k)\n}\n"
  let second = "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, map_contains_key }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Optional<String> {\n  let a = map_contains_key(m: m, key: k)\n  map_get(m, k)\n}\n"
  let scope_a = match roster_applied(before: before, outcome: roster_occ_twin_outcome(row_key: "map_get/first", keys: ["control/rename.dag:7:3"], text: before, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)) {
    RosterApplyRefused { reason: r } => "CONTROL-FAIL occurrences-two-rows: first row refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + "\n"
    RosterApplyWritten { content: c } => if c == first { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL occurrences-two-rows: first row wrote " + c + "\n" }
  }
  let scope_b = match roster_applied(before: before, outcome: roster_occ_twin_outcome(row_key: "map_get/second", keys: ["control/rename.dag:6:11"], text: before, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)) {
    RosterApplyRefused { reason: r } => "CONTROL-FAIL occurrences-two-rows: second row refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + "\n"
    RosterApplyWritten { content: c } => if c == second { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL occurrences-two-rows: second row wrote " + c + "\n" }
  }
  scope_a + scope_b
}

fn roster_occ_unknown_row_control() -> String {
  let scope = OneHome { home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.algebra"), rows: OnlyOccurrences { row: "map_get/third", call: "map_get", occurrences: ["control/rename.dag:7:3"] } }
  match roster_scope_selection_refusal_in(table: roster_occ_twin_rows(), scope: scope) {
    Present { value: r } => if roster_refusal_text(reason: r) == "scope-selects-no-row home=std.algebra row=map_get/third call=map_get" { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL occurrences-unknown-row-key-refuses: refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + "\n" }
    Absent => "CONTROL-FAIL occurrences-unknown-row-key-refuses: an unknown row key was admitted\n"
  }
}

// AN UNDERIVABLE COMPANION REFUSES THE FILE IT WOULD GOVERN: a rename row whose callee the home does not declare.
fn roster_companion_underivable_control(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  let ghost = [RosterHeadRow { call: "map_get", key: "map_get", import_name: "no_such_lookup", home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.algebra"), labels: [], head: RenameHead { to: "no_such_lookup", positional: ["m", "key"] } }]
  let companions = roster_rename_companions(rows: ghost, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
  let text = "module c.rename\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, no_such_lookup }\n\nfn f(m: Map<String, String>, k: String) -> Bool {\n  match no_such_lookup(m: m, key: k) {\n    Present { value: _ } => true\n    Absent => false\n  }\n}\n"
  match roster_sweep_text_rows(sides: roster_home_sides(rows: ghost), companions: companions, path: "control/rename.dag", text: text, prepared: prepared, lex: lex, candidates: ghost, closures: roster_control_closures()) {
    RosterRefused { reason: r } => if starts_with(s: roster_refusal_text(reason: r), prefix: "companion-underivable call=map_get") { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL companion-underivable: refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + "\n" }
    other => "CONTROL-FAIL companion-underivable: not refused, got " + roster_render_outcome(path: "control/rename.dag", outcome: other)
  }
}

// A HOME OTHER THAN std.algebra, in ONE write: pass 1 inserts `import std.host_text { chars }` after the last import AND
// renames each `chars(s:` label to `text:` (a file with the import and the old label does not resolve), leaving a non-call
// `s:` and a call to another function alone; pass 2 is Clean. Multibyte text after the call checks the label extents.
fn roster_control_home_converges(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  let before = "module c.host\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, collection_count_shape }\n\nfn f(x: String) -> Int {\n  g(s: x) + count(xs: chars(s: x)) + count(xs: chars(s: \"é😀\"))\n}\n"
  let after = "module c.host\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, collection_count_shape }\nimport std.host_text { chars }\n\nfn f(x: String) -> Int {\n  g(s: x) + count(xs: chars(text: x)) + count(xs: chars(text: \"é😀\"))\n}\n"
  match roster_applied(before: before, outcome: roster_sweep_text(path: "control/host.dag", text: before, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)) {
    RosterApplyRefused { reason: r } => "CONTROL-FAIL home-converges: pass 1 refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + "\n"
    RosterApplyWritten { content: c1 } =>
      if c1 != after { "CONTROL-FAIL home-converges: pass 1 did not write the std.host_text import and exactly the chars(s: relabels\n" } else {
        match roster_sweep_text(path: "control/host.dag", text: c1, prepared: prepared, lex: lex) {
          RosterClean => ""
          _ => "CONTROL-FAIL home-converges: pass 2 is not Clean\n"
        }
      }
  }
}

// A METHOD SPELLING IS NOT THE FREE NAME: `x.chars(s: y)` beside a free `chars(s: x)` relabels only the free call (review
// 82002's specimen). The method's label keeps `s:`.
fn roster_control_label_method_spelling(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  let before = "module c.method\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, collection_count_shape }\n\nfn f(x: String, y: Box) -> Int {\n  count(xs: chars(s: x)) + y.chars(s: x)\n}\n"
  let after = "module c.method\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, collection_count_shape }\nimport std.host_text { chars }\n\nfn f(x: String, y: Box) -> Int {\n  count(xs: chars(text: x)) + y.chars(s: x)\n}\n"
  match roster_applied(before: before, outcome: roster_sweep_text(path: "control/method.dag", text: before, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)) {
    RosterApplyRefused { reason: r } => "CONTROL-FAIL label-method-spelling: refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + "\n"
    RosterApplyWritten { content: c } => if c == after { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL label-method-spelling: the method call's label was renamed, or the free call's was not\n" }
  }
}

// THE #14338 CELLS, PINNED TO THE FIX: a module whose only mention of a row's name is a call of a name its own scope
// binds must sweep CLEAN -- no import, no label edit. Both fixtures below predate the position axis and demanded a
// refusal instead; that premise was the DEFECT, not the invariant. Measured, the sweep never wants a row for them at all: their `chars` mentions are the LABEL
// spelling in a signature row plus a call head read value/frame (executed on #14435:
// "| type/unbound | return/unbound | return/unbound | label/unbound | label/unbound | value/unbound | value/frame |
// ... OUTCOME=Clean"). With the position issuer switched off (the fix-off arm) the signature spelling reads a value
// position, the import comes back, and these two go red -- the revert arm for the collector's own fix.
fn roster_control_sweeps_clean_locally_bound(name: String, text: String, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  match roster_sweep_text(path: "control/" + name + ".dag", text: text, prepared: prepared, lex: lex) {
    RosterClean => ""
    RosterRefused { reason: r } => "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + "; a module whose row-name mention is a locally bound call must sweep clean\n"
    RosterEdit { start: _, end: _, text: t, own_line: _ } => "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": import proposed for a locally bound name: " + t + "\n"
    RosterLabelEdits { edits: edits } => "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": " + int_to_decimal_string(value: length(xs: edits)) + " label edits proposed for a locally bound name\n"
    RosterEditWithLabels { start: _, end: _, text: t, own_line: _, labels: labels } => "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": import and " + int_to_decimal_string(value: length(xs: labels)) + " label edits proposed for a locally bound name: " + t + "\n"
  }
}

// THE D4 CONTROLS ON THE ROSTER SIDE (tidy-ant-251, msg_e59d873e item 2 / msg_717e069d D4), three specimens over ONE
// row of v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep roster_head_rows (call `count` @ std.algebra) so the sweep is genuinely looking
// for the name and Clean can never be true because the row is inert:
//   imported tag  `count.Yes { n: k }` with count imported -> the head is HeadBindingUndecided at a pattern tag position:
//                 never a row. The previous PR head made exactly this head an acquisition CANDIDATE (it read a non-value
//                 position as "not a value, therefore a candidate"); v2.compiler.module_acquisition keeps it a
//                 non-candidate from the binding fact alone, and no roster row may say otherwise.
//   unbound tag   the same body without the import -> still no row: v2.workflow.roster_home_kind gives Label and
//                 PatternTag NO matching declaration kind, so the sweep never imports for a tag position. That does not
//                 strand the program: the head is still an acquisition candidate (module_acquisition reads the binding
//                 fact only, and its own control a_member_ordinary_imported_qualified_tag_... pins that side).
//   value call    `count(xs: xs)` with no import -> the row's import IS the fix, so the two Clean results above cannot
//                 be satisfied by a sweep that never fires.
fn roster_control_imported_qualified_tag(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  roster_control_d4_clean(name: "d4-imported-tag", text: roster_d4_tag_subject(with_import: true), prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
}

fn roster_control_unbound_qualified_tag(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  roster_control_d4_clean(name: "d4-unbound-tag", text: roster_d4_tag_subject(with_import: false), prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
}

fn roster_control_d4_clean(name: String, text: String, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  match roster_sweep_text(path: "control/" + name + ".dag", text: text, prepared: prepared, lex: lex) {
    RosterClean => ""
    RosterRefused { reason: reason } => "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: reason) + "\n"
    RosterEdit { start: _, end: _, text: t, own_line: _ } => "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": import proposed at a pattern tag position: " + t + "\n"
    RosterLabelEdits { edits: edits } => "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": " + int_to_decimal_string(value: length(xs: edits)) + " label edits proposed at a pattern tag position\n"
    RosterEditWithLabels { start: _, end: _, text: t, own_line: _, labels: _ } => "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": import and label edits proposed at a pattern tag position: " + t + "\n"
  }
}

// THE LIVE POSITIVE OF THE PAIR: the same row's name at a value position, unbound, must still produce its import.
fn roster_control_d4_value_call_positive(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  match roster_sweep_text(path: "control/d4-value.dag", text: "module c.d4.value\n\nfn f(xs: List<String>) -> Int {\n  count(xs: xs)\n}\n", prepared: prepared, lex: lex) {
    RosterEdit { start: _, end: _, text: t, own_line: _ } =>
      // The expected text carries the LEADING NEWLINE the sweep itself emits: this specimen has no import line, so the
      // first import anchors after the parsed module header (roster_module_header_end) as its own line (#14486). Pinning
      // the text WITHOUT it would pin the pre-#14486 shape and pass only if the anchor regressed.
      if t == "\nimport std.algebra { collection_count_shape }" { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL d4-value-positive: proposed [" + t + "] instead of [\nimport std.algebra { collection_count_shape }]\n" }
    RosterClean => "CONTROL-FAIL d4-value-positive: a free value-position call of a row's name swept Clean -- the free-name reading moved\n"
    RosterRefused { reason: reason } => "CONTROL-FAIL d4-value-positive: refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: reason) + "\n"
    RosterLabelEdits { edits: edits } => "CONTROL-FAIL d4-value-positive: " + int_to_decimal_string(value: length(xs: edits)) + " label edits instead of the import\n"
    RosterEditWithLabels { start: _, end: _, text: t, own_line: _, labels: _ } => "CONTROL-FAIL d4-value-positive: " + t + " with label edits, expected the import alone\n"
  }
}

// THE SUBJECT OF THE PAIR: one source, the import as the only difference, so the two controls cannot drift apart.
fn roster_d4_tag_subject(with_import: Bool) -> String {
  if with_import {
    "module c.d4.tag\n\nimport std.algebra { count }\n\nfn f(o: Slot) -> Int {\n  match o {\n    count.Yes { n: k } => k\n    count.No => 0\n  }\n}\n"
  } else {
    "module c.d4.untag\n\nfn f(o: Slot) -> Int {\n  match o {\n    count.Yes { n: k } => k\n    count.No => 0\n  }\n}\n"
  }
}

// THE GUARD IS DISSOLVED: a module that binds a row's name in one function and calls it free in another gets the import for
// the free call (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode a_roster_sweep_counts_a_bound_or_label_spelling_as_an_unbound_call). One binder
// form per control, each paired with a free call in a sibling function so Clean cannot be satisfied by an inert row: a
// parameter, a `let` (whose declaring occurrence is no site), and a match-arm record pun (UNDECIDED by design, never counted).
// The parameter cell: the label plan joins each parse-tree head to the collector's own verdict on the SAME occurrence (by source
// offset, refusing any head it cannot place), so the bound `chars` in `h(s: chars)` is a head the collector explains as bound, not a disagreement.
fn roster_control_free_call_beside_param(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  roster_control_imports_for_free_call(name: "free-call-beside-param", text: "module c.guard\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(x: String) -> Int {\n  chars(s: x)\n}\n\nfn g(chars: Int) -> Int {\n  h(s: chars)\n}\n", needle: "import std.host_text { chars }", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
}

// The bound head precedes the free one here: a join by position in a list would pair them wrongly; the offset join must not.
fn roster_control_free_call_after_param(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  roster_control_imports_for_free_call(name: "free-call-after-param", text: "module c.guard2\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn g(chars: Int) -> Int {\n  h(s: chars)\n}\n\nfn f(x: String) -> Int {\n  chars(s: x)\n}\n", needle: "import std.host_text { chars }", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
}

// Nested free calls in one fn beside a parameter: outer/inner order must pair the same way in both trees.
fn roster_control_nested_call_beside_param(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  roster_control_imports_for_free_call(name: "nested-call-beside-param", text: "module c.guard3\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn g(chars: Int) -> Int {\n  h(s: chars)\n}\n\nfn f(x: String) -> Int {\n  chars(s: chars(s: x))\n}\n", needle: "import std.host_text { chars }", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
}

// Restored from #14338 with its result restated (review 85013): a nested free call that is also a label-carrying row,
// beside a parameter of the same name used as a value. The free call imports and relabels; the bound value is untouched.
fn roster_control_label_bound_occurrence(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  let before = "module c.bound\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, collection_count_shape }\n\nfn f(x: String) -> Int {\n  count(xs: chars(s: x))\n}\n\nfn g(chars: Int) -> Int {\n  h(s: chars)\n}\n"
  let after = "module c.bound\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, collection_count_shape }\nimport std.host_text { chars }\n\nfn f(x: String) -> Int {\n  count(xs: chars(text: x))\n}\n\nfn g(chars: Int) -> Int {\n  h(s: chars)\n}\n"
  match roster_applied(before: before, outcome: roster_sweep_text(path: "control/bound.dag", text: before, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)) {
    RosterApplyWritten { content: c } => if c == after { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL label-bound-occurrence: wrote [" + c + "]\n" }
    RosterApplyRefused { reason: r } => "CONTROL-FAIL label-bound-occurrence: refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + "\n"
  }
}

fn roster_control_free_call_beside_let(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  roster_control_imports_for_free_call(name: "free-call-beside-let", text: "module c.guardlet\n\nfn f(x: String) -> Int {\n  count(xs: x)\n}\n\nfn k() -> Int {\n  let count = 0\n  count\n}\n", needle: "import std.algebra { collection_count_shape }", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
}

fn roster_control_free_call_beside_pun(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  roster_control_imports_for_free_call(name: "free-call-beside-pun", text: "module c.guardpun\n\nfn f(v: Thing) -> Int {\n  match v {\n    Dup { count } => count\n    Other => 0\n  }\n}\n\nfn g(xs: List<Int>) -> Int {\n  count(xs: xs)\n}\n", needle: "import std.algebra { collection_count_shape }", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
}

fn roster_control_imports_for_free_call(name: String, text: String, needle: String, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  match roster_sweep_text(path: "control/" + name + ".dag", text: text, prepared: prepared, lex: lex) {
    RosterEdit { start: _, end: _, text: t, own_line: _ } =>
      if string_contains(s: t, pattern: needle) { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": proposed [" + t + "] instead of [" + needle + "]\n" }
    RosterEditWithLabels { start: _, end: _, text: t, own_line: _, labels: _ } =>
      if string_contains(s: t, pattern: needle) { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": proposed [" + t + "] instead of [" + needle + "]\n" }
    RosterClean => "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": a genuine free call swept Clean beside a local binder of its name\n"
    RosterRefused { reason: r } => "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + "; a local binder of the name must not refuse a module with a free call\n"
    RosterLabelEdits { edits: _ } => "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": label edits with no import\n"
  }
}

fn roster_control_specimen(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  roster_control_sweeps_clean_locally_bound(name: "specimen", text: "module c.spec\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, collection_join_shape }\n\nfn v(s: String, chars: List<String>) -> String {\n  join(chars, \"\")\n}\n\nfn w(s: String) -> String {\n  v(s: s, chars: [])\n}\n", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
}

fn roster_control_called_parameter(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  roster_control_sweeps_clean_locally_bound(name: "called-parameter", text: "module c.called\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn u(chars: fn(String) -> Int, x: String) -> Int {\n  chars(s: x)\n}\n", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
}

// A NESTED CALL'S LABEL IS NOT THE OUTER CALL'S: chars(s: g(s: x)) relabels only chars's own direct argument; the inner g's
// s: is an argument of g (the stopping rule of v2.extdeps.languages.dag dag_call_direct_arg_slots).
fn roster_control_nested_call_label(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  let before = "module c.nested\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, collection_count_shape }\n\nfn f(x: String) -> Int {\n  count(xs: chars(s: g(s: x)))\n}\n"
  let after = "module c.nested\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, collection_count_shape }\nimport std.host_text { chars }\n\nfn f(x: String) -> Int {\n  count(xs: chars(text: g(s: x)))\n}\n"
  match roster_applied(before: before, outcome: roster_sweep_text(path: "control/nested.dag", text: before, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)) {
    RosterApplyWritten { content: c } => if c == after { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL nested-call-label: the inner call's label was renamed, or the outer call's was not\n" }
    RosterApplyRefused { reason: r } => "CONTROL-FAIL nested-call-label: refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + "\n"
  }
}

// THE COUNT-AGREEMENT DISCRIMINATOR, with NO local binder named chars : chars
// also occurs in a TYPE position, `y: chars`, which the reference-site collector records as a free site but which is not a
// primary-expression head, so the two counts disagree and the label plan must refuse exactly label-sites-ambiguous.
fn roster_control_label_sites_disagree(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  match roster_sweep_text(path: "control/disagree.dag", text: "module c.disagree\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, collection_count_shape }\n\nfn f(x: String, y: chars) -> Int {\n  count(xs: chars(s: x))\n}\n", prepared: prepared, lex: lex) {
    RosterEditWithLabels { start: _, end: _, text: t, own_line: _, labels: labels } =>
      if t == "import std.host_text { chars }" && length(xs: labels) == 1 { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL label-sites-disagree: import [" + t + "] with " + int_to_decimal_string(value: length(xs: labels)) + " label edits, expected the chars import with exactly 1\n" }
    RosterClean => "CONTROL-FAIL label-sites-disagree: the free call head of chars no longer wants its import -- the free-name reading moved\n"
    RosterEdit { start: _, end: _, text: t, own_line: _ } => "CONTROL-FAIL label-sites-disagree: import [" + t + "] with no label edit\n"
    RosterLabelEdits { edits: edits } => "CONTROL-FAIL label-sites-disagree: " + int_to_decimal_string(value: length(xs: edits)) + " label edits with no import\n"
    RosterRefused { reason: r } => "CONTROL-FAIL label-sites-disagree: refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + "; the type-position annotation `y: chars` must not be counted as a free site\n"
  }
}

// THE SECOND PASS OVER THE APPLIED EDIT (review 83367c). Pass 1 above plans the chars import AND the label rename in one
// write; the file it lands is re-swept here, and the imported `chars` heads read HeadBindingUndecided -- the branch this
// review caught skipping the position-x-kind check. With the fix, only the CALL head (Value position, value home) stays a
// candidate: pass 2 = Clean, `y: chars` untouched, exactly the call's label renamed (pass 1 already landed it). With the
// branch reverted to the unconditional KindMatched, the imported annotation head joins the candidates, the label plan
// counts 2 free against 1 primary head, and pass 2 refuses LabelsAmbiguous -- RED -- while pass 1 stays green (its heads
// are unbound, not undecided). That pair of outcomes is the whole point: the imported branch is exercised where it is
// load-bearing, and no second filter in this module decides what the authority already decided.
fn roster_control_label_pass2_clean(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  let before = "module c.disagree\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons, collection_count_shape }\n\nfn f(x: String, y: chars) -> Int {\n  count(xs: chars(s: x))\n}\n"
  match roster_sweep_text(path: "control/disagree.dag", text: before, prepared: prepared, lex: lex) {
    RosterEditWithLabels { start: _, end: _, text: t, own_line: _, labels: labels } =>
      if t != "import std.host_text { chars }" || length(xs: labels) != 1 {
        "CONTROL-FAIL label-pass2-clean: pass 1 planned [" + t + "] with " + int_to_decimal_string(value: length(xs: labels)) + " labels\n"
      } else {
        match roster_applied(before: before, outcome: roster_sweep_text(path: "control/disagree.dag", text: before, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)) {
          RosterApplyRefused { reason: r } => "CONTROL-FAIL label-pass2-clean: applying pass 1 refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + "\n"
          RosterApplyWritten { content: after } =>
            if !string_contains(s: after, pattern: "import std.host_text { chars }") {
              "CONTROL-FAIL label-pass2-clean: the applied file lost the chars import\n"
            } else if !string_contains(s: after, pattern: "y: chars") {
              "CONTROL-FAIL label-pass2-clean: the applied file edited the type-position annotation `y: chars`\n"
            } else if !string_contains(s: after, pattern: "chars(text: x)") {
              "CONTROL-FAIL label-pass2-clean: the applied file did not rename the call's label to text:\n"
            } else {
              // THE FIXPOINT: pass 2 must be EXACTLY Clean (side-chat review v14435, item 1). Any further import or any
              // non-empty label edit is RED -- pass 1 landed every edit this fixture wants, so a pass-2 sweep that still
              // PLANS something is re-opening a row the applied file already settled, not converging. It also never
              // REFUSES: LabelsAmbiguous at pass 2 is exactly the imported annotation head joining the label candidates,
              // the defect this control exists to catch (the OFF-UNDECIDED flip turns this arm RED). The fixture is the
              // chars row: pass 1 imports chars and renames the call's label; every other head (the imported `count` at
              // its declared label `xs`) needs nothing, so RosterClean is the only outcome the sweep's own fixpoint
              // produces. No isolation of the fixture is needed to reach it -- measured, not assumed.
              match roster_sweep_text(path: "control/disagree.dag", text: after, prepared: prepared, lex: lex) {
                RosterClean => ""
                RosterRefused { reason: r } => "CONTROL-FAIL label-pass2-clean: re-sweeping the applied file refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + " -- the imported annotation head is being counted as a free candidate\n"
                RosterEdit { start: _, end: _, text: t2, own_line: _ } => "CONTROL-FAIL label-pass2-clean: re-sweeping the applied file planned a FURTHER import [" + t2 + "] -- pass 2 is the fixpoint and must be exactly Clean\n"
                RosterLabelEdits { edits: e } => "CONTROL-FAIL label-pass2-clean: re-sweeping the applied file planned " + int_to_decimal_string(value: length(xs: e)) + " FURTHER label edits -- pass 2 is the fixpoint and must be exactly Clean\n"
                RosterEditWithLabels { start: _, end: _, text: t2, own_line: _, labels: l } => "CONTROL-FAIL label-pass2-clean: re-sweeping the applied file planned a FURTHER import [" + t2 + "] with " + int_to_decimal_string(value: length(xs: l)) + " labels -- pass 2 is the fixpoint and must be exactly Clean\n"
              }
            }
        }
      }
    RosterClean => "CONTROL-FAIL label-pass2-clean: pass 1 came back Clean; the fixture no longer exercises the imported-head path\n"
    RosterEdit { start: _, end: _, text: t, own_line: _ } => "CONTROL-FAIL label-pass2-clean: pass 1 planned [" + t + "] with no label edit; pass 2 has nothing to exercise\n"
    RosterLabelEdits { edits: e } => "CONTROL-FAIL label-pass2-clean: pass 1 planned only " + int_to_decimal_string(value: length(xs: e)) + " label edits\n"
    RosterRefused { reason: r } => "CONTROL-FAIL label-pass2-clean: pass 1 refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + "\n"
  }
}

// A POSITIONAL READ PAST AN UNREADABLE ARGUMENT keeps its slot (v2.extdeps.languages.dag dag_call_direct_arg_slots). Both
// unreadable kinds parse_production_captured_child_optional maps to Absent are covered: a MISSING capture and an AMBIGUOUS one
// (two captured edges). Each is followed by a valid positional argument that must not be selected for the unreadable slot.
// The call's direct arguments are readable, missing, readable, ambiguous, readable -- a shape no parse produces, so they are
// SUPPLIED here, at the producer's own interface: positions 1 and 3 answer Absent, positions 2 and 4 answer their own
// arguments, never a neighbour. Dropping unreadable slots shifted every later position (side chat on #14338).
type RosterSynthCapture
  = SynthCaptured { node: Node }
  | SynthCaptureMissing
  | SynthCaptureAmbiguous { first: Node, second: Node }

// THE DISJOINT-EDIT CONTROLS, at the invariant's own interface (supplied edit plans; the planner's real route reaches it
// through every rename and label control above). REDs: two zero-width insertions at one offset, and a replacement that
// covers another edit's start. Positives: the rename shape (an insertion at a replacement's start, then insertions after
// it) and two adjacent replacements.
fn roster_control_edits_disjoint_verdicts() -> List<RosterControlVerdict> {
  [
    roster_control_verdict(name: "edits-coincide", fail: roster_edits_disjoint_expect(name: "edits-coincide", edits: [roster_edit_insert(at: 4), roster_edit_insert(at: 4)], want: "edits-coincide at=4")),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "edits-overlap", fail: roster_edits_disjoint_expect(name: "edits-overlap", edits: [roster_edit_replace(start: 2, end: 9), roster_edit_replace(start: 5, end: 7)], want: "edits-overlap start=5 end=7 covered-to=9")),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "edits-insert-inside-replacement", fail: roster_edits_disjoint_expect(name: "edits-insert-inside-replacement", edits: [roster_edit_replace(start: 2, end: 9), roster_edit_insert(at: 5)], want: "edits-overlap start=5 end=5 covered-to=9")),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "edits-rename-shape", fail: roster_edits_disjoint_expect(name: "edits-rename-shape", edits: [roster_edit_insert(at: 3), roster_edit_replace(start: 3, end: 10), roster_edit_insert(at: 11), roster_edit_insert(at: 15)], want: "")),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "import-and-label-coincide", fail: roster_import_labels_expect(name: "import-and-label-coincide", start: 30, end: 30, labels: [roster_edit_insert(at: 30)], want: "edits-coincide at=30")),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "import-then-label-disjoint", fail: roster_import_labels_expect(name: "import-then-label-disjoint", start: 30, end: 30, labels: [roster_edit_insert(at: 41)], want: "")),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "edits-adjacent-replacements", fail: roster_edits_disjoint_expect(name: "edits-adjacent-replacements", edits: [roster_edit_replace(start: 0, end: 4), roster_edit_replace(start: 4, end: 8)], want: "")),
    // THE PIPE SITE'S THREE EDITS are half-open neighbours: the connector [l, h) ends where the relocated head [h, h+n) starts,
    // which ends where the paren [h+n, h+n+1) starts. Adjacency is admitted; an overlap of one byte refuses.
    roster_control_verdict(name: "edits-pipe-three-adjacent", fail: roster_edits_disjoint_expect(name: "edits-pipe-three-adjacent", edits: [roster_edit_replace(start: 2, end: 6), roster_edit_replace(start: 6, end: 13), roster_edit_replace(start: 13, end: 14)], want: "")),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "edits-connector-overlaps-head-by-one", fail: roster_edits_disjoint_expect(name: "edits-connector-overlaps-head-by-one", edits: [roster_edit_replace(start: 2, end: 7), roster_edit_replace(start: 6, end: 13)], want: "edits-overlap start=6 end=13 covered-to=7")),
    roster_control_verdict(name: "relocation-splice", fail: roster_relocation_splice_controls())
  ]
}

// THE RELOCATION AT THE SPLICE: the head is removed and `to` then `suffix` is written at insert_at, operands untouched. A
// relocation whose text does not begin with the head has no construction (RosterHeadRelocation holds the head and its suffix),
// so it has no RED here; the splice's own REDs (a `from` the bytes do not hold, an extent off a scalar boundary) apply to it.
fn roster_relocation_splice_controls() -> String {
  let before = "m |> map_get(k)"
  let good = [RosterLabelEdit { start: 5, end: 12, from: "map_get", to: "", relocation: Present { value: RosterHeadRelocation { insert_at: 0, to: "map_lookup", suffix: "(m: " } } }, RosterLabelEdit { start: 1, end: 5, from: " |> ", to: "", relocation: Absent }, RosterLabelEdit { start: 12, end: 13, from: "(", to: ", key: ", relocation: Absent }]
  // The removed head must be the bytes it names: a relocation whose `from` the source does not hold refuses at the splice.
  let stale = [RosterLabelEdit { start: 5, end: 12, from: "map_set", to: "", relocation: Present { value: RosterHeadRelocation { insert_at: 0, to: "map_lookup", suffix: "(m: " } } }]
  let sorted = list_sort_by_key(xs: good, key: roster_label_edit_order_key, order: int_total_order())
  let good_text = match roster_label_splices(before: before, edits: sorted) {
    RosterApplyWritten { content: c } => if c == "map_lookup(m: m, key: k)" { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL relocation-splice: wrote " + c + "\n" }
    RosterApplyRefused { reason: r } => "CONTROL-FAIL relocation-splice: refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + "\n"
  }
  let stale_text = match roster_label_splices(before: before, edits: stale) {
    RosterApplyRefused { reason: r } => if roster_refusal_text(reason: r) == "extent-mismatch" { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL relocation-splice-stale-head: refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + "\n" }
    RosterApplyWritten { content: c } => "CONTROL-FAIL relocation-splice-stale-head: wrote " + c + "\n"
  }
  good_text + stale_text
}

fn roster_import_labels_expect(name: String, start: Int, end: Int, labels: List<RosterLabelEdit>, want: String) -> String {
  let got = match roster_import_and_labels_disjoint(start: start, end: end, text: "import std.algebra { map_lookup }", labels: labels) {
    Present { value: r } => roster_refusal_text(reason: r)
    Absent => ""
  }
  if got == want { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": want '" + want + "', got '" + got + "'\n" }
}

fn roster_edit_insert(at: Int) -> RosterLabelEdit {
  RosterLabelEdit { start: at, end: at, from: "", to: "k: ", relocation: Absent }
}

fn roster_edit_replace(start: Int, end: Int) -> RosterLabelEdit {
  RosterLabelEdit { start: start, end: end, from: "x", to: "y", relocation: Absent }
}

fn roster_edits_disjoint_expect(name: String, edits: List<RosterLabelEdit>, want: String) -> String {
  let got = match roster_label_edits_disjoint(edits: edits) {
    LabelsRenameRefused { reason: r } => roster_refusal_text(reason: r)
    LabelsSelected { edits: _ } => ""
    LabelsAmbiguous => "ambiguous"
  }
  if got == want { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": want '" + want + "', got '" + got + "'\n" }
}

fn roster_control_positional_past_unreadable() -> String {
  let call = roster_synth_conj(children: [
    Edge { label: Positional, target: roster_synth_arg(capture: SynthCaptured { node: roster_synth_atom(id: ^roster_slot_first) }), declaration: NotADeclaration },
    Edge { label: Positional, target: roster_synth_arg(capture: SynthCaptureMissing), declaration: NotADeclaration },
    Edge { label: Positional, target: roster_synth_arg(capture: SynthCaptured { node: roster_synth_atom(id: ^roster_slot_third) }), declaration: NotADeclaration },
    Edge { label: Positional, target: roster_synth_arg(capture: SynthCaptureAmbiguous { first: roster_synth_atom(id: ^roster_slot_ambiguous_a), second: roster_synth_atom(id: ^roster_slot_ambiguous_b) }), declaration: NotADeclaration },
    Edge { label: Positional, target: roster_synth_arg(capture: SynthCaptured { node: roster_synth_atom(id: ^roster_slot_fifth) }), declaration: NotADeclaration }
  ])
  if roster_position_absent(call: call, position: 1)
    && roster_position_is(call: call, position: 2, want: ^roster_slot_third)
    && roster_position_absent(call: call, position: 3)
    && roster_position_is(call: call, position: 4, want: ^roster_slot_fifth) {
    ""
  } else {
    "CONTROL-FAIL positional-past-unreadable: a positional read past a missing or ambiguous capture shifted onto its neighbour\n"
  }
}

fn roster_position_absent(call: Node, position: Int) -> Bool {
  match dag_call_positional_arg_value_optional(node: call, position: position) { Absent => true  Present { value: _ } => false }
}

fn roster_position_is(call: Node, position: Int, want: Symbol) -> Bool {
  match dag_call_positional_arg_value_optional(node: call, position: position) {
    Present { value: n } => match node_atom_identity_optional(node: n) { Present { value: id } => id == want  Absent => false }
    Absent => false
  }
}

fn roster_synth_atom(id: Symbol) -> Node {
  Node { kind: TypeNode { connective: Atom { identity: id } }, children: [], occurrence_id: OccurrenceSynthetic }
}

fn roster_synth_conj(children: List<Edge>) -> Node {
  Node { kind: TypeNode { connective: Conj }, children: children, occurrence_id: OccurrenceSynthetic }
}

fn roster_synth_captured_edge(target: Node) -> Edge {
  Edge { label: Authored { name: ^grammar_production_captured_node_projection }, target: target, declaration: NotADeclaration }
}

// An ^dag_surface_arg production: its identity edge, and zero, one or two captured edges.
fn roster_synth_arg(capture: RosterSynthCapture) -> Node {
  let identity = Edge { label: Authored { name: ^grammar_production_identity_node_projection }, target: roster_synth_atom(id: ^dag_surface_arg), declaration: NotADeclaration }
  match capture {
    SynthCaptured { node: c } => roster_synth_conj(children: [identity, roster_synth_captured_edge(target: c)])
    SynthCaptureMissing => roster_synth_conj(children: [identity])
    SynthCaptureAmbiguous { first: a, second: b } => roster_synth_conj(children: [identity, roster_synth_captured_edge(target: a), roster_synth_captured_edge(target: b)])
  }
}

// A MODULE THAT DECLARES ITS OWN chars is not a caller of the home: no import is needed, so no label is renamed.
fn roster_control_label_local_call(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  match roster_sweep_text(path: "control/local.dag", text: "module c.local\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn chars(s: String) -> Int {\n  1\n}\n\nfn f(x: String) -> Int {\n  chars(s: x)\n}\n", prepared: prepared, lex: lex) {
    RosterClean => ""
    _ => "CONTROL-FAIL label-local-call: a module-local chars was swept\n"
  }
}

fn roster_control_homonym(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  match roster_sweep_text(path: "control/homonym.dag", text: "module c.homonym\n\nimport examples.decoy { collection_concat_shape }\n\nfn f(xs: List<String>, ys: List<String>) -> List<String> {\n  concat(a: xs, b: ys)\n}\n", prepared: prepared, lex: lex) {
    RosterRefused { reason: reason } =>
      if roster_refusal_text(reason: reason) == "shape-name-bound-elsewhere" { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL homonym: refused for " + roster_refusal_text(reason: reason) + "\n" }
    _ => "CONTROL-FAIL homonym: a shape name bound to another declaration was not refused as a conflict\n"
  }
}

// A ONE-NAME WAVE TOUCHES ONLY ITS ROW (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode a_one_home_sweep_moves_every_row_of_that_home).
// Each fixture is swept twice over std.algebra: OnlyCall is the wave's grain and must be narrow; EveryRowOfHome is the
// old one-home grain and must show the defect, so the pair discriminates.
//   wider-row-set: a free count call beside a free concat call. OnlyCall count imports collection_count_shape and NOT
//     collection_concat_shape; the whole home imports both.
//   wrong-row-refusal: count is a parameter in one fn and a free call in another, beside a free concat call. OnlyCall
//     concat imports collection_concat_shape and NOT collection_count_shape; the whole home also imports
//     collection_count_shape for h's free count, a name the concat wave never moves. (This arm once expected the whole
//     home to refuse home-name-locally-bound; that guard is deleted and the offset join leaves g's parameter alone.)
fn roster_control_row_scope(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  let wider = "module c.rowscope.wider\n\nfn f(xs: List<String>, ys: List<String>) -> Int {\n  count(xs: concat(a: xs, b: ys))\n}\n"
  let wrong = "module c.rowscope.wrong\n\nfn g(count: Int) -> Int {\n  count\n}\n\nfn h(xs: List<String>, ys: List<String>) -> Int {\n  count(xs: concat(a: xs, b: ys))\n}\n"
  let algebra = qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.algebra")
  roster_row_scope_import(name: "wider-row-set/row", text: wider, scope: OneHome { home: algebra, rows: OnlyCall { call: "count" } }, wants: "collection_count_shape", forbids: "collection_concat_shape", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
    + roster_row_scope_import(name: "wider-row-set/home", text: wider, scope: OneHome { home: algebra, rows: EveryRowOfHome }, wants: "collection_concat_shape", forbids: "", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
    + roster_row_scope_import(name: "wrong-row-refusal/row", text: wrong, scope: OneHome { home: algebra, rows: OnlyCall { call: "concat" } }, wants: "collection_concat_shape", forbids: "collection_count_shape", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
    + roster_row_scope_import(name: "wrong-row-refusal/home", text: wrong, scope: OneHome { home: algebra, rows: EveryRowOfHome }, wants: "collection_count_shape", forbids: "", prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
}

// A SCOPE THAT SELECTS NOTHING REFUSES, it never reads as converged (side chat on #14883). Each RED goes through the real
// entry; the apply RED runs at a nonexistent root, so a selection refusal (and not apply-lock-unavailable) proves the check
// precedes the lock. The positive control is the same entry with a selecting call reaching the files.
fn roster_control_scope_selects_its_row() -> String {
  let algebra = qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.algebra")
  let count_row = RosterHeadRow { call: "count", key: "count", import_name: "collection_count_shape", home: algebra, labels: [], head: KeepHead }
  roster_scope_exit_refuses(name: "misspelled-call", exit: roster_import_sweep_row_exit(paths_csv: "control/none.dag", home: "std.algebra", call: "cuont"), refusal: RefusalScopeSelectsNoRow { home: "std.algebra", selection: "call=cuont" })
    + roster_scope_exit_refuses(name: "wrong-home", exit: roster_import_sweep_row_exit(paths_csv: "control/none.dag", home: "std.host_text", call: "count"), refusal: RefusalScopeSelectsNoRow { home: "std.host_text", selection: "call=count" })
    + roster_scope_exit_refuses(name: "unknown-home", exit: roster_import_sweep_home_exit(paths_csv: "control/none.dag", home: "std.no_such_home"), refusal: RefusalScopeSelectsNoRow { home: "std.no_such_home", selection: "every-row" })
    + roster_scope_exit_refuses(name: "apply-before-lock", exit: roster_import_sweep_apply_row_exit(root_dir: "/nonexistent-roster-control-root", paths_csv: "control/none.dag", home: "std.algebra", call: "cuont"), refusal: RefusalScopeSelectsNoRow { home: "std.algebra", selection: "call=cuont" })
    + roster_scope_exit_refuses(name: "selecting-call", exit: roster_import_sweep_row_exit(paths_csv: "control/none.dag", home: "std.algebra", call: "count"), refusal: RefusalUnreadable)
    + match roster_scope_selection_refusal_in(table: [count_row, count_row], scope: OneHome { home: algebra, rows: OnlyCall { call: "count" } }) {
        Present { value: r } =>
          if roster_refusal_text(reason: r) == roster_refusal_text(reason: RefusalScopeSelectsSeveralRows { home: "std.algebra", call: "count", count: 2 }) { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL scope-selection several-rows: refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + "\n" }
        Absent => "CONTROL-FAIL scope-selection several-rows: an OnlyCall over two rows was admitted\n"
      }
    + match roster_scope_selection_refusal_in(table: [count_row], scope: OneHome { home: algebra, rows: OnlyCall { call: "count" } }) {
        Present { value: r } => "CONTROL-FAIL scope-selection one-row: refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + "\n"
        Absent => ""
      }
}

// The refusal row the entry must exit with, compared as the exact rendered reason (the run's verdict IS its rows).
fn roster_scope_exit_refuses(name: String, exit: ProcessExit, refusal: RosterRefusalReason) -> String {
  let path = match refusal {
    RefusalUnreadable => "control/none.dag"
    _ => "*"
  }
  if roster_exit_reason_is(exit: exit, reason: roster_refuse_row(path: path, reason: refusal)) { "" } else {
    match exit {
      ExitSuccess => "CONTROL-FAIL scope-selection " + name + ": succeeded, expected " + roster_refusal_text(reason: refusal) + "\n"
      ExitFailure { code: _, reason: r } => "CONTROL-FAIL scope-selection " + name + ": exited " + r + ", expected " + roster_refusal_text(reason: refusal) + "\n"
    }
  }
}

fn roster_row_scope_outcome(name: String, text: String, scope: RosterHomeScope, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> RosterOutcome {
  roster_sweep_text_scoped(sides: roster_home_sides(rows: roster_rows_for_scope(scope: scope)), companions: [], path: "control/" + name + ".dag", text: text, prepared: prepared, lex: lex, scope: scope, closures: roster_control_closures())
}

fn roster_row_scope_import(name: String, text: String, scope: RosterHomeScope, wants: String, forbids: String, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  match roster_row_scope_outcome(name: name, text: text, scope: scope, prepared: prepared, lex: lex) {
    RosterEdit { start: _, end: _, text: t, own_line: _ } => roster_row_scope_import_text(name: name, t: t, wants: wants, forbids: forbids)
    RosterEditWithLabels { start: _, end: _, text: t, own_line: _, labels: _ } => roster_row_scope_import_text(name: name, t: t, wants: wants, forbids: forbids)
    RosterRefused { reason: r } => "CONTROL-FAIL row-scope " + name + ": refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + "\n"
    RosterClean => "CONTROL-FAIL row-scope " + name + ": Clean, no import planned\n"
    RosterLabelEdits { edits: _ } => "CONTROL-FAIL row-scope " + name + ": only label edits\n"
  }
}

fn roster_row_scope_import_text(name: String, t: String, wants: String, forbids: String) -> String {
  if !string_contains(s: t, pattern: wants) {
    "CONTROL-FAIL row-scope " + name + ": import " + t + " lacks " + wants + "\n"
  } else if forbids != "" && string_contains(s: t, pattern: forbids) {
    "CONTROL-FAIL row-scope " + name + ": import " + t + " carries " + forbids + ", a row outside the run's scope\n"
  } else {
    ""
  }
}

// AN IMPORT THAT WOULD CLOSE A CYCLE IS REFUSED, NAMED, AND NEVER EMITTED. The pair differs only in whether the swept
// module is in the home's closure: inside it, the refusal names home and module; outside it, the same text gets its import.
fn roster_control_import_closes_cycle(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  let text = "module c.cyc\n\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(x: String) -> Int {\n  count(xs: chars(s: x))\n}\n"
  let scope = OneHome { home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.host_text"), rows: EveryRowOfHome }
  let cyclic = [RosterClosureRead { home: "std.host_text", modules: ["std.host_text", "c.cyc"] }]
  let inside = match roster_sweep_text_scoped(sides: roster_home_sides(rows: roster_rows_for_scope(scope: scope)), companions: [], path: "control/cyc.dag", text: text, prepared: prepared, lex: lex, scope: scope, closures: cyclic) {
    RosterRefused { reason: r } =>
      if roster_refusal_text(reason: r) == "import-closes-cycle home=std.host_text module=c.cyc" { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL import-closes-cycle: refused for another reason " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + "\n" }
    _ => "CONTROL-FAIL import-closes-cycle: a cycle-closing import was not refused\n"
  }
  let outside = match roster_sweep_text_scoped(sides: roster_home_sides(rows: roster_rows_for_scope(scope: scope)), companions: [], path: "control/cyc.dag", text: text, prepared: prepared, lex: lex, scope: scope, closures: roster_control_closures()) {
    RosterEditWithLabels { start: _, end: _, text: _, own_line: _, labels: _ } => ""
    _ => "CONTROL-FAIL import-closes-cycle: the acyclic twin did not get its import\n"
  }
  let unread = match roster_sweep_text_scoped(sides: roster_home_sides(rows: roster_rows_for_scope(scope: scope)), companions: [], path: "control/cyc.dag", text: text, prepared: prepared, lex: lex, scope: scope, closures: []) {
    RosterRefused { reason: r } =>
      if roster_refusal_text(reason: r) == "home-closure-unread home=std.host_text" { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL import-closes-cycle: an unread closure refused for another reason\n" }
    _ => "CONTROL-FAIL import-closes-cycle: a home with no closure was assumed acyclic\n"
  }
  inside + outside + unread
}

// AN ALL-HOMES MUTATION REFUSES, TYPED, before any lock, read or write: the home-less apply entry has no scope to apply.
fn roster_control_apply_needs_one_home() -> String {
  match roster_import_sweep_apply_exit(root_dir: "/nonexistent-roster-control-root", paths_csv: "dag/std/types.dag") {
    ExitSuccess => "CONTROL-FAIL apply-needs-one-home: an all-homes apply succeeded\n"
    ExitFailure { code: c, reason: r } =>
      if roster_exit_reason_is(exit: ExitFailure { code: c, reason: r }, reason: roster_refuse_row(path: "*", reason: RefusalApplyNeedsOneHome)) { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL apply-needs-one-home: refused for another reason\n" }
  }
}

fn roster_exit_reason_is(exit: ProcessExit, reason: String) -> Bool {
  match exit {
    ExitSuccess => false
    ExitFailure { code: _, reason: r } => r == reason
  }
}

// THE INHABITANCE CLAIM for the supplied closures: the real producer, through the compiler's acquisition door, reads
// std.types' closure and it holds std.algebra (std.types defines List over std.algebra's FreeMonoid), so importing std.types
// into std.algebra is refused by the real path.
fn roster_control_closure_inhabited() -> String {
  match roster_cycle_refusal(closures: [roster_home_closure_read(home: "std.types", bindings: roster_repository_bindings(root: ""))], home: "std.types", module: "std.algebra") {
    Present { value: RefusalImportClosesCycle { home: _, module: _ } } => ""
    Present { value: r } => "CONTROL-FAIL closure-inhabited: the real closure of std.types refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + "\n"
    Absent => "CONTROL-FAIL closure-inhabited: the real closure of std.types does not hold std.algebra\n"
  }
}

// THE ROW PROTOCOL HOLDS FOR A MULTILINE REPLACEMENT: the outcome's EDIT row is one line and reads back to the edit's own
// start, end and replacement.
fn roster_control_edit_row_round_trip(outcome: RosterOutcome) -> String {
  match outcome {
    RosterEditWithLabels { start: st, end: en, text: tx, own_line: ol, labels: _ } =>
      if roster_edit_row_reads_back(row: roster_render_outcome(path: "control/bare.dag", outcome: RosterEdit { start: st, end: en, text: tx, own_line: ol }), start: st, end: en, replacement: roster_edit_replacement(text: tx, own_line: ol)) { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL no-import-anchor: the EDIT row does not read back to its edit\n" }
    RosterEdit { start: st, end: en, text: tx, own_line: ol } =>
      if roster_edit_row_reads_back(row: roster_render_outcome(path: "control/bare.dag", outcome: outcome), start: st, end: en, replacement: roster_edit_replacement(text: tx, own_line: ol)) { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL no-import-anchor: the EDIT row does not read back to its edit\n" }
    _ => "CONTROL-FAIL no-import-anchor: pass 1 is not an import edit\n"
  }
}

// A MODULE WITH NO IMPORT LINE is in reach: pass 1 writes exactly one import, directly after the module header and before
// the first top-level item, and leaves the header's own bytes untouched; pass 2 (the fixed point) is Clean.
fn roster_control_no_import_anchor(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  let before = "module c.bare\n\nfn f(x: String) -> Int {\n  count(xs: chars(s: x))\n}\n"
  let after = "module c.bare\n\nimport std.host_text { chars }\n\nfn f(x: String) -> Int {\n  count(xs: chars(text: x))\n}\n"
  let outcome = roster_sweep_text_scoped(sides: roster_home_sides(rows: roster_rows_for_scope(scope: OneHome { home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.host_text"), rows: EveryRowOfHome })), companions: [], path: "control/bare.dag", text: before, prepared: prepared, lex: lex, scope: OneHome { home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.host_text"), rows: EveryRowOfHome }, closures: roster_control_closures())
  let applied = match roster_applied(before: before, outcome: outcome) {
    RosterApplyRefused { reason: r } => "CONTROL-FAIL no-import-anchor: pass 1 refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + "\n"
    RosterApplyWritten { content: c1 } =>
      if c1 != after { "CONTROL-FAIL no-import-anchor: pass 1 did not write exactly one import after the module header\n" } else {
        match roster_sweep_text_scoped(sides: roster_home_sides(rows: roster_rows_for_scope(scope: OneHome { home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.host_text"), rows: EveryRowOfHome })), companions: [], path: "control/bare.dag", text: c1, prepared: prepared, lex: lex, scope: OneHome { home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.host_text"), rows: EveryRowOfHome }, closures: roster_control_closures()) {
          RosterClean => ""
          _ => "CONTROL-FAIL no-import-anchor: pass 2 is not Clean\n"
        }
      }
  }
  roster_control_edit_row_round_trip(outcome: outcome) + applied
}

fn roster_control_present(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  match roster_sweep_text(path: "control/present.dag", text: "module c.present\n\nimport std.algebra { collection_concat_shape }\n\nfn f(xs: List<String>, ys: List<String>) -> List<String> {\n  concat(a: xs, b: ys)\n}\n", prepared: prepared, lex: lex) {
    RosterClean => ""
    _ => "CONTROL-FAIL present: an existing std.algebra import was not recognised\n"
  }
}

fn roster_control_multibyte(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  let before = "module c.multibyte\n\n// 😀 é 日本 before the import\nimport std.algebra { Cons }\n\nfn f(xs: List<String>) -> Int {\n  count(xs: xs)\n}\n\nfn g() -> String {\n  \"tail 😀 é\"\n}\n"
  let expected = "module c.multibyte\n\n// 😀 é 日本 before the import\nimport std.algebra { Cons, collection_count_shape }\n\nfn f(xs: List<String>) -> Int {\n  count(xs: xs)\n}\n\nfn g() -> String {\n  \"tail 😀 é\"\n}\n"
  match roster_applied(before: before, outcome: roster_sweep_text(path: "control/multibyte.dag", text: before, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)) {
    RosterApplyWritten { content: content } =>
      if content == expected { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL multibyte: spliced text differs from the expected text outside or inside the extent\n" }
    RosterApplyRefused { reason: reason } => "CONTROL-FAIL multibyte: refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: reason) + "\n"
  }
}

// An unreadable generation file leaves the history unestablished (no restart of the nonce count); only an absent one is first use.
fn roster_control_generation() -> String {
  let first = roster_generation_history(success: false, content: "", error_kind: "not_found")
  let denied = roster_generation_history(success: false, content: "", error_kind: "permission_denied")
  let other = roster_generation_history(success: false, content: "", error_kind: "other")
  let known = roster_generation_history(success: true, content: "xx", error_kind: "")
  let first_ok = match first {
    RosterHistoryKnown { content: c } => c == ""
    RosterHistoryUnestablished => false
  }
  let denied_bad = match denied {
    RosterHistoryKnown { content: c } => false
    RosterHistoryUnestablished => true
  }
  let other_bad = match other {
    RosterHistoryKnown { content: c } => false
    RosterHistoryUnestablished => true
  }
  let known_ok = match known {
    RosterHistoryKnown { content: c } => c == "xx"
    RosterHistoryUnestablished => false
  }
  if first_ok && denied_bad && other_bad && known_ok { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL generation: an unreadable history was read as empty\n" }
}

fn roster_control_status_names() -> String {
  let entries = " M src/a.dag\u{0}?? src/b.dag\u{0}R  new.dag\u{0}old.dag\u{0}"
  if roster_status_names_path(entries_nul: entries, path: "src/a.dag") && roster_status_names_path(entries_nul: entries, path: "old.dag") && !roster_status_names_path(entries_nul: entries, path: "src/c.dag") && !roster_status_names_path(entries_nul: entries, path: "a.dag") {
    ""
  } else {
    "CONTROL-FAIL status: porcelain fields misread\n"
  }
}

fn roster_control_ancestor() -> String {
  let entries = "?? src\u{0} D docs/x.dag\u{0}?? srcx\u{0}"
  if roster_status_names_ancestor(entries_nul: entries, path: "src/f.dag") && roster_status_names_ancestor(entries_nul: "?? src/\u{0}", path: "src/a/f.dag") && !roster_status_names_ancestor(entries_nul: entries, path: "srcy/f.dag") && !roster_status_names_ancestor(entries_nul: entries, path: "src") {
    ""
  } else {
    "CONTROL-FAIL ancestor: status entry naming a parent directory misread\n"
  }
}

// THE POSITION-TO-HOME-KIND CONTROLS (tidy-ant-251's roster correction, msg_66a5409b), run by roster_controls_report.
// Each parses + normalizes its specimen through the SAME front end the sweep runs and asks the ONE classifier
// (roster_site_is_free, which delegates the position/kind compatibility to v2.workflow.roster_home_kind
// position_matches_home_kind) how many sites of the row's name want that row's import.
//
// THE HOMES ARE DECLARATIONS THE CENSUS ACTUALLY CLASSIFIES -- measured, not assumed. The homes here are:
//   TYPE home  std.algebra.FreeMonoid   -- dag/std/algebra.dag `type FreeMonoid<a>` -> census kind TypeItem
//   VALUE home std.host_text.chars      -- dag/std/host_text.dag `fn chars(text: HostText)` -> census kind FnItem
// An aliased type home (std.types List/Map/Set) reads TypeItem too, since the host item_kind reads the parser's recorded
// kind; roster_control_wave_two_alias_homes_are_types pins that, and "wave-two-list-imports" below runs the real row.
// and each specimen spells the name its row claims.
//   type-home-in-type-position   `fn f(xs: FreeMonoid<Int>) -> FreeMonoid<Int> { xs }` -> the binder annotation and the
//                                two recorded return sites DO want the import (the shape Wave 2 needs).
//   value-home-in-value-position `fn f(x: String) -> Int { chars(s: x) }` -> exactly the body's call head wants it: 1,
//                                not 2, because the signature row's mention of a parameter is a LABEL spelling, which
//                                matches no declaration kind.
//   value-home-in-type-position  `fn f(y: chars) -> Int { 0 }` -> NOTHING wants it; this is the fixture whose row the
//                                pre-correction sweep emitted (`import std.host_text { chars }` for a module that needs
//                                no such import).
//   type-home-in-value-position  `fn f(xs: Slot) -> Int { FreeMonoid(xs) }` -> the value-position call head must NOT
//                                match, so a value use of a type home never imports.
fn roster_kind_controls(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  roster_control_census_knows_the_homes()
    + roster_control_wave_two_alias_homes_are_types()
    + roster_kind_control(name: "type-home-in-type-position", text: roster_kind_specimen_type_annotation(), row: roster_kind_type_row(), expected: 3, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
    + roster_kind_control(name: "value-home-in-value-position", text: roster_kind_specimen_value_call(), row: roster_kind_value_row(), expected: 1, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
    + roster_kind_control(name: "value-home-in-type-position", text: roster_kind_specimen_value_home_in_type(), row: roster_kind_value_row(), expected: 0, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
    + roster_kind_control(name: "type-home-in-value-position", text: roster_kind_specimen_type_home_as_value(), row: roster_kind_type_row(), expected: 0, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
    + roster_kind_control(name: "called-parameter-head-is-not-free", text: roster_kind_specimen_called_parameter(), row: roster_kind_value_row(), expected: 0, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
    + roster_kind_control(name: "data-home-in-value-position", text: roster_kind_specimen_data_call(), row: roster_kind_data_row(), expected: 1, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
    + roster_kind_control(name: "data-home-in-type-position", text: roster_kind_specimen_data_in_type(), row: roster_kind_data_row(), expected: 0, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
    + roster_kind_control(name: "unclassifiable-home-is-not-free", text: roster_kind_specimen_aliased_type(), row: roster_kind_unclassified_row(), expected: 0, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
    + roster_kind_unclassified_control(name: "unclassified-home-refuses", text: roster_kind_specimen_aliased_type(), row: roster_kind_unclassified_row(), prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
    + roster_kind_unclassified_control(name: "out-of-home-declaration-refuses", text: roster_kind_specimen_value_call(), row: roster_kind_out_of_home_row(), prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
    + roster_kind_unclassified_control(name: "underivable-home-refuses", text: roster_kind_specimen_value_call(), row: roster_kind_underivable_home_row(), prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
    + roster_kind_control(name: "wave-two-list-imports", text: roster_kind_specimen_aliased_type(), row: roster_kind_wave_two_list_row(), expected: 3, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
    + roster_kind_control(name: "classified-home-flips-to-row", text: roster_kind_specimen_aliased_type(), row: roster_kind_classified_flipped_row(), expected: 3, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
    + roster_kind_clean_control(name: "classified-home-imports", text: roster_kind_specimen_aliased_type(), row: roster_kind_classified_flipped_row(), prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
}

// THE UNCLASSIFIED-HOME TRIO (review 83187). The specimen is wise-moth-707's Wave 2 fixture: `fn f(xs: List<Int>) ->
// List<Int>` with no import. Its row names a home the census has NO rows for (std.no_such_home), the one remaining
// shape of 'the census cannot classify' now that aliases read TypeItem, so the position rule CANNOT decide it, and
// three things must hold at once:
//  1. unclassifiable-home-is-not-free -- the site is NOT counted free for the row (the pre-fix sweep imported on
//     that silence, and a Bool verdict could not express the difference between "no" and "cannot tell");
//  2. unclassified-home-refuses -- a sweep asked to cover that row REFUSES, located
//     (home-kind-unclassified home=std.no_such_home name=List), instead of finishing Clean or proposing the import;
//  3. classified-home-flips-to-row / classified-home-imports -- with the SAME position and the SAME unbound head, a
//     home whose census classifies the name as a type (std.algebra FreeMonoid, TypeItem) decides Matched: the site
//     counts free and the sweep plans the import. So the refusal fires exactly when the CENSUS cannot decide, never
//     from the position alone.
fn roster_kind_specimen_aliased_type() -> String {
  "module c.kind.aliasgap\n\nfn f(xs: List<Int>) -> List<Int> {\n  xs\n}\n"
}

fn roster_kind_unclassified_row() -> RosterHeadRow {
  RosterHeadRow { call: "List", key: "List", import_name: "List", home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.no_such_home"), labels: [], head: KeepHead }
}

// The real Wave 2 row: List at std.types, an aliased type the census now reads as TypeItem.
fn roster_kind_wave_two_list_row() -> RosterHeadRow {
  RosterHeadRow { call: "List", key: "List", import_name: "List", home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.types"), labels: [], head: KeepHead }
}

// The identical row over a census-classified type home: only `home` differs, which is the whole point.
fn roster_kind_classified_flipped_row() -> RosterHeadRow {
  RosterHeadRow { call: "List", key: "List", import_name: "FreeMonoid", home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.algebra"), labels: [], head: KeepHead }
}

fn roster_kind_unclassified_control(name: String, text: String, row: RosterHeadRow, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  match roster_sweep_text_rows(sides: roster_home_sides(rows: [row]), companions: [], path: "control/" + name + ".dag", text: text, prepared: prepared, lex: lex, candidates: [row], closures: roster_control_closures()) {
    RosterRefused { reason: r } =>
      if roster_refusal_text(reason: r) == "home-kind-unclassified home=" + roster_qn_text(qn: row.home) + " name=" + row.import_name {
        ""
      } else {
        "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": refused for " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + " instead of the located census verdict\n"
      }
    RosterClean => "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": the sweep finished Clean over a home the census cannot classify -- a fabricated success (DESIGN 5)\n"
    RosterEdit { start: _, end: _, text: t, own_line: _ } => "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": the sweep planned an import from a home it cannot classify: " + t + "\n"
    RosterLabelEdits { edits: _ } => "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": label edits planned over an unclassifiable home\n"
    RosterEditWithLabels { start: _, end: _, text: t, own_line: _, labels: _ } => "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": import and label edits planned over an unclassifiable home: " + t + "\n"
  }
}

fn roster_kind_clean_control(name: String, text: String, row: RosterHeadRow, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  match roster_sweep_text_rows(sides: roster_home_sides(rows: [row]), companions: [], path: "control/" + name + ".dag", text: text, prepared: prepared, lex: lex, candidates: [row], closures: roster_control_closures()) {
    RosterEdit { start: _, end: _, text: t, own_line: _ } =>
      if string_contains(s: t, pattern: row.import_name) { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": import plans " + t + " for " + row.import_name + "\n" }
    RosterRefused { reason: r } => "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": refused for " + roster_refusal_text(reason: r) + " over a census-classified type home\n"
    RosterClean => "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": Clean -- a free unbound type-position head of a classified type home planned no import\n"
    RosterLabelEdits { edits: _ } => "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": only label edits for an unimported shape\n"
    RosterEditWithLabels { start: _, end: _, text: t, own_line: _, labels: _ } => "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": " + t + "\n"
  }
}

// THE DATA-CONSTANT PAIR (review 83116): a `data` row is a TYPED CONSTANT, so it is referenced at value positions and
// must get its import there -- and it is not a type, so a type-position mention of it must import nothing. The subject
// is a real `data` declaration the census KEYS (see roster_kind_data_row for the measured choice: std.algebra
// kernel_algebra_profile, dag/std/algebra.dag:956, keyed kinds=[Data,]). Before the correction (DataItem classed as a
// type) the value-position head got NO import and the annotation got one -- a plausible sweep with a missing required
// import.
fn roster_kind_specimen_data_call() -> String {
  "module c.kind.datacall\n\nfn f(n: Int) -> Int {\n  kernel_algebra_profile\n}\n"
}

fn roster_kind_specimen_data_in_type() -> String {
  "module c.kind.datatype\n\nfn f(y: kernel_algebra_profile) -> Int {\n  0\n}\n"
}

// THE DATA ROW IS A CENSUS-KEYED data DECLARATION: measured (roster_census_diag_probe), v2.std.decl_index keys
// std.algebra.kernel_algebra_profile (dag/std/algebra.dag:956) with kinds=[Data,], is_value=Y. It was chosen OVER
// v2.lens.enforcement.standing_intent whole_corpus_scope -- a real data row this sweep's own table reads -- because the
// census keys NO row at all for that qualified name (measured kinds=[]): a census coverage gap, reported to the manager
// as a defect, not absorbed. A control may not assert through an unkeyed census; it would measure the census's silence.
fn roster_kind_data_row() -> RosterHeadRow {
  RosterHeadRow { call: "kernel_algebra_profile", key: "kernel_algebra_profile", import_name: "kernel_algebra_profile", home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.algebra"), labels: [], head: KeepHead }
}

// THE #14338 SPECIMEN ITSELF, as a position control: `fn u(chars: fn(String) -> Int, x: String) -> Int { chars(s: x) }`.
// The call head is INSIDE the scope that binds `chars`, so v2.compiler.lexical_scope answers value/frame and the row
// wants NOTHING -- this is the defect gone at its root, measured rather than asserted. Before the fix the same site
// read value/unbound and the sweep emitted `import std.host_text { chars }` for a module that declares the parameter.
fn roster_kind_specimen_called_parameter() -> String {
  "module c.kind.calledparam\n\nfn u(chars: fn(String) -> Int, x: String) -> Int {\n  chars(s: x)\n}\n"
}

// THE TWO ROWS THE CONTROLS USE, defined once so the premise control and the specimens cannot drift onto different
// declarations. Built at the same boundary the real rows are: the dotted home is read into a QualifiedName.
fn roster_kind_type_row() -> RosterHeadRow {
  RosterHeadRow { call: "FreeMonoid", key: "FreeMonoid", import_name: "FreeMonoid", home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.algebra"), labels: [], head: KeepHead }
}

// THE HOME-DIRECTORY POOL PAIR (Seat 7). The home kind is read from the home module's own storage directory, so a name
// declared only OUTSIDE that directory must refuse, located, rather than vanish into a Clean. The twin of each is
// value-home-in-value-position: the same specimen and spelling, whose real home std.host_text declares chars and so
// counts 1. std.roster_seat7_absent_home derives dag/std/roster_seat7_absent_home.dag, whose directory holds no chars of
// that module (chars is std.host_text's); std.9underivable derives no file at all, so its pool is empty.
fn roster_kind_out_of_home_row() -> RosterHeadRow {
  RosterHeadRow { call: "chars", key: "chars", import_name: "chars", home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.roster_seat7_absent_home"), labels: [], head: KeepHead }
}

fn roster_kind_underivable_home_row() -> RosterHeadRow {
  RosterHeadRow { call: "chars", key: "chars", import_name: "chars", home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.9underivable"), labels: [], head: KeepHead }
}

fn roster_kind_value_row() -> RosterHeadRow {
  RosterHeadRow { call: "chars", key: "chars", import_name: "chars", home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: "std.host_text"), labels: [], head: KeepHead }
}

// THE SPECIMEN'S RECORDED SITES, through the same three front-end steps roster_sweep_text_scoped runs (tokenize, parse,
// normalize), so the position a site carries is the position the sweep would have decided from. No import is supplied:
// the import decision reads sites in the pre-import phase, and that is the phase these controls pin.
fn roster_kind_sites(text: String, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> Optional<FreeMonoid<ScopedReferenceSite>> {
  match tokenize_prepared(text: text, file: symbol_intern_lexeme(lexeme: "control/kind.dag"), prepared: lex) {
    Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => Absent
    Accepted { value: stream, diagnostics: _ } =>
      match parse_module_prepared(tokens: stream, prepared: prepared) {
        Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => Absent
        Accepted { value: artifact, diagnostics: _ } =>
          match normalize_with(parse_tree: artifact.tree, source: NormalizeWithIsolatedAllocator, spans: artifact.span_index) {
            Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => Absent
            Accepted { value: scoped, diagnostics: _ } =>
              Present { value: collect_scoped_module_reference_sites(root: scoped.tree.root, imported: []).sites }
          }
      }
  }
}

fn roster_kind_control(name: String, text: String, row: RosterHeadRow, expected: Int, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  match roster_kind_sites(text: text, prepared: prepared, lex: lex) {
    Absent => "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": the specimen did not normalize\n"
    Present { value: sites } =>
      let wanted = fold_list(xs: sites, empty: 0, cons: fn(n, st) {
        if roster_spelling_is(qn: st.site.spelling, call: row.call) && roster_site_is_free(sides: roster_home_sides(rows: [row]), site: st, row: row, imported_from_home: false) { n + 1 } else { n }
      })
      if wanted == expected { "" } else {
        "CONTROL-FAIL " + name + ": " + int_to_decimal_string(value: wanted) + " sites of " + row.call + " want the " + roster_qn_text(qn: row.home)
          + " import, expected " + int_to_decimal_string(value: expected) + " -- " + roster_home_kind_sites_text(sites: sites) + "\n"
      }
  }
}

// THE SPECIMENS, as authored source. Each goes through tokenize, parse and normalize exactly as roster_sweep_text_scoped
// does, so the position a site carries is the position the sweep would have decided from. No import is supplied: the
// import decision reads sites in the pre-import phase, and that is the phase these controls pin. No module path segment
// is a grammar keyword -- `module c.kind.type` does not parse (measured: "the specimen did not normalize").
fn roster_kind_specimen_type_annotation() -> String {
  "module c.kind.typemention\n\nfn f(xs: FreeMonoid<Int>) -> FreeMonoid<Int> {\n  xs\n}\n"
}

fn roster_kind_specimen_value_call() -> String {
  "module c.kind.valuecall\n\nfn f(x: String) -> Int {\n  chars(s: x)\n}\n"
}

fn roster_kind_specimen_value_home_in_type() -> String {
  "module c.kind.valuehome\n\nfn f(y: chars) -> Int {\n  0\n}\n"
}

fn roster_kind_specimen_type_home_as_value() -> String {
  "module c.kind.typehome\n\nfn f(xs: Slot) -> Int {\n  FreeMonoid(xs)\n}\n"
}

// THE PREMISE OF THE FOUR CONTROLS ABOVE: the census must classify BOTH homes, as OPPOSITE kinds. Without it the four
// could pass because the census reads NOTHING anywhere -- position_matches_home_kind answers false in both directions
// when a home is unknown, which is exactly the decoration reading this control exists to forbid. It earned that role:
// the first revision of the four controls named homes the census does not classify, and this control is what reported
// it. The roots it read under are printed on failure, because a home missing under one root list is a different fact
// from a home missing under all of them.
fn roster_control_census_knows_the_homes() -> String {
  let type_row = roster_kind_type_row()
  let value_row = roster_kind_value_row()
  let data_row = roster_kind_data_row()
  let sides = roster_home_sides_read(asks: [
    RosterHomeAsk { home: roster_qn_text(qn: type_row.home), import_name: type_row.import_name },
    RosterHomeAsk { home: roster_qn_text(qn: value_row.home), import_name: value_row.import_name },
    RosterHomeAsk { home: roster_qn_text(qn: data_row.home), import_name: data_row.import_name }
  ])
  let wrong = (if roster_home_side_is_type(side: roster_home_side_of(sides: sides, home: roster_qn_text(qn: type_row.home), import_name: type_row.import_name)) { "" } else { type_row.import_name + " @ " + roster_qn_text(qn: type_row.home) + " reads no type/data declaration" })
    + (if roster_home_side_is_value(side: roster_home_side_of(sides: sides, home: roster_qn_text(qn: value_row.home), import_name: value_row.import_name)) { "" } else { "; " + value_row.import_name + " @ " + roster_qn_text(qn: value_row.home) + " reads no value declaration" })
    + (if !roster_home_side_is_type(side: roster_home_side_of(sides: sides, home: roster_qn_text(qn: value_row.home), import_name: value_row.import_name)) { "" } else { "; " + value_row.import_name + " @ " + roster_qn_text(qn: value_row.home) + " ALSO reads a TYPE declaration" })
    + (if !roster_home_side_is_value(side: roster_home_side_of(sides: sides, home: roster_qn_text(qn: type_row.home), import_name: type_row.import_name)) { "" } else { "; " + type_row.import_name + " @ " + roster_qn_text(qn: type_row.home) + " ALSO reads a VALUE declaration" })
    + (if roster_home_side_is_value(side: roster_home_side_of(sides: sides, home: roster_qn_text(qn: data_row.home), import_name: data_row.import_name)) { "" } else { "; data home " + roster_qn_text(qn: data_row.home) + "." + data_row.import_name + " reads no value declaration (a typed `data` constant is a value)" })
    + (if !roster_home_side_is_type(side: roster_home_side_of(sides: sides, home: roster_qn_text(qn: data_row.home), import_name: data_row.import_name)) { "" } else { "; data home " + roster_qn_text(qn: data_row.home) + "." + data_row.import_name + " reads a TYPE declaration" })
  if wrong == "" { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL census-homes: " + wrong + " (v2.std.decl_index decl_facts_at over the home directories " + roster_home_pool_roots_text(home: roster_qn_text(qn: type_row.home)) + roster_home_pool_roots_text(home: roster_qn_text(qn: value_row.home)) + roster_home_pool_roots_text(home: roster_qn_text(qn: data_row.home)) + ")\n" }
}

// WAVE 2'S HOMES ARE TYPES TO THE CENSUS. std.types List/Map/Set are ALIASED type declarations
// (`type List<element> = FreeMonoid<element>`), and the host item_kind reads the kind the parser recorded
// (module_item_kind == ModuleItemTypeDeclaration), so an alias reads TypeItem like a record or a coproduct. The control
// requires all three to read as TYPE declarations; it goes red if an alias falls back to the census's cannot-classify
// answer (OtherItem), which would silently stop their rows importing.
fn roster_control_wave_two_alias_homes_are_types() -> String {
  let names = ["List", "Map", "Set"]
  let sides = roster_home_sides_read(asks: list_map(xs: names, f: fn(n) { RosterHomeAsk { home: "std.types", import_name: n } }))
  let not_types = fold_list(xs: names, empty: "", cons: fn(acc, n) {
    if roster_home_side_is_type(side: roster_home_side_of(sides: sides, home: "std.types", import_name: n)) { acc } else { acc + " " + n }
  })
  if not_types == "" {
    ""
  } else {
    "CONTROL-FAIL wave-two-alias-homes: the census does not read these std.types aliases as type declarations:" + not_types + "\n"
  }
}

fn roster_control_annotation(prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> String {
  let before = "module c.annotation\n\nimport std.algebra {\n  // 😀 kept\n  Cons\n}\n\nfn f(xs: List<String>) -> Int {\n  count(xs: xs)\n}\n"
  match roster_applied(before: before, outcome: roster_sweep_text(path: "control/annotation.dag", text: before, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)) {
    RosterApplyRefused { reason: reason } =>
      if roster_refusal_text(reason: reason) == "extent-has-annotation" { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL annotation: refused for " + roster_refusal_text(reason: reason) + "\n" }
    RosterApplyWritten { content: _ } => "CONTROL-FAIL annotation: the splice erased an annotation\n"
  }
}

// THE LOCK CONTROLS (effectful), run as `gunbc run … --function roster_import_sweep_lock_controls_exit --arg root_dir=<absolute scratch dir>`.
// The scratch dir must be one the caller just created EMPTY (no mkdir operation is reachable from a .dag effect, so the controls
// cannot create it themselves): a non-empty dir, or one with a `.git` entry, is refused before anything is touched. The controls
// create and delete only the files they created in it (`.roster_control_*`, the lock and the generation file), never a `.git`,
// and never touch the real worktree: they take the lock with roster_lock_take, which makes no claim about the root.
//   unheld:   a token built without roster_lock_acquire (no lock file) refuses `lock-not-held`; the target keeps its bytes.
//   stale:    a token from an earlier acquisition refuses `lock-not-held` while another acquisition holds the lock.
//   contend:  with the lock held, a second take on the same root is refused.
//   traversal: roster_apply_edit itself (the write boundary) refuses `../outside.dag` under a held lock and creates nothing.
//   spellings: the scratch dir and a subdirectory of the real toplevel are not the git toplevel, so acquire refuses `root-not-git-toplevel`
//             and creates no lock; a relative or non-canonical root is refused.
//   (the pure controls cover an unreadable generation history and the porcelain reader; the git admission of a target
//   (symlink 120000, untracked, modified) is exercised by the real apply run, not by a planted observation.)
fn roster_import_sweep_lock_controls_exit(root_dir: String) -> ProcessExit {
  let listed = Filesystem.List(path: root_dir)
  if !roster_root_admitted(root_dir: root_dir) || !listed.success || listed.entries != "" {
    exit_failure(reason: "CONTROL-FAIL scratch dir must be an absolute, existing, EMPTY directory the caller just created\n")
  } else {
    let report = roster_lock_controls_report(root_dir: root_dir)
    let cleaned = Filesystem.Delete(path: roster_generation_file(root: root_dir))
    let left = Filesystem.List(path: root_dir)
    if report == "" && cleaned.success && left.success && left.entries == "" { ExitSuccess } else { exit_failure(reason: report + "CONTROL-FAIL scratch dir not left empty\n") }
  }
}

fn roster_lock_controls_report(root_dir: String) -> String {
  roster_control_unheld(root_dir: root_dir)
    + roster_control_stale(root_dir: root_dir)
    + roster_control_contend(root_dir: root_dir)
    + roster_control_traversal(root_dir: root_dir)
    + roster_control_spellings(root_dir: root_dir)
}

fn roster_control_unheld(root_dir: String) -> String {
  let before = roster_control_source(module_name: "c.unheld")
  let target = ".roster_control_unheld.dag"
  if !Filesystem.WriteCreateNew(path: root_dir + "/" + target, content: before).success {
    "CONTROL-FAIL unheld: scratch target could not be created\n"
  } else {
    let refused = roster_apply_edit(
      held: RosterHeldLock { root: root_dir, nonce: "forged" },
      path: target,
      before: before,
      outcome: roster_control_valid_edit(module_name: "c.unheld")
    )
    let after = Filesystem.Read(path: root_dir + "/" + target)
    let removed = Filesystem.Delete(path: root_dir + "/" + target)
    if refused != roster_refuse_row(path: target, reason: RefusalLockNotHeld) {
      "CONTROL-FAIL unheld: got " + refused
    } else if !after.success || after.content != before {
      "CONTROL-FAIL unheld: the target changed without the lock\n"
    } else {
      ""
    }
  }
}

fn roster_control_stale(root_dir: String) -> String {
  let before = roster_control_source(module_name: "c.stale")
  let target = ".roster_control_stale.dag"
  match roster_lock_take(root_dir: root_dir) {
    RosterLockRefused { reason: reason } => "CONTROL-FAIL stale: first acquire refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: reason) + "\n"
    RosterLockAcquired { held: first } =>
      if !roster_lock_release(held: first) {
        "CONTROL-FAIL stale: first release failed\n"
      } else {
        match roster_lock_take(root_dir: root_dir) {
          RosterLockRefused { reason: reason } => "CONTROL-FAIL stale: second acquire refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: reason) + "\n"
          RosterLockAcquired { held: second } =>
            if !Filesystem.WriteCreateNew(path: root_dir + "/" + target, content: before).success {
              "CONTROL-FAIL stale: scratch target could not be created\n"
            } else {
              let refused = roster_apply_edit(
                held: first,
                path: target,
                before: before,
                outcome: roster_control_valid_edit(module_name: "c.stale")
              )
              let after = Filesystem.Read(path: root_dir + "/" + target)
              let removed = Filesystem.Delete(path: root_dir + "/" + target)
              let stale_release = roster_lock_release(held: first)
              let released = roster_lock_release(held: second)
              if first.nonce == second.nonce {
                "CONTROL-FAIL stale: two acquisitions shared a nonce\n"
              } else if refused != roster_refuse_row(path: target, reason: RefusalLockNotHeld) {
                "CONTROL-FAIL stale: got " + refused
              } else if !after.success || after.content != before {
                "CONTROL-FAIL stale: a stale token changed the target\n"
              } else if stale_release || !released {
                "CONTROL-FAIL stale: a stale token released the current holder's lock\n"
              } else {
                ""
              }
            }
        }
      }
  }
}

fn roster_control_contend(root_dir: String) -> String {
  match roster_lock_take(root_dir: root_dir) {
    RosterLockRefused { reason: reason } => "CONTROL-FAIL contend: first acquire refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: reason) + "\n"
    RosterLockAcquired { held: held } => {
      let second = match roster_lock_take(root_dir: root_dir) {
        RosterLockRefused { reason: reason } => roster_refusal_text(reason: reason)
        RosterLockAcquired { held: _ } => "acquired"
      }
      let released = roster_lock_release(held: held)
      if second == "apply-lock-unavailable" && released { "" } else { "CONTROL-FAIL contend: second acquire answered " + second + "\n" }
    }
  }
}

fn roster_control_traversal(root_dir: String) -> String {
  match roster_lock_take(root_dir: root_dir) {
    RosterLockRefused { reason: reason } => "CONTROL-FAIL traversal: acquire refused " + roster_refusal_text(reason: reason) + "\n"
    RosterLockAcquired { held: held } => {
      let edit = roster_control_valid_edit(module_name: "c.traversal")
      let source = roster_control_source(module_name: "c.traversal")
      let up = roster_apply_edit(held: held, path: "../roster_control_outside.dag", before: source, outcome: edit)
      let abs = roster_apply_edit(held: held, path: "/tmp/roster_control_outside.dag", before: source, outcome: edit)
      let made = Filesystem.Read(path: root_dir + "/../roster_control_outside.dag")
      let released = roster_lock_release(held: held)
      if up == roster_refuse_row(path: "../roster_control_outside.dag", reason: RefusalPathOutsideRoot) && abs == roster_refuse_row(path: "/tmp/roster_control_outside.dag", reason: RefusalPathOutsideRoot) && !made.success && released {
        ""
      } else {
        "CONTROL-FAIL traversal: got " + up + abs
      }
    }
  }
}

fn roster_control_spellings(root_dir: String) -> String {
  let top = git.Inspect.Toplevel().path as String
  let scratch = match roster_lock_acquire(root_dir: root_dir) {
    RosterLockRefused { reason: reason } => roster_refusal_text(reason: reason)
    RosterLockAcquired { held: _ } => "acquired"
  }
  let sub = match roster_lock_acquire(root_dir: top + "/src") {
    RosterLockRefused { reason: reason } => roster_refusal_text(reason: reason)
    RosterLockAcquired { held: _ } => "acquired"
  }
  let lock_made = Filesystem.Read(path: roster_lock_file(root: root_dir))
  if scratch == "root-not-git-toplevel" && sub == "root-not-git-toplevel" && !lock_made.success && !roster_root_admitted(root_dir: "relative/dir") && !roster_root_admitted(root_dir: "/a/../b") && !roster_root_admitted(root_dir: "/a//b") && roster_root_admitted(root_dir: "/a/b") {
    ""
  } else {
    "CONTROL-FAIL spellings: scratch answered " + scratch + ", subdirectory answered " + sub + "\n"
  }
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// THE COMPANION IMPORT OF A RENAME (tidy-ant-251's ruling on the map_get wave). A RenameHead row moves a call from an
// ambient spelling to a declared callee. When that callee returns a DECLARED type (std.algebra map_lookup returns
// std.optional Optional<V>, where the ambient map_get returned the kernel Optional), a module that matches the result with
// AMBIENT tags of that type (Present / Absent with no std.optional import) binds the payload with no type: measured on the
// seed, a Set<String> payload returned as an Int is ACCEPTED (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode
// an_ambient_tag_over_a_declared_coproduct_binds_its_payload_untyped). So the rename also imports, from the module that
// declares the callee's return type, exactly the variant tags the module uses at ambient pattern-tag positions.
//
// DERIVED, NEVER AUTHORED: the companion is read once per run from the callee's own declaration -- the home module's
// normalized tree, the declaration's declared return type (its arrow's codomain), that type's binding in the home's
// imports (or the home itself), and the declaring module's coproduct variants (v2.std.type_binder type_decl_view). A row
// whose chain does not read carries CompanionUnderivable, and any file it would govern refuses, located by the link.
type RosterCompanion
  = CompanionDerived { call: String, to: String, module: String, tags: List<String>, closure: RosterHomeClosure }
  | CompanionUnderivable { call: String, to: String, detail: String }
  | CompanionNone

type RosterModuleRead
  = ModuleReadOk { root: Node, imports: List<AliasBindingRow> }
  | ModuleReadFailed { detail: String }

fn roster_module_read(name: String, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> RosterModuleRead {
  match module_file(layout: repository_storage_layout(), name: name) {
    ModuleNameUnderivable { name: _, cause: c } => ModuleReadFailed { detail: "module " + name + " has no storage path: " + c }
    ModuleFileDerived { file: f } =>
      let path = repository_path_of_module_file(file: f)
      let read = Filesystem.Read(path: path)
      if !read.success {
        ModuleReadFailed { detail: "module " + name + " unreadable at " + path }
      } else {
        match tokenize_prepared(text: read.content, file: symbol_intern_lexeme(lexeme: path), prepared: lex) {
          Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => ModuleReadFailed { detail: "module " + name + " does not tokenize" }
          Accepted { value: stream, diagnostics: _ } =>
            match parse_module_prepared(tokens: stream, prepared: prepared) {
              Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => ModuleReadFailed { detail: "module " + name + " does not parse" }
              Accepted { value: artifact, diagnostics: _ } =>
                match normalize_with(parse_tree: artifact.tree, source: NormalizeWithIsolatedAllocator, spans: artifact.span_index) {
                  Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => ModuleReadFailed { detail: "module " + name + " does not normalize" }
                  Accepted { value: scoped, diagnostics: _ } => ModuleReadOk { root: scoped.tree.root, imports: scoped.tree.import_bindings }
                }
            }
        }
      }
  }
}

fn roster_edge_authored(e: Edge) -> String {
  match e.label {
    Authored { name: n } => symbol_lexeme(sym: n)
    Positional => ""
    StructuralLabel { label: _ } => ""
  }
}

fn roster_edge_target(e: Edge) -> Node {
  e.target
}

// The declaration a module's normalized tree carries under `name`: the target of the first edge so labelled.
fn roster_declaration_node(root: Node, name: String) -> Optional<Node> {
  fold_list(xs: node_subtree_nodes(root: root), empty: Absent, cons: fn(acc, n) {
    match acc {
      Present { value: _ } => acc
      Absent => roster_child_labelled(n: n, name: name)
    }
  })
}

fn roster_child_labelled(n: Node, name: String) -> Optional<Node> {
  fold_list(xs: n.children, empty: Absent, cons: fn(acc, e) {
    match acc {
      Present { value: _ } => acc
      Absent => if roster_edge_authored(e: e) == name { Present { value: roster_edge_target(e: e) } } else { Absent }
    }
  })
}

// The head spelling of a function declaration's declared return type: its arrow's codomain (positional 1), first atom.
fn roster_return_head(arrow: Node) -> Optional<String> {
  match list_at_optional(xs: positional_child_target_nodes(node: arrow), index: 1) {
    Absent => Absent
    Present { value: ret } =>
      fold_list(xs: node_subtree_nodes(root: ret), empty: Absent, cons: fn(acc, n) {
        match acc {
          Present { value: _ } => acc
          Absent =>
            match node_atom_identity_optional(node: n) {
              Present { value: sym } => Present { value: symbol_lexeme(sym: sym) }
              Absent => Absent
            }
        }
      })
  }
}

// Where `spelling` is declared, as seen from the home: its import binding's target, or the home itself.
fn roster_type_owner(home: String, imports: List<AliasBindingRow>, root: Node, spelling: String) -> Optional<String> {
  match fold_list(xs: imports, empty: Absent, cons: fn(acc, b) { match acc { Present { value: _ } => acc  Absent => roster_binding_target_if(b: b, spelling: spelling) } }) {
    Present { value: q } => Present { value: q }
    Absent =>
      match roster_declaration_node(root: root, name: spelling) {
        Present { value: _ } => Present { value: home + "." + spelling }
        Absent => Absent
      }
  }
}

fn roster_binding_target_if(b: AliasBindingRow, spelling: String) -> Optional<String> {
  if symbol_lexeme(sym: b.binding) == spelling { Present { value: roster_qn_text(qn: b.target) } } else { Absent }
}

fn roster_dotted_init(q: String) -> String {
  roster_join(xs: take_prefix(xs: split(s: q, delimiter: "."), n: length(xs: split(s: q, delimiter: ".")) - 1), sep: ".")
}

fn roster_dotted_last(q: String) -> String {
  match list_at_optional(xs: split(s: q, delimiter: "."), index: length(xs: split(s: q, delimiter: ".")) - 1) {
    Present { value: l } => l
    Absent => q
  }
}

// A coproduct's variant names: the direct labels of its member (v2.std.type_binder type_decl_view). Not a coproduct: [].
fn roster_variant_tags(decl: Node) -> List<String> {
  let member = match type_decl_view(target: decl) {
    GenericTypeDecl { binders: _, member: m } => Present { value: m }
    PlainTypeDecl { member: m } => Present { value: m }
    TypeAlias { binders: _, aliased: _ } => Absent
    OpaqueTypeDecl { binders: _ } => Absent
    NotATypeDecl => Absent
  }
  match member {
    Absent => []
    Present { value: m } => fold_list(xs: m.children, empty: [], cons: fn(acc, e) { if roster_edge_authored(e: e) == "" { acc } else { list_snoc_item(xs: acc, item: roster_edge_authored(e: e)) } })
  }
}

fn roster_companion_of(row: RosterHeadRow, to: String, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> RosterCompanion {
  let home = roster_qn_text(qn: row.home)
  match roster_module_read(name: home, prepared: prepared, lex: lex) {
    ModuleReadFailed { detail: d } => CompanionUnderivable { call: row.call, to: to, detail: d }
    ModuleReadOk { root: hroot, imports: himports } =>
      match roster_declaration_node(root: hroot, name: to) {
        Absent => CompanionUnderivable { call: row.call, to: to, detail: "home " + home + " declares no " + to }
        Present { value: callee } =>
          match roster_return_head(arrow: callee) {
            Absent => CompanionUnderivable { call: row.call, to: to, detail: home + "." + to + " has no readable declared return type" }
            Present { value: ret } =>
              match roster_type_owner(home: home, imports: himports, root: hroot, spelling: ret) {
                Absent => CompanionUnderivable { call: row.call, to: to, detail: "return type " + ret + " is neither imported nor declared by " + home }
                Present { value: owner } => roster_companion_from_owner(row: row, to: to, owner: owner, prepared: prepared, lex: lex)
              }
          }
      }
  }
}

fn roster_companion_from_owner(row: RosterHeadRow, to: String, owner: String, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> RosterCompanion {
  let module = roster_dotted_init(q: owner)
  match roster_module_read(name: module, prepared: prepared, lex: lex) {
    ModuleReadFailed { detail: d } => CompanionUnderivable { call: row.call, to: to, detail: d }
    ModuleReadOk { root: mroot, imports: _ } =>
      match roster_declaration_node(root: mroot, name: roster_dotted_last(q: owner)) {
        Absent => CompanionUnderivable { call: row.call, to: to, detail: module + " declares no " + roster_dotted_last(q: owner) }
        // A return type that is not a coproduct has no tags an ambient pattern could stand in for: nothing to import.
        Present { value: decl } =>
          CompanionDerived { call: row.call, to: to, module: module, tags: roster_variant_tags(decl: decl), closure: roster_home_closure_read(home: module, bindings: roster_repository_bindings(root: "")) }
      }
  }
}

// ONCE PER RUN, one per RenameHead row; a KeepHead row has no companion and costs nothing.
fn roster_rename_companions(rows: List<RosterHeadRow>, prepared: PreparedGrammar, lex: PreparedLexRules) -> List<RosterCompanion> {
  fold_list(xs: rows, empty: [], cons: fn(acc, r) {
    match r.head {
      KeepHead => acc
      RenameHead { to: t, positional: _ } => list_snoc_item(xs: acc, item: roster_companion_of(row: r, to: t, prepared: prepared, lex: lex))
    }
  })
}

// THE COMPANION PASS, run on a file whose rows and labels have converged (Clean). For each companion whose renamed callee
// the file now imports from its home: the companion's tags the file uses at an AMBIENT pattern-tag position (lexically
// unbound) and does not import already. None: Clean. Some: one import edit from the companion's module, cycle-checked
// against that module's closure. Tags the file does not use are never added; other ambient names are another wave's.
fn roster_companion_outcome(companions: List<RosterCompanion>, parse_root: Node, spans: SpanIndex, normalized_root: Node, imported: List<AliasBindingRow>, homes: List<RosterHeadRow>) -> RosterOutcome {
  let sites = collect_scoped_module_reference_sites(root: normalized_root, imported: list_map(xs: imported, f: fn(b) { b.binding })).sites
  fold_list(xs: companions, empty: RosterClean, cons: fn(acc, c) {
    match acc {
      RosterClean => roster_one_companion(c: c, parse_root: parse_root, spans: spans, imported: imported, sites: sites, homes: homes)
      other => other
    }
  })
}

fn roster_callee_imported(imported: List<AliasBindingRow>, homes: List<RosterHeadRow>, call: String, to: String) -> Bool {
  fold_list(xs: homes, empty: false, cons: fn(f, r) { f || ((r.call == call) && fold_list(xs: imported, empty: false, cons: fn(g, b) { g || roster_binding_is(b: b, qn: roster_qn_text(qn: r.home) + "." + to, name: to) })) })
}

fn roster_binding_is(b: AliasBindingRow, qn: String, name: String) -> Bool {
  (symbol_lexeme(sym: b.binding) == name) && (roster_qn_text(qn: b.target) == qn)
}

// WHAT ONE SITE SAYS ABOUT A COMPANION TAG. Three answers, because the walk has three: the tag is spelled free at a pattern
// position (Ambient, the import is needed), it is bound or not a pattern-tag mention of it (NotAmbient), or the walk
// could not decide its head. An undecided head the module's own imports bind is decided by them (an imported tag is
// not ambient); any other undecided head stays Undecided, and the companion refuses on it instead of reading it as free
// or bound.
type RosterTagSite
  = TagSiteAmbient
  | TagSiteNotAmbient
  | TagSiteUndecided

fn roster_tag_site(st: ScopedReferenceSite, tag: String, imported: List<AliasBindingRow>) -> RosterTagSite {
  let at_tag = match st.position {
    PatternTagPosition => true
    LabelPosition => false
    ValuePosition => false
    TypeAnnotationPosition => false
    ReturnPosition => false
  }
  if !(at_tag && roster_spelling_is(qn: st.site.spelling, call: tag)) {
    TagSiteNotAmbient
  } else {
    match st.head {
      HeadLexicallyUnbound => TagSiteAmbient
      HeadBoundAtRootValue => TagSiteNotAmbient
      HeadBoundInFrame => TagSiteNotAmbient
      HeadBindingUndecided =>
        if fold_list(xs: imported, empty: false, cons: fn(g, b) { g || (symbol_lexeme(sym: b.binding) == tag) }) { TagSiteNotAmbient } else { TagSiteUndecided }
    }
  }
}

// One tag over every site of the file: Undecided anywhere wins (the need is unknown), then Ambient anywhere.
fn roster_tag_need(sites: FreeMonoid<ScopedReferenceSite>, tag: String, imported: List<AliasBindingRow>) -> RosterTagSite {
  fold_list(xs: sites, empty: TagSiteNotAmbient, cons: fn(acc, st) {
    match acc {
      TagSiteUndecided => TagSiteUndecided
      _ =>
        match roster_tag_site(st: st, tag: tag, imported: imported) {
          TagSiteUndecided => TagSiteUndecided
          TagSiteAmbient => TagSiteAmbient
          TagSiteNotAmbient => acc
        }
    }
  })
}

type RosterTagsNeeded
  = TagsNeeded { tags: List<String> }
  | TagUndecided { tag: String }

fn roster_one_companion(c: RosterCompanion, parse_root: Node, spans: SpanIndex, imported: List<AliasBindingRow>, sites: FreeMonoid<ScopedReferenceSite>, homes: List<RosterHeadRow>) -> RosterOutcome {
  match c {
    CompanionNone => RosterClean
    CompanionUnderivable { call: call, to: to, detail: d } =>
      if roster_callee_imported(imported: imported, homes: homes, call: call, to: to) { RosterRefused { reason: RefusalCompanionUnderivable { call: call, detail: d } } } else { RosterClean }
    CompanionDerived { call: call, to: to, module: module, tags: tags, closure: closure } =>
      if !roster_callee_imported(imported: imported, homes: homes, call: call, to: to) {
        RosterClean
      } else {
        let needed = fold_list(xs: tags, empty: TagsNeeded { tags: [] }, cons: fn(acc, t) {
          match acc {
            TagUndecided { tag: u } => acc
            TagsNeeded { tags: ts } =>
              match roster_tag_need(sites: sites, tag: t, imported: imported) {
                TagSiteUndecided => TagUndecided { tag: t }
                TagSiteAmbient => TagsNeeded { tags: list_snoc_item(xs: ts, item: t) }
                TagSiteNotAmbient => acc
              }
          }
        })
        match needed {
          TagUndecided { tag: u } => RosterRefused { reason: RefusalCompanionTagUndecided { call: call, tag: u } }
          TagsNeeded { tags: ts } =>
            if is_empty(xs: ts) {
              RosterClean
            } else {
              match roster_module_cycle_refusal(parse_root: parse_root, closures: [closure], home: module) {
                Present { value: reason } => RosterRefused { reason: reason }
                Absent => roster_import_names_edit(parse_root: parse_root, spans: spans, home: qualified_name_from_dotted_string(dotted: module), wanted: ts)
              }
            }
        }
      }
  }
}

// The rename controls alone (RenameHead, its pipe form and the named-argument rule), for a run that does not need the whole
// control report: empty when every control holds.
// THE HAND-RUN READING: the count and names of the controls that ran, then any failure, then the count check.
fn roster_rename_controls_ran(verdicts: List<RosterControlVerdict>) -> String {
  int_to_decimal_string(value: length(xs: verdicts)) + " controls ran: " + roster_join_exact(xs: list_map(xs: verdicts, f: fn(v) { v.name }), sep: ", ") + "\n"
    + roster_control_fails(verdicts: verdicts) + roster_rename_control_count_check(verdicts: verdicts)
}

fn roster_rename_controls_report() -> String {
  match dag_prepared_grammar() {
    Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => "CONTROL-FAIL grammar-unprepared\n"
    Accepted { value: prepared, diagnostics: _ } => roster_rename_controls_ran(verdicts: roster_rename_controls_verdicts_all(prepared: prepared, lex: dag_prepared_lex()))
  }
}
